  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHAPTER 1 - MSX SYSTEM OVERVIEW")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The MSX2 was designed to be fully compatible with the MSX1, but there are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("many enhanced features in the MSX2. Chapter 1 introduces the enhanced ")
  ManualsHelp_L("features of the MSX2, and shows block figures and standard tables. This ")
  ManualsHelp_L("information is conceptual, but will be needed to understand dexcriptions in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("volume 2 and later.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1. FROM MSX1 TO MSX2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To begin with, let us took back to the original purpose or intention of MSX ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and then sum up the transition from MSX1 to MSX2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.1 What is MSX?")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX was announced as a new 8-bit computer standard in the autumn of 1983. In ")
  ManualsHelp_L("early days the word " + Chr(34) + "compatibility" + Chr(34) + " was not understood correctly and there ")
  ManualsHelp_L("were misunderstandings that MSX could execute programs from other computers. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since MSX can execute programs only for MSX, it was said that were was no ")
  ManualsHelp_L("difference from the PC series (NEC) or FM series (Fujitsu) personal ")
  ManualsHelp_L("computers, which could only execute programs using their format.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Several years passed before personal computers became popular. In the early ")
  ManualsHelp_L("days only dedicated enthousiasts bought computers, which were difficult to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("use, and, needless to say, incompatible. They were satisfied to tinker with ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the computer and study it. But now computer use has expanded to include ")
  ManualsHelp_L("several classes of users. In other words, the personal computer is becoming a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("commodity item such as televisions or radio cassette recorders. Therefore, ")
  ManualsHelp_L(Chr(34) + "compatibility" + Chr(34) + " is coming to be a problem. If each TV station needs a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("different television set or if each radio cassette recorder needs a different ")
  ManualsHelp_L("tape, do you suppose they would be popular? Software or programs of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("computer as a home electric product must be compatible.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The design team for MSX considered these problems. Since a computer is most ")
  ManualsHelp_L("powerful when left flexible and easy to expand, a " + Chr(34) + "final" + Chr(34) + " standard format was ")
  ManualsHelp_L("not practical. There are too many matters to define and hardware in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("constantly improving. Therefore MSX started with fixing format of the most ")
  ManualsHelp_L("fundamental harware and software such as DOS and BASIC, and the hardware bus ")
  ManualsHelp_L("which is the basis for expansion. Since the computer is used by itself and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("does not interact with other computers, the problem is small. But formats ")
  ManualsHelp_L("must be fixed if the computer is to be connected to " + Chr(34) + "peripherals" + Chr(34) + " and handle ")
  ManualsHelp_L("or accumulate various data. Fortunately MSX had the approval of many home ")
  ManualsHelp_L("appliance electric companies and an MSX format was established early. This ")
  ManualsHelp_L("allowed the system to be well known so that several manufacturers could make ")
  ManualsHelp_L("compatible peripherals for the MSX standard.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Some of the useful features included in the MSX system include the use of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("double precision BCD for normal BASIC arithmetic and the same file format as ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MS-DOS. The real capabilities of the MSX machine will come to light as it is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("used across several fields.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.2 Environment of the MSX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Over one million MSX machines had been sold by December 1985 and are used ")
  ManualsHelp_L("mainly as game machines or primers by primary and junior high school ")
  ManualsHelp_L("students. But MSX use has gradually spread to include such uses as ")
  ManualsHelp_L("communication terminals, Japanese word processing, factory automation, and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("audio visual control. For improving its capabilities, a disk system and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX-DOS have been prepared, and languages such as C, FORTH, and LOGO are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("available. BIOS, which is the collection of input/output routines in BASIC ")
  ManualsHelp_L("ROM, and BDOS, which resides in the disk interface ROM and has compatibility ")
  ManualsHelp_L("with CP/M system calls have both been improved. So an excellent programming ")
  ManualsHelp_L("environment is now available. Chinese Character input, light pen and mouse ")
  ManualsHelp_L("input, and the RS-232C interface have been standardised, and stantardisation ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of other peripherals is proceeding. The keyboard and character set are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("consistent with international standards, and there are minor variations to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("satisfy the needs of individual countries.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Several new peripherals have been developed. Standard devices include ")
  ManualsHelp_L("printers, disk drives, and mice; audio/visual devices include laser drives, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("VTRs, synthesizer controllers, and video acquisition systems. Factory ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Automation devices include robot controllers, room temperature controllers, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("various adaptors for modem and telephone lines, and a health controller ")
  ManualsHelp_L("combined with a hemadynamometer has been developed. So you can see that the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("potential uses for MSX computers has really grown.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Many applications other than games are now supplied on disks and are becoming ")
  ManualsHelp_L("more practical. There are now Japanese word processors capable of clause ")
  ManualsHelp_L("transformation, data bases which can exchange data with higher-level systems, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and CAI and CAD systems.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.3 Extended Contents of MSX2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX2 was announced in May 1985 as a system having upgraded compatibility with ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX. Programs created under the MSX environment can be executed on MSX2 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("without any modifications, even at the assembly language level. Data and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("programs stored on cassette tapes or disks can be used without modification. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Features added by the MSX2 system are improved screen display, higher ")
  ManualsHelp_L("resolution, more colours available, and higher graphics speed. A ")
  ManualsHelp_L("battery-powered clock and RAMDISK feature have also been added. In this ")
  ManualsHelp_L("manual the name MSX2 refers to the computer made along the MSX2 standard and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the name MSX1 refers to the computer made along the previous MSX standard.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("System configuration is shown in Figures 1.1 and 1.2 and Table 1.1 and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("indicate the differences between MSX1 and MSX2. The differences are described ")
  ManualsHelp_L("as follows:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 1.1 MSX2/MSX1 standard comparison")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			     MSX2	       |	   MSX1")
  ManualsHelp_L("		-------------------------------+---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("CPU		|    Z80A or equivalent (clock 3.579545 MHz +- 1%)	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|------------------------------+--------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		| 48K (MSX-BASIC version 2.0)  |  32K (MSX-BASIC ver 1.0) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  ROM	|      MAIN-ROM 32K	       |       MAIN-ROM 32K	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|      SUB-ROM	16K	       |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("MEMORY	  RAM	| 64K or more		       |  8K or more		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  VRAM	| 64K or 128K		       |  16K			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|------------------------------+--------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("LSI for VDP	| V-9938 (MSX-VIDEO)	       |  TMS9918 or equivalent   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("CMT		|		  FSK  1200/2400 baud			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("PSG		|    8 octaves tri-chord output (AY-3-8910 compatible)	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Keyboard	| Alphanumeric		       |  Alphanumeric		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		| Graphic symbols	       |  Graphic symbols	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Floppy disk (*) |		 Based on MS-DOS format 		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Printer 	| 8-bit parallel	       |  (*)			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("ROM cartridge	|			 I/O bus			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|     with slot for game cartridge and expansion bus	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Joystick	|	       2	       |  1 or 2 (*)		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|------------------------------+--------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLOCK-IC	| Standard		       |  (*)			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|------------------------------+--------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("RAM disk	| Standard		       |  Different for 	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("feature 	|			       |  each maker		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		-----------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(*) Optional")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
