  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* MSX-BASIC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC has also been extended from version 1.0 to version 2.0 in order to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("support a new VDP, backup RAM, CLOCK-IC, and so on. Compatibility with MSX1 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is maintained. When using the newly extended screen mode, be careful when ")
  ManualsHelp_L("specifiyng range, since ranges are slightly different in MSX2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX2 has three types of memory, ROM, RAM, VRAM, which are described below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Standard ROM size is 48K bytes. The MSX ROM uses only 32K bytes. The extra ")
  ManualsHelp_L("16K bytes portion of the MSX2 contains routines supporting the extended ")
  ManualsHelp_L("features.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The " + Chr(34) + "MAIN-ROM" + Chr(34) + " consists of 32K bytes and contains the BASIC interpreter, and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the " + Chr(34) + "extended ROM" + Chr(34) + " or " + Chr(34) + "SUB-ROM" + Chr(34) + " consists of 16K bytes and contains routines ")
  ManualsHelp_L("for the extended features.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Standard RAM size is 64K bytes, which is large enough so that MSX-DOS can be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("executed. The RAM size of MSX1 varied from 8K to 64K bytes, so in some cases ")
  ManualsHelp_L("large programs could not be executed without expanding RAM. MSX2 does not ")
  ManualsHelp_L("have this problem.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("A minimum of 64K bytes are required for VRAM in order to execute the added ")
  ManualsHelp_L("features of the screen display. VRAM is thus four times larger than in MSX1, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("which had only 16 K bytes VRAM. But many machines actually use a VRAM size of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("128K bytes, which is eight times larger. Machines with 128K bytes VRAM can ")
  ManualsHelp_L("display 256 colours at the same time.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX machines which have 64K bytes VRAM but cannot be expanded to 128K bytes ")
  ManualsHelp_L("are marked " + Chr(34) + "VRAM64K" + Chr(34) + " on their catalogue or packaging.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The MSX series computers use a video display processor (VDP) type LSI chip ")
  ManualsHelp_L("for controlling the screen output. The VDP used for MSX1 was the TMS9918, but ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the MSX2 uses the V9938 (MSX-VIDEO), which has upper and full compatibility ")
  ManualsHelp_L("with the TMS9918 and can execute software for TMS9918 without any ")
  ManualsHelp_L("modification.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Table 1.2 shows the VDP standard and Table 1.3 shows each screen mode. V9938 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is an excellent LSI chip with digitising, superimposing, and hardware ")
  ManualsHelp_L("scrolling features. Chapter 4 of this manual describes it in detail.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 1.2  VDP specifications")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    V9938	    |	    TMS9918")
  ManualsHelp_L("			----------------------------+----------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("Screen mode		|  10 (see table 1.3)	    |	       4	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|---------------------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Number of dots		|  512 x 212 maximum	    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("(horizontal x		|  424 dots for vertical    |  256 x 192 maximum  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("vertical)		|  can be achieved by	    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|  interlace feature	    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|---------------------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  Number of	|			    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  colours to	|  512 maximum		    |	16 maximum	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  specify	|			    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("Colour			|---------------------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  Number of	|			    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  colours to	|  256 maximum		    |	16 maximum	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  display at	|			    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  the same time |			    |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|-------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Character set		|	    alphanumeric + graphic symbols	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|	      256 characters  8 x 8 dots	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|-------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Sprite colour		|  16 maximum per sprite    |	1 per sprite	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|---------------------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Palette feature 	|  Yes			    |	No		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 1.3  V9938 screen mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Mode		Number of	Dots	   Colours	Palette   Sprite")
  ManualsHelp_L("		characters")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Text 1      |  40 x 24   |	       |   2 from 512 |   Yes	|   No")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Text 2      |  80 x 24   |	       |   4 from 512 |   Yes	|   No")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Multi-colour| 	   |  64 x  48 |  16 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Graphic 1   |  32 x 24   |	       |  16 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Graphic 2   | 	   | 256 x 192 |  16 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Graphic 3   | 	   | 256 x 192 |  16 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Graphic 4   | 	   | 256 x 212 |  16 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Graphic 5   | 	   | 512 x 212 |   4 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Graphic 6   | 	   | 512 x 212 |  16 from 512 |   Yes	|  Mode 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Graphic 7   | 	   | 256 x 212 | 256 from 256 |   No	|  Mode 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(*) Feature modes available from TMS9918 (however, palette feature only from ")
  ManualsHelp_L("V9938).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Battery-powered Clock-IC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Battery-powered RAM is connected to the I/O port and is used for storage of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("setup information and for keeping track of the date and time. Setup ")
  ManualsHelp_L("information specifies the screen colour and mode at reset. This allows the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("user to set up the desired environment when the system is booted.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The CLOCK-IC works independently of the main power supply. After being set ")
  ManualsHelp_L("once new time settings are no longer required.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RAM Disk Feature")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When using BASIC on MSX1 machines which had 64K bytes RAM, only 32K bytes of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("RAM were used; the other 32K bytes were unused since the BASIC interpreter ")
  ManualsHelp_L("occupied the address space. On MSX2 machines this unused RAM can be used as a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("RAMDISK. For users who do not have a disk drive, this feature is very useful ")
  ManualsHelp_L("when loading or saving BASIC programs temporarily.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2. MSX2 SYSTEM OVERVIEW")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This section gives a simple overview of the MSX2 software and hardware ")
  ManualsHelp_L("systems. To help you understand the concepts, diagrams which would be useful ")
  ManualsHelp_L("when developping softwarem, such as VRAM map, the I/O map, and the interface ")
  ManualsHelp_L("standard, are found in the APPENDIX of this manual.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.1 Hardware overview")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("First of all, look at the block diagram in Figure 1.3 to understand the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("hardware configuration of the MSX2 as a whole.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
