  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Text file typed by:	Nestor Soriano (Konami Man) - SPAIN")
  ManualsHelp_L("			March 1997")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.72, last " + Chr(34) + "10000H" + Chr(34) + " is corrected to " + Chr(34) + "1FFFFH" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Table 4.6, in TEOR line, " + Chr(34) + "else DC+..." + Chr(34) + " is corrected to " + Chr(34) + "else DC=..." + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.76, in R#45 figure, DIX and DIY bits have been placed ")
  ManualsHelp_L("correctly (they were inverted in the original).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.79, in R#42 and R#43 explanation, " + Chr(34) + "NY -> of dots..." + Chr(34) + " has been ")
  ManualsHelp_L("changed to " + Chr(34) + "NY -> number of dots..." + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In List 4.9, in the line with the comment " + Chr(34) + "YMMM command" + Chr(34) + ", 11010000 bitfield ")
  ManualsHelp_L("has been corrected to 11100000.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.84, " + Chr(34) + "*" + Chr(34) + " mark removed from the explanation of NX.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.85, in R#45 explanation,	" + Chr(34) + "select source memory" + Chr(34) + " text has been ")
  ManualsHelp_L("corrected to " + Chr(34) + "select destination memory" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In List 4.13, labels beginning with " + Chr(34) + "LMMC" + Chr(34) + " have been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "LMCM" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In List 4.15, in the line with the comment " + Chr(34) + "NY" + Chr(34) + ", the " + Chr(34) + "OUT (C),H" + Chr(34) + " ")
  ManualsHelp_L("instruction has been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "OUT (C),L" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In section 6.5.9, the explanation of usage of the LINE command were mixed ")
  ManualsHelp_L("wih other text. It has been corrected.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.94, a line explaining the meaning of R#44 has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.97, BX9 bit has been supressed in S#9 figure.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 4.99, a line explaining the meaning of R#44 has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Table 4.7, " + Chr(34) + "CLR L" + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "CMR L" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHAPTER 4 - VDP AND DISPLAY SCREEN (Part 6)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6. VDP COMMAND USAGE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX-VIDEO can execute basic graphic operations, which are called VDP ")
  ManualsHelp_L("commands. These are done by accessing special harware and are available in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the GRAPHIC 4 to GRAPHIC 7 modes. These graphic commands have been made easy ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to implement, requiring only that the necessary parameters be set in the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("proper registers before invoking them. This section describes these VDP ")
  ManualsHelp_L("commands.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.1 Coordinate System of VDP Commands")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When VDP commands are executed, the location of the source and destination ")
  ManualsHelp_L("points are represented as (X, Y) coordinates as shown in Figure 4.72. When ")
  ManualsHelp_L("commands are executed, there is no page division and the entire 128K bytes ")
  ManualsHelp_L("VRAM is placed in a large coordinate system.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.72	Coordinate system of VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    GRAPHIC 4  (SCREEN 5)			GRAPHIC 5  (SCREEN 6)")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------	  00000H    ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,0) 	     (255,0) |	    |	    | (0,0)		 (511,0) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    Page 0	     |	    |	    |		Page 0		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,255)	   (255,255) |	    |	    | (0,255)	       (511,255) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------------------------|	  08000H    |----------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,256)	   (255,256) |	    |	    | (0,256)	       (511,256) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    Page 1	     |	    |	    |		Page 1		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,511)	   (255,511) |	    |	    | (0,511)	       (511,511) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------------------------|	  10000H    |----------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,512)	   (255,512) |	    |	    | (0,512)	       (511,512) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    Page 2	     |	    |	    |		Page 2		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,767)	   (255,767) |	    |	    | (0,767)	       (511,767) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------------------------|	  18000H    |----------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,768)	   (255,768) |	    |	    | (0,768)	       (511,768) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    Page 3	     |	    |	    |		Page 3		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,1023)	  (255,1023) |	    |	    | (0,1023)	      (511,1023) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------	  1FFFFH    ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    GRAPHIC 7  (SCREEN 8)			GRAPHIC 6  (SCREEN 7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------	  00000H    ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,0) 	     (255,0) |	    |	    | (0,0)		 (511,0) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    Page 0	     |	    |	    |		Page 0		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,255)	   (255,255) |	    |	    | (0,255)	       (511,255) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------------------------|	  10000H    |----------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,256)	   (255,256) |	    |	    | (0,256)	       (511,256) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    Page 1	     |	    |	    |		Page 1		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (0,511)	   (255,511) |	    |	    | (0,511)	       (511,511) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------	  1FFFFH    ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.2 VDP Commands")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("There are 12 types of VDP commands which can be executed by MSX-VIDEO. These ")
  ManualsHelp_L("are shown in Table 4.5.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 4.5  List of VDP commands")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Command name | Destination | Source | Units | Mnemonic | R#46 (4 hi ord) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    VRAM     |	CPU   | bytes |   HMMC	 |  1	1   1	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| High speed   |    VRAM     |	VRAM  | bytes |   YMMM	 |  1	1   1	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| move	       |    VRAM     |	VRAM  | bytes |   HMMM	 |  1	1   0	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    VRAM     |	VDP   | bytes |   HMMV	 |  1	1   0	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    VRAM     |	CPU   | dots  |   LMMC	 |  1	0   1	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Logical      |    CPU      |	VRAM  | dots  |   LMCM	 |  1	0   1	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| move	       |    VRAM     |	VRAM  | dots  |   LMMM	 |  1	0   0	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    VRAM     |	VDP   | dots  |   LMMV	 |  1	0   0	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Line	       |    VRAM     |	VDP   | dots  |   LINE	 |  0	1   1	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Search       |    VRAM     |	VDP   | dots  |   SRCH	 |  0	1   1	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Pset	       |    VRAM     |	VDP   | dots  |   PSET	 |  0	1   0	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Point        |    VDP      |	VRAM  | dots  |   POINT  |  0	1   0	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    ----     |	----  | ----- |   ----	 |  0	0   1	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Reserved     |    ----     |	----  | ----- |   ----	 |  0	0   1	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    ----     |	----  | ----- |   ----	 |  0	0   0	1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-------------+--------+-------+----------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Stop	       |    ----     |	----  | ----- |   ----	 |  0	0   0	0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* When data is written in R#46 (Command register), MSX-VIDEO begins to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("execute the command after setting 1 to bit 0 (CE/Command Execute) of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("status register S#2. Necessary parameters should be set in register R#32 to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45 before the command is executed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* When the execution of the command ends, CE becomes 0.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* To stop the execution of the command, execute STOP command.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Actions of the commands are guaranteed only in the bitmap modes (GRAPHIC 4 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to GRAPHIC 7).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.3 Logical Operations")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When commands are executed, various logical operations can be done between ")
  ManualsHelp_L("data in VRAM and the specified data. Each operation will be done according to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the rules listed in Table 4.6.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In the table, SC represents the source color and DC represents the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("destination colour. IMP, AND, OR, EOR and NOT write the result of each ")
  ManualsHelp_L("operation to the destination. In operations whose names are preceded by " + Chr(34) + "T" + Chr(34) + ", ")
  ManualsHelp_L("dots which correspond with SC=0 are not the objects of the operations and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("remains as DC. Using these operations enables only colour portions of two ")
  ManualsHelp_L("figures to be overlapped, so they are especially effective for animations.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.7 shows an example of these operations.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 4.6  List of logical operations")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Logical name |					|L03 L02 L01 L00|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+----------------------------------------+---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     IMP      | DC=SC					| 0   0   0   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     AND      | DC=SCxDC				| 0   0   0   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     OR       | DC=SC+DC				| 0   0   1   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    __	     __ 			|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     EOR      | DC=SCxDC+SCxDC 			| 0   0   1   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |    __					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     NOT      | DC=SC					| 0   1   0   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     ----     |					| 0   1   0   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     ----     |					| 0   1   1   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     ----     |					| 0   1   1   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+----------------------------------------+---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     TIMP     | if SC=0 then DC=DC else DC=SC		| 1   0   0   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     TAND     | if SC=0 then DC=DC else DC=SCxDC	| 1   0   0   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     TOR      | if SC=0 then DC=DC else DC=SC+DC	| 1   0   1   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |			    __	     __ |		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     TEOR     | if SC=0 then DC=DC else DC=SCxDC+SCxDC | 1   0   1   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |			    __		|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     TNOT     | if SC=0 then DC=DC else DC=SC		| 1   1   0   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     ----     |					| 1   1   0   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     ----     |					| 1   1   1   0 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     ----     |					| 1   1   1   1 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |					|		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* SC  = Source colour code")
  ManualsHelp_L("* DC  = Destination colour code")
  ManualsHelp_L("* EOR = Exclusive OR")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.7  Example of the logical operation with T")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1000 '***********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("1010 '  List 4.7   logical operation with T")
  ManualsHelp_L("1020 '***********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("1030 '")
  ManualsHelp_L("1040 SCREEN8 : COLOR 15,0,0 : CLS")
  ManualsHelp_L("1050 DIM A%(3587)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1060 '")
  ManualsHelp_L("1070 LINE (50,50)-(60,100),48,8 : PAINT (51,51),156,48")
  ManualsHelp_L("1080 CIRCLE (55,30),30,255 : PAINT (55,30),240,255")
  ManualsHelp_L("1090 COPY(20,0)-(90,100) TO A%")
  ManualsHelp_L("1100 CLS")
  ManualsHelp_L("1110 '")
  ManualsHelp_L("1120 R=RND(-TIME)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1130 FOR Y=0 TO 100 STEP 3")
  ManualsHelp_L("1140   X=INT(RND(1)*186)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1150   COPY A% TO (X,Y),,TPSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("1160 NEXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("1170 '")
  ManualsHelp_L("1180 GOTO 1180")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.4 Area Specification")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("AREA-MOVE commands are for transferring screen data inside areas surrounded ")
  ManualsHelp_L("by a rectangle. The area to be transferred is specified by one vertex and the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("length of each side of the rectangle as shown in Figure 4.73. SX and SY ")
  ManualsHelp_L("represent the basic point of the rectangle to be transferred and NX and NY ")
  ManualsHelp_L("represent the lengt of each side in dots. The two bits, DIX and DIY, are for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the direction of transferring data (the meaning of DIX and DIY depends on the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("type of command). The point where the area is to be transferred is specified ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in DX and DY.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.73	Area specification")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|							       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     (SX,SY)						       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	x----------------- -->				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 | DIX				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	------------------  --+ 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY		      | 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V		      | 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      |      (DX,DY)		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      +->  x-----------------	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   ------------------	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|							       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5 Use of Each Command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Commands are clasified into three types, high-speed transfer commands, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("logical transfer commands, and drawing commands. This section describes the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("commands and their use.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.1 HMMC (CPU -> VRAM high-speed transfer)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Data is transferred into the specified area of VRAM from the CPU (see Figure ")
  ManualsHelp_L("4.74). Logical operations cannot be specified. Data is transferred in bytes ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in high-speed transfer commands such as HMMC. Note that the low order bit of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the X-coordinate is not referred to in GRAPHIC 4, or 6 modes. The two low ")
  ManualsHelp_L("order bits are not referred to in GRAPHIC 5 mode (see Figure 4.75).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Set the parameters as shown in Figure 4.76 to the appropriate registers. At ")
  ManualsHelp_L("this point, write only the first byte of data to be transferred from the CPU ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in R#44. Writing the command code F0H in R#46 causes the command to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("executed, and UMSX-VIDEO receives data from R#44 and writes it to VRAM, then ")
  ManualsHelp_L("waits for data from the CPU.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The CPU writes data after the second byte in R#44. Note that data should be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("transferred after MSX-VIDEO can receive data (in the case that TR bit is ")
  ManualsHelp_L(Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + "), referring to TR bit of S#2. When the CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ", this means ")
  ManualsHelp_L("that all data has been transferred (see figure 4.77). List 4.8 shows an ")
  ManualsHelp_L("example of using HMMC.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.74	Action of HMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |   MSX-VIDEO      CPU")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------	   -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    (DX,DY)					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	x------------------------ --> DIX	  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	   NX		|		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY			|<----------------+----|     |-----|	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|			|		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	-------------------------		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------	   -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select the destination memory	0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be transferred in X direction (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be transferred in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  destination origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  destination origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  1st byte of data to be transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* The one low-order bit for GRAPHIC 4 and 6 modes, or two low-order bits for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 5 mode of the DX and NX registers are ignored.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.75	Dots not to be referred to")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("       MSB   7	  6    5    4	 3    2    1	0    LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 4  |	:    :	  :    |    :	 :    :    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    (1) 		(2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since 1 VRAM byte represents 2 dots, 1 low order bit of X-coordinate is not ")
  ManualsHelp_L("referred to.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("       MSB   7	  6    5    4	 3    2    1	0    LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 5  |	:    |	  :    |    :	 |    :    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       (1)	 (2)	   (3)	     (4)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since 1 VRAM byte represents 4 dots, 2 low order bits of X-coordinate are not ")
  ManualsHelp_L("referred to.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("       MSB   7	  6    5    4	 3    2    1	0    LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 6  |	:    :	  :    |    :	 :    :    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    (1) 		(2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since 1 VRAM byte represents 2 dots, 1 low order bit of X-coordinate is not ")
  ManualsHelp_L("referred to.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.76	Register settings of HMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> HMMC register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| destination origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- NX ---> X direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- NY ---> Y direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+d")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)	|a")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|t")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		    |			|			|a")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+-------------------+-------------------+			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		X=2N		   X=2N+1	  (N=0, 1, ..., 127)	|t")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|o")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)	|b")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|e")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|	  |	    |	      | 	|			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+---------+---------+---------+---------+			|t")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   X=4N     X=4N+1    X=4N+2	X=4N+3	  (N=0, 1, ..., 127)	|r")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|a")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|n")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)	|s")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+f.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      1 byte per dot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| -- | DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |   direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       +-> direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> select destination memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> HMMC command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 1  | 1  | 1  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.77	HMMC command execution flow chart")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/-------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|     HMMC start    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\-------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|   register setup  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| command execution |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------------->|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | Read status register #2 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\ Yes (CE bit = 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|   command end?    |-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  | No (CE bit = 1)		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|<------|     transfer?     |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| No	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (TR bit=0)	  | Yes (TR bit = 1)		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	---------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|   transfer data   |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	---------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+-----------------+				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  +-----------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  V")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/--------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|      HMMC end      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\--------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.8  Example of HMMC command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.8   HMMC sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		to use, set H, L, D, E, IX and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		RAM (IX) ---> VRAM (H,L)-(D,E)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMC:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,36")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,17+80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 36")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,HMMC1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMC1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,HMMC2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMC2:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;first DATA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,0F0H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;HMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,44+80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,17+80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LOOP:	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	0,A			;check CE bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,EXIT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	7,A			;check TR bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXIT:	LD	A,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS		;when exit, you must select S#0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:				;read status register specified by A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:				;wait VDP ready")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.2 YMMM (high-speed transfer between VRAM in Y direction)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Data from a specified VRAM area is transferred into another area in VRAM. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note that transfers using this command can only be done in the Y direction ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(see Figure 4.78).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the data as shown in Figure 4.79 in the proper registers, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("writing command code E0H in R#46 causes the command to be executed. When the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", it indicates that the command is currently being ")
  ManualsHelp_L("executed. List 4.9 shows an example of using YMMM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.78	Actions of YMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		 (DX,DY)			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 x------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 -------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				     ^		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				     |		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				     |		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		 (DX,SY)			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 x------------------------| --> DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 | NY			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 |			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 -------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 | DIY			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			 V			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select the destination memory	0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SY:  source origin Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be transferred in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: set which to be transferred, to te right end or to the left end of the")
  ManualsHelp_L("     screen from the source origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  destination origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  destination origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* The one low-order bit for GRAPHIC 4 and 6 modes, or two low-order bits for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 5 mode of the DX register are ignored.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.79	Register settings of YMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> YMMM register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#34	| SY7| SY6| SY5| SY4| SY3| SY2| SY1| SY0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- SY --> source origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#35	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SY9| SY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- DX --> destination and")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	 source origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- DY --> destination origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  number of dots to")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- NY ---> be transferred in")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| -- | DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |   direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       +-> direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> select destination memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> YMMM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 1  | 1  | 0  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.9  Example of YMMM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.9   YMMM sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		to use, set L, E, B, C, D(bit 2) and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		VRAM (B,L)-(*,E) ---> VRAM (B,C)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		DIX must be set in D(bit 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("YMMM:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC			;save destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,34")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,17+80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 34")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;SY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L			;make NY and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,YMMM1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("YMMM1:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , D := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE			;restore DX,DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			;save DIX,DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),D			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,11100000B		;YMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.3  HMMM (high-speed transfer between VRAM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Data of specified VRAM area is transferred into another area in VRAM (see ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure 4.80).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.81, writing D0H in R#46 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("causes the command to be executed. While the command is being executed, CE ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ". List 4.10 shows an example of using HMMM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.80	Actions of HMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|							       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     (SX,SY)						       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	------------------ -->				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	NX	 | DIX				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	------------------  --+ 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY		      | 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V		      | 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      |      (DX,DY)		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      +->  ------------------	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   ------------------	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|							       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXS: select the source memory		0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select the destination memory	0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SX:  source origin X-coordinate (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("SY:  source origin Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be transferred in X direction (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be transferred in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  destination origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  destination origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* The one low-order bit for GRAPHIC 4 and 6 modes, or two low-order bits for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 5 mode of the SX, DX, and NX register are ignored.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.81	Register settings of HMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> HMMM register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#32	| SX7| SX6| SX5| SX4| SX3| SX2| SX1| SX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#33	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| source origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#34	| SY7| SY6| SY5| SY4| SY3| SY2| SY1| SY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#35	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SY9| SY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| destination origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NX ---> X direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NY ---> Y direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| MXS| DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |    |   direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |    +-> direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  +------> select source memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> select destination memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> HMMM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 1  | 0  | 1  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.10  Example of HMMM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.10   HMMM sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, D, E, B, C and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 VRAM (H,L)-(D,E) ---> VRAM (B,C)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 DIX must be set in D(bit 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMM:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC			;save destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,32")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 32")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;SX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;SY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,HMMM1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMM1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L			;make NY and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,HMMM2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMM2:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE			;restore DX,DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			;save DIX,DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),D			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,11010000B		;HMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.4 HMMV (painting the rectangle in high speed)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Each byte of data in the specified VRAM area is painted by the specified ")
  ManualsHelp_L("colour code (see Figure 4.82)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.83, writing C0H in R#46 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("causes the command to be executed. While the command is being executed, the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("CE bit of S#2 is 1. List 4.11 shows an example of using HMMV.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.82	Actions of HMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |   MSX-VIDEO")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    (DX,DY)					  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	x------------------------ --> DIX	  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	   NX		|		  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY			|<----------------+----|     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|			|		  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	-------------------------		  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY					  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V					  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select memory			0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be painted in X direction (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be painted in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)*")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  Painted data")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* The one low-order bit for GRAPHIC 4 and 6 modes, or two low-order bits for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRAPHIC 5 mode of the DX and NX registers are ignored.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.83	Register settings of HMMV command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> HMMV register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NX ---> X direction to")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  be painted")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NY ---> Y direction to")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  be painted")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+d")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)	|a")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|t")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		    |			|			|a")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+-------------------+-------------------+			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		X=2N		   X=2N+1	  (N=0, 1, ..., 127)	|t")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|o")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)	|b")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|e")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|	  |	    |	      | 	|			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+---------+---------+---------+---------+			|p")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   X=4N     X=4N+1    X=4N+2	X=4N+3	  (N=0, 1, ..., 127)	|a")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|i")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|n")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)	|t")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+e")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      1 byte / dot					 d")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| -- | DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |   painting direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       +-> painting direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> memory selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> HMMV command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 1  | 0  | 0  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.11  Example of HMMV command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.11   HMMV sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, D, E, B and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 B ---> VRAM (H,L)-(D,E) fill")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMV:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,36")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 36")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,HMMV1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMV1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L			;make NY and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,HMMV2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("HMMV2:	OUT	(C),H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,A			;H := NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),B			;fill data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,11000000B		;HMMV command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.5 LMMC (CPU -> VRAM logical transfer)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Data is transferred from the CPU to thespecified VRAM area in dots (see ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure 4.84). Logical operations with the source can be specified. In the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("logical transfer commands, such as LMMC, data is transfered in dots and one ")
  ManualsHelp_L("byte is required for the information of one pixel in all screen modes.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the data as shown in Figure 4.85, write command code B0H in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46. At this point, logical operations can be specified by using the 4 low ")
  ManualsHelp_L("order bits of the command register. Data is transferred with reference to the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("TR and CE bit of S#2, as in HMMC (see Figure 4.86). List 4.12 shows an ")
  ManualsHelp_L("example of using LMMC.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.84	Action of LMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |   MSX-VIDEO      CPU")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------	   -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    (DX,DY)					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	x------------------------ --> DIX	  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	   NX		|		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY			|<----------------+----|     |-----|	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|			|		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	-------------------------		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------	   -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select destination memory		0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be transferred in X direction (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be transferred in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  destination origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  destination origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  1st byte of data to be transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.85	Register settings of LMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMMC register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| destination origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NX ---> X direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NY ---> Y direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		   --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| -- | -- | -- | -- | CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("								     | data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		     | to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| -- | -- | -- | -- | -- | -- | CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)    | trans-")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		     | ferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("								     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		   --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| -- | DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |   direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       +-> direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> select destination memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMMC command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 0  | 1  | 1  | L03| L02| L01| L00| CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    +-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      Logical operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.86	LMMC command execution flow chart")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/-------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|     LMMC start    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\-------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|   register setup  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| command execution |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------------->|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | read status register #2 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\ Yes (CE bit = 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|   command end?    |-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  | No (CE bit = 1)		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|<------|     transfer?     |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| No	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (TR bit=0)	  | Yes (TR bit = 1)		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	---------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|   transfer data   |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	---------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+-----------------+				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  +-----------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  V")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/--------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|      LMMC end      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\--------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.12  Example of LMMC command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.12	LMMC sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		  to use, set H, L, D, E, IX, A and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		  RAM (IX) ---> VRAM (H,L)-(D,E) (logi-OP : A)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMC:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,A			;B := LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,36")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 36")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,LMMC1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMC1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,LMMC2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMC2:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;first DATA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,B			;A := LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	10110000B		;LMMC command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LOOP:	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	0,A			;check CE bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	Z,EXIT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	7,A			;check TR bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	Z,LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXIT:	LD	A,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.6 LMCM (VRAM - CPU logical transfer)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Data is transferred from the specified VRAM area to CPU in dots (see Figure ")
  ManualsHelp_L("4.87)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.88, writing command code ")
  ManualsHelp_L("A0H in R#46 causes the command to be executed and data to be transferred from ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX-VIDEO. The CPU refers to the TR bit of S#2 and, since data of MSX-VIDEO ")
  ManualsHelp_L("has been prepared if this bit is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the CPU reads data from S#7. When CE ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ", data comes to the end (see Figure 4.89). List 4.13 shows ")
  ManualsHelp_L("an example of using LMCM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.87	Action of LMCM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |   MSX-VIDEO      CPU")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------	   -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    (SX,SY)					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	x------------------------ --> DIX	  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	   NX		|		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY			|-----------------+--->|     |---->|	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|			|		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	-------------------------		  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V					  |    |     |	   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------	   -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXS: select source memory		0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SX:  source origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("SY:  source origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be transferred in X direction (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be transferred in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.88	Register settings of LMCM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMCM register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#32	| SX7| SX6| SX5| SX4| SX3| SX2| SX1| SX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#33	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| source origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#34	| SY7| SY6| SY5| SY4| SY3| SY2| SY1| SY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#35	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SY9| SY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NX ---> X direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NY ---> Y direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | -- | MXS| DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  |    |   direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  |    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  |    +-> direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  +------> select source memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMCM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 0  | 1  | 0  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#7	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | C3 | C2 | C1 | C0 | status register(GRAPHIC4,6)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#7	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | C1 | C0 | status register (GRAPHIC 5)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#7	| C7 | C6 | C5 | C4 | C3 | C2 | C1 | C0 | status register (GRAPHIC 7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.89	LMCM command execution flow chart")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/-------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|     LMCM start    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\-------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|   register setup  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| command execution |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------------->|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | read status register #2 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\ No (TR bit = 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|  data prepared?   |-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  | Yes (TR bit = 1)		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | read status register #7 |		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |<----------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\")
  ManualsHelp_L("+-------|   command end?    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  No	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////")
  ManualsHelp_L("  (CE bit=1)	  | Yes (CE bit = 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  V")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/--------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|      LMCM end      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\--------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Note 1: Read status register #7 in " + Chr(34) + "register setup" + Chr(34) + ", since TR bit should be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("reset before the command execution.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Note 2: Though last data was set in register #7 and TR bit was 1, the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("command would end inside of the MSX-VIDEO and CE would be zero.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.13  Example of LMCM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.13	LMCM sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		  to use, set H, L, D, E, IX, A and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		  VRAM (H,L)-(D,E) ---> RAM (IX)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMCM:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,A			;B := LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,32")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 32")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;SX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;SY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,LMCM1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMCM1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,LMCM2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMCM2:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,7")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,B			;A := LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	10100000B		;LMCM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("LOOP:	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	0,A			;check CE bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	Z,EXIT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	7,A			;check TR bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	Z,LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,7")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(IX+0),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXIT:	LD	A,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.7. LMMM (VRAM->VRAM logical transfer)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Data of the specified VRAM area is transferred into another VRAM area in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("dots (see figure 4.9)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.91, writing command code ")
  ManualsHelp_L("9XH (X means a logical operation) in R#46 causes the command to be executed. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("While the CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the command is being executed. List 4.14 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("shows an example of using LMMM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.90	Actions of LMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|							       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     (SX,SY)						       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	------------------ -->				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	NX	 | DIX				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|		 |				       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	------------------  --+ 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY		      | 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V		      | 			       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      |      (DX,DY)		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      +->  ------------------	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   |		    |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				   ------------------	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|							       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXS: select the source memory		0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select the destination memory	0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SX:  source origin X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("SY:  source origin Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be transferred in X direction (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be transferred in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  destination origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  destination origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.91	Register settings of LMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMMM register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#32	| SX7| SX6| SX5| SX4| SX3| SX2| SX1| SX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#33	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| source origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#34	| SY7| SY6| SY5| SY4| SY3| SY2| SY1| SY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#35	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SY9| SY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| destination origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NX ---> X direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  Number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NY ---> Y direction to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  transferred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| MXS| DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |    |   direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |    +-> direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	  +------> select source memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> select destination memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMMM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 0  | 0  | 1  | L03| L02| L01| L00| CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    +-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      Logical operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.14  Example of LMMM command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.14   LMMM sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, D, E, B, C, A and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 VRAM (H,L)-(D,E) ---> VRAM (B,C) (logi-OP : A)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMM:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			]save LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC			;save DESTINATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,32")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 32")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;SX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;SY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,LMMM1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMM1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L			;make NY and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,LMMM2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMM2:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE			;restore DX,DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			;save DIX,DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),D			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;dummy")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF			;A := LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	10010000B		;LMMM command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L(".	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.8 LMMV (VRAM logical paint)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The specified VRAM area is painted by the colour code in dots (see Figure ")
  ManualsHelp_L("4.92). Logical operations between data in VRAM and the specified data are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("allowed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.93, writing command code ")
  ManualsHelp_L("8Xh (X means a logical operation) in R#46 causes the command to be executed. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("While the CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the command is being executed. List 4.15 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("shows an example of using LMMV.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.92	Actions of LMMV command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |   MSX-VIDEO")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    (DX,DY)					  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	x------------------------ --> DIX	  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|	   NX		|		  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| NY			|<----------------+----|     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	|			|		  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	-------------------------		  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	| DIY					  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	V					  |    |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |    -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select memory			0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NX:  number of dots to be painted in X direction (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("NY:  number of dots to be painted in Y direction (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of NX from the origin	0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of NY from the origin	0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  Painted data")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.93	Register settings of LMMV command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMMV register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	  number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NX ---> X direction to")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	  be painted")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	  number of dots in")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| NY ---> Y direction to")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	  be painted")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)	|data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|to")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)	|be")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|tran")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|sfe")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)	|rred")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| -- | DIY| DIX| -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |   painting direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       +-> painting direction (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> memory selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LMMV command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 1  | 0  | 0  | 0  | L03| L03| L01| L00| CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    +-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      Logical operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.15  Example of LMMV command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.15   LMMV sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, D, E, B, A and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 data B ---> fill VRAM (H,L)-(D,E) (logi-op : A)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMV:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			;save LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC			;save FILL DATA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,36")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 36")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make NX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,LMMV1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMV1:	LD	H,A			;H := NX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L			;make NY and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,LMMV2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LMMV2:	LD	L,A			;L := NY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;FILL DATA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;DIX and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF			;restore LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A,10000000B		;LMMV command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.9 LINE (drawing a line)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Lines can be drawn between any coordinates in VRAM. The parameters to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("specified include the (X,Y) coordinates of the starting point and the X and Y ")
  ManualsHelp_L("lengths in units to the ending point (see Figure 4.94). Logical operations ")
  ManualsHelp_L("between data in VRAM and the specified data are allowed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.94, writing command code ")
  ManualsHelp_L("7XH (X means a logical operation) in R#46 causes the command to be executed. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("While the CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the command is being executed. List 4.16 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("shows an example of using LINE.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.94	Actions of LINE command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			    / :  ^		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			  /   :  |		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			/     : DIY		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		      /       : 		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    /	  Min : 		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  /	      : 		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		/	      : 		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      /     Maj       : 		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	     x................. -> DIX		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	  (DX,DY)				  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: select memory			0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Maj: number of dots of major side (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Maj: number of dots of minor side (0 to 512)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAJ: 0 = The major side is parallel to X axis")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAJ: 1 = The major side is parallel to Y axis,")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 or the major side = the minor side")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction of the end from the origin    0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIY: direction of the end from the origin    0 = below, 1 = above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX:  origin  X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY:  origin  Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  Line colour data")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.95	Register settings of LINE command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LINE register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#40	| NX7| NX6| NX5| NX4| NX3| NX2| NX1| NX0|	      number of dots")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| Maj (NX) -> of the major")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#41	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NX8|	      side")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#42	| NY7| NY6| NY5| NY4| NY3| NY2| NY1| NY0|	      number of dots")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| Min (NY) -> of the minor")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#43	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | NY9| NY8|	      side")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|co-")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|lour")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)	|code")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	|  0 | -- | MXD| -- | DIY| DIX| -- | MAJ| ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |    |	     major side selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |    V")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |   direction to the end (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |	       +-> direction to the end (Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> memory selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> LINE command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 0  | 1  | 1  | 1  | L03| L03| L01| L00| CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    +-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      Logical operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.16  Example of LINE command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.16   LINE sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, D, E, B, A and go")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 draw LINE (H,L)-(D,E) with color B, log-op A")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINE:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			;save LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC			;save COLOR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP		;wait end of command")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,36")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#17 := 36")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#3's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;DX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;DY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H			;make DX and DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,LINE1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINE1:	LD	H,A			;H := DX , D := DIX")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L			;make DY and DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SUB	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00001000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NC,LINE2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEG")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINE2:	LD	L,A			;L := DY , E := DIY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	H			;make Maj and Min")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	C,LINE3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;long side")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;short side")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,00000001B		;MAJ := 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	LINE4")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINE3:	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H			;NX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L			;NY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,00000000B		;MAJ := 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINE4:	OR	D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E			;A := DIX , DIY , MAJ")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL			;H := COLOR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF			;A := LOGICAL OPERATION")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	01110000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.10 SRCH (colour code search)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SRCH searches for the existence of the specified colour from any coordinate ")
  ManualsHelp_L("on VRAM to the right or the left (see figure 4.96). This is very useful for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("paint routines.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.97, writing 60H in R#46 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("causes the command to be executed. The command terminates when the objective ")
  ManualsHelp_L("colour is found or when it cannot be found after searching for it to the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("screen edge. While the CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the command is being executed ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(see Figure 4.98).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After the command ends, the objective colour code is stored in S#8 and S#9. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.17 shows an example of using SRCH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.96	Actions of SRCH command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    (SX,SY)	 DIX			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       x......................>x	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				    Border	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				    colour	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|				    point	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: memory selection for the seacrh	0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SX: search origin X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("SY: search origin Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIX: direction for the search from the origin	 0 = right, 1 = left")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("EQ:  0 = ends the execution when the border colour is found")
  ManualsHelp_L("     1 = ends the execution when the colour is found other than the")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 border colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  border colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.97	Register settings of SRCH command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> SRCH register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#32	| SX7| SX6| SX5| SX4| SX3| SX2| SX1| SX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#33	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| search origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#34	| SY7| SY6| SY5| SY4| SY3| SY2| SY1| SY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#35	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SY9| SY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("									 b")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+o")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)	|r")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|d")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|e")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|r")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|c")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|o")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|l")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)	|o")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+u")
  ManualsHelp_L("									 r")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	| -- | -- | MXD| -- | -- | DIX| EQ | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |		    |	the condition for terminating")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |		    |	the execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |		    V")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |		   search direction (X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> memory selection for the search")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> SRCH command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 0  | 1  | 1  | 0  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#2	| -- | -- | -- | BO | -- | -- | -- | CE | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 |		     when the command ends : 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 +-------> when the border colour is found : 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#8	| BX7| BX6| BX5| BX4| BX3| BX2| BX1| BX0| X-coordinate when the")
  ManualsHelp_L("	----------------------------------------- border colour is found")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#9	| 1  | 1  | 1  | 1  | 1  | 1  | 1  | BX8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.98	SRCH command execution flowchart")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/-------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|     SRCH start    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\-------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|   register setup  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| command execution |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------------->|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | Read status register #2 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	//////////+\\\\\\\\\\")
  ManualsHelp_L("+-------|   command end?    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   No	\\\\\\\\\\+//////////")
  ManualsHelp_L("(CE bit = 1)	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  | Yes (CE bit = 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     /////////////+\\\\\\\\\\\\\")
  ManualsHelp_L("+----| Is border colour found? |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    \\\\\\\\\\\\\+/////////////")
  ManualsHelp_L("| No		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| (BO bit = 0)	  | Yes (BO bit = 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | Read status register #8 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    | Read status register #2 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    ---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------------->|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  V")
  ManualsHelp_L("	/--------------------\")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|      SRCH end      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	\--------------------/")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.17  Example of SRCH command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.17   SRCH sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, E, A as follows")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 srch (x:H, y:L, color:E, arg(reg#45) : A)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 returns: Z  (not found)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";			  NZ (A := X)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SRCH:	DI				;disable interrupt")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF			;save arg")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C			;C := PORT#1's address")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,32+80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#32 := H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#33 := 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#34 := L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#35 := 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,44+80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A			;R#44 := E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF			;A := ARG")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E			;R#45 := A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,01100000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E			;R#46 := SRCH command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LOOP:	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	0,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,LOOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,9")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BIT	4,E")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.18  Simple PAINT routine using SRCH and LINE")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.18   SRCH and LINE sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 search color to right and left,")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 then draw line between the two points")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EXTRN	SRCH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EXTRN	LINE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Y	EQU	0A800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("X	EQU	0A801H")
  ManualsHelp_L("COL	EQU	0A802H")
  ManualsHelp_L("ARG	EQU	0A803H")
  ManualsHelp_L("PCOL	EQU	0A804H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAIN:	LD	(STK),SP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	SP,AREA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,(Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(COL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(ARG)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SET	2,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	SRCH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,S1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("S1:	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(ARG)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RES	2,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	SRCH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,S2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(X)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("S2:	DEC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(PCOL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,0			;PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	LINE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	SP,(STK)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- work area -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STK:	DS	2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DS	200")
  ManualsHelp_L("AREA:	$")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.19  Example of the use of simple PAINT routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1000 '***********************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("1010 ' list 4.19   SRCH and LINE sample")
  ManualsHelp_L("1020 ' Operate cursor while holding down the space bar.")
  ManualsHelp_L("1030 '***********************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("1040 '")
  ManualsHelp_L("1050 SCREEN 5")
  ManualsHelp_L("1060 FOR I=0 TO 50:LINE -(RND(1)*255,RND(1)*211),15:NEXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("1070 I=&HA000 :DEF USR=I")
  ManualsHelp_L("1080 READ A$")
  ManualsHelp_L("1090 IF  A$=" + Chr(34) + "END" + Chr(34) + " THEN 1130")
  ManualsHelp_L("1100   POKE I,VAL(" + Chr(34) + "&H" + Chr(34) + "+A$):I=I+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1110   READ A$")
  ManualsHelp_L("1120 GOTO 1090")
  ManualsHelp_L("1130 X=128:Y=100:COL=15:PCOL=2:ARG=0")
  ManualsHelp_L("1140 CURS=0")
  ManualsHelp_L("1150 A=STICK(0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1160 CURS=(CURS+1) AND 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1170 LINE (X-5,I)-(X+5,I),15,,XOR")
  ManualsHelp_L("1180 LINE (X,Y-5)-(X,Y+5),15,,XOR")
  ManualsHelp_L("1190 IF CURS=1 THEN 1290")
  ManualsHelp_L("1200 IF A=1 THEN Y=Y-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1210 IF A=2 THEN Y=Y-1:X=X+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1220 IF A=3 THEN X=X+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1230 IF A=4 THEN X=X+1:Y=Y+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1240 IF A=5 THEN Y=Y+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1250 IF A=6 THEN Y=Y+1:X=X-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1260 IF A=7 THEN X=X-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1270 IF A=8 THEN X=X-1:Y=Y-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1280 IF STRIG(9) THEN GOSUB 1300")
  ManualsHelp_L("1290 GOTO 1150")
  ManualsHelp_L("1300 POKE &HA800,Y")
  ManualsHelp_L("1310 POKE &HA801,X")
  ManualsHelp_L("1320 POKE &HA802,COL")
  ManualsHelp_L("1330 POKE &HA803,ARG")
  ManualsHelp_L("1340 POKE &HA804,PCOL")
  ManualsHelp_L("1350 A=USR(0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1360 RETURN")
  ManualsHelp_L("1370 DATA ED,73,80,A8,31,4A,A9,2A,00,A8,3A,02")
  ManualsHelp_L("1380 DATA A8,5F,3A,03,A8,E5,D5,CB,D7,CD,AD")
  ManualsHelp_L("1390 DATA A0,D1,E1,C2,21,A0,3A,01,A8")
  ManualsHelp_L("1400 DATA 3D,3C,F5,3A,03,A8,CB,97,CD,AD,A0,C2")
  ManualsHelp_L("1410 DATA 32,A0,3A,01,AB,3C,3D,57,F1,67,3A")
  ManualsHelp_L("1420 DATA 00,A8,6F,5F,3A,04,A8,47,3E")
  ManualsHelp_L("1430 DATA 00,CD,49,A0,ED,7B,80,A8,C9,F3,F5,CD")
  ManualsHelp_L("1440 DATA 0D,A1,C5,3A,06,00,4F,0C,3E,24,ED")
  ManualsHelp_L("1450 DATA 79,3E,91,ED,79,0C,0C,AF,ED")
  ManualsHelp_L("1460 DATA 61,ED,79,ED,69,ED,79,7C,92,16,04,D2")
  ManualsHelp_L("1470 DATA 72,A0,16,00,ED,44,67,7D,93,1E,08")
  ManualsHelp_L("1480 DATA D2,7E,A0,1E,00,ED,44,BC,DA")
  ManualsHelp_L("1490 DATA 90,A0,ED,79,AF,ED,79,ED,61,ED,79,26")
  ManualsHelp_L("1500 DATA 01,C3,9C,A0,ED,61,67,AF,ED,79,ED")
  ManualsHelp_L("1510 DATA 61,ED,79,26,00,7C,B2,B3,E1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1520 DATA ED,61,ED,79,F1,E6,0F,F6,70,ED,79,FB")
  ManualsHelp_L("1530 DATA C9,F5,F3,CD,0D,A1,ED,4B,06,00,0C")
  ManualsHelp_L("1540 DATA 3E,A0,16,00,ED,61,ED,79,3C")
  ManualsHelp_L("1550 DATA ED,51,ED,79,3C,ED,69,ED,79,3C,ED,51")
  ManualsHelp_L("1560 DATA ED,79,3E,AC,ED,59,ED,79,3C,5F,F1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1570 DATA ED,79,ED,59,3E,60,ED,79,1C")
  ManualsHelp_L("1580 DATA ED,59,3E,02,CD,FD,A0,CB,47,C2,E2,A0")
  ManualsHelp_L("1590 DATA 5F,3E,08,CD,FD,A0,57,3E,00,CD,FD")
  ManualsHelp_L("1600 DATA A0,7A,CB,63,FB,C9,C5,ED,4B")
  ManualsHelp_L("1610 DATA 06,00,0C,ED,79,3E,8F,ED,79,ED,78,C1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1620 DATA C9,3E,02,CD,FD,A0,E6,01,C2,0D,A1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1630 DATA AF,CD,FD,A0,C9,END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.11 PSET (drawing a point)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("A point is drawn at any coordinate in VRAM (see figure 4.99).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.100, writing 5XH (X means a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("logical operation) in R#46 causes the command to be executed. While the CE ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the command is being executed. List 4.20 shows an example ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of using PSET.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.99	Actions of PSET command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       (DX,DY)				  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  x				  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: memory selection			0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DX: origin X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("DY: origin Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLR (R#44:Colour register):  point colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.100  Register settings of PSET command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> PSET register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#36	| DX7| DX6| DX5| DX4| DX3| DX2| DX1| DX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#37	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#38	| DY7| DY6| DY5| DY4| DY3| DY2| DY1| DY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| DY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#39	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | DY9| DY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#44	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 4,6)	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|co-")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|lour")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 5)	|code")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("									|data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| CR7| CR6| CR5| CR4| CR3| CR2| CR1| CR0| CLR (GRAPHIC 7)	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	| 0  | -- | MXD| -- | -- | -- | -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     +-----------> memory selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> PSET command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 0  | 1  | 0  | 1  | L03| L02| L01| L00| CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    +-------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      Logical operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.20  Example of PSET command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.20   PSET sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L, E, A as follows")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 pset (x:H, y:L), color:E, logi-OP:A")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PSET:	DI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,36")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,44")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,01010000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5.12 POINT (reading a colour code)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("POINT reads the colour code in any coordinate of VRAM (see Figure 4.101).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("After setting the parameters as shown in Figure 4.102, writing 40H in R#46 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("causes the command to be executed. While the CE bit of S#2 is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("command is being executed. After the command terminates, the colour code of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the specified coordinate is set in S#7. List 4.21 shows an example of using ")
  ManualsHelp_L("POINT.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.101  Actions of POINT command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      VRAM or expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       (SX,SY)				  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  x				  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|						  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MXD: memory selection			0 = VRAM, 1 = expansion RAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SX:  origin X-coordinate (0 to 511)")
  ManualsHelp_L("SY:  origin Y-coordinate (0 to 1023)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 4.102  Register settings of POINT command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> POINT register setup")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#32	| SX7| SX6| SX5| SX4| SX3| SX2| SX1| SX0|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SX ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#33	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SX8|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("							| origin")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#34	| SY7| SY6| SY5| SY4| SY3| SY2| SY1| SY0|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----| SY ---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#35	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | SY9| SY8|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#45	| -- | -- | -- | MXS| -- | -- | -- | -- | ARG (Argument register)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  +-----------> memory selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("> POINT command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    MSB   7    6    5	 4    3    2	1    0	  LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R#46	| 0  | 1  | 0  | 0  | -- | -- | -- | -- | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#2	| -- | -- | -- | -- | -- | -- | -- | CE | CMR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("					     when the command ends : 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		     --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("S#7	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | C3 | C2 | C1 | C0 | CL (GRAPHIC 4,6)     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		       |co-")
  ManualsHelp_L("								       |lour")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | 0  | C1 | C0 | CL (GRAPHIC 5)       |code")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("								       |data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| C7 | C6 | C5 | C4 | C3 | C2 | C1 | C0 | CL (GRAPHIC 7)       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-----------------------------------------		     --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.21  Example of POINT command execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.21   POINT sample")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 to use, set H, L as follows")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 POINT ( x:H, y:L )")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		 returns:   A := COLOR CODE")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	POINT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP:	EQU	0006H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRVDP:	EQU	0007H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("POINT:	DI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,32")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+17")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+45")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,01000000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,80H+46")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,7")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.STATUS:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(WRVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8FH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OUT	(C),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(RDVDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(C)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT.VDP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,WAIT.VDP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GET.STATUS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.22  PAINT routine using PSET and POINT")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 4.22  paint routine using PSET and POINT")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	ENTRY:	X:H, Y:L, BORDER COLOR:D, PAINT COLOR:E")
  ManualsHelp_L(";****************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EXTRN	PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EXTRN	POINT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Q.LENGTH	EQU	256*2*2")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAX.Y		EQU	211")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- paint main routine -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PAINT:	CALL	POINT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	Z")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	INIT.Q")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(COL),DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUT.Q")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(COL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A			;logi-OP : PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("PAINT0: CALL	GET.Q")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	NZ,PAINT.SUB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	Z,PAINT1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEC	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PAINT.SUB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("PAINT1: DEC	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	NZ,PAINT.SUB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,MAX.Y")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	NC,PAINT.SUB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	PAINT0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- check point and pset -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PAINT.SUB:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	POINT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(BORD)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	Z")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(COL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	Z")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUT.Q")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- init Q.BUFFER pointer -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIT.Q:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,Q.BUF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(Q.TOP),HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(Q.BTM),HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- put point to Q.BUF (X:H , Y:L) -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUT.Q:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,(Q.TOP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,Q.BUF+Q.LENGTH+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A			;clear CARRY")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SBC	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	C,PUT.Q1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,Q.BUF")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUT.Q1:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(HL),D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(HL),E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(Q.TOP),HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- take point data to D, E -----")
  ManualsHelp_L(";      returns:   NC   H:x, L:y")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		  C    buffer empty")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.Q:	LD	HL,(Q.BTM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,(Q.TOP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SBC	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	NZ,GET.Q0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SCF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.Q0: LD	HL,(Q.BTM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,Q.BUF+Q.LENGTH+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SBC	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	C,GET.Q1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,Q.BUF")
  ManualsHelp_L("GET.Q1: LD	D,(HL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,(HL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(Q.BTM),HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- work area -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("COL	DS	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("BORD	DS	1")
  ManualsHelp_L("Q.TOP	DS	2")
  ManualsHelp_L("Q.BTM	DS	2")
  ManualsHelp_L("Q.BUF	DS	Q.LENGTH")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 4.23  Example of using the PAINT routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1000 '***********************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("1010 ' list 4.23   paint routine using POINT and PSET")
  ManualsHelp_L("1020 ' Position cursor at beginnig of paint area and press the space bar.")
  ManualsHelp_L("1030 '***********************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("1040 '")
  ManualsHelp_L("1050 SCREEN 5")
  ManualsHelp_L("1060 FOR I=0 TO 50")
  ManualsHelp_L("1070 LINE -(RND(1)*255,RND(1)*211),15")
  ManualsHelp_L("1080 NEXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("1090 I=&HA000 :DEF USR=I")
  ManualsHelp_L("1100 READ A$")
  ManualsHelp_L("1110 IF  A$=" + Chr(34) + "END" + Chr(34) + " THEN 1150")
  ManualsHelp_L("1120   POKE I,VAL(" + Chr(34) + "&H" + Chr(34) + "+A$):I=I+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1130   READ A$")
  ManualsHelp_L("1140 GOTO 1110")
  ManualsHelp_L("1150 X=128:Y=100:COL=15:PCOL=2")
  ManualsHelp_L("1160 CURS=0")
  ManualsHelp_L("1170 A=STICK(0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1180 CURS=(CURS+1) AND 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1190 LINE (X-5,I)-(X+5,I),15,,XOR")
  ManualsHelp_L("1200 LINE (X,Y-5)-(X,Y+5),15,,XOR")
  ManualsHelp_L("1210 IF CURS=1 THEN 1310")
  ManualsHelp_L("1220 IF A=1 THEN Y=Y-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1230 IF A=2 THEN Y=Y-1:X=X+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1240 IF A=3 THEN X=X+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1250 IF A=4 THEN X=X+1:Y=Y+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1260 IF A=5 THEN Y=Y+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1270 IF A=6 THEN Y=Y+1:X=X-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1280 IF A=7 THEN X=X-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1290 IF A=8 THEN X=X-1:Y=Y-1")
  ManualsHelp_L("1300 IF STRIG(9) THEN GOSUB 1320")
  ManualsHelp_L("1310 GOTO 1170")
  ManualsHelp_L("1320 POKE &HA8CA,Y")
  ManualsHelp_L("1330 POKE &HA8CB,X")
  ManualsHelp_L("1340 POKE &HA8CD,COL")
  ManualsHelp_L("1350 POKE &HA8CC,PCOL")
  ManualsHelp_L("1360 A=USR(0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("1370 RETURN")
  ManualsHelp_L("1380 DATA ED,73,00,A8,31,CA,A8,2A,CA,A8,ED,5B,CC,A8,CD,67")
  ManualsHelp_L("1390 DATA A0,ED,7B,00,A8,C9,E5,21,D4,A8,22,D0,A8,22,D2,A8")
  ManualsHelp_L("1400 DATA E1,C9,EB,2A,D0,A8,01,D5,AC,B7,E5,ED,42,E1,DA,34")
  ManualsHelp_L("1410 DATA A0,21,D4,A8,72,23,73,23,22,D0,A8,EB,C9,2A,D2,A8")
  ManualsHelp_L("1420 DATA ED,4B,D0,A8,B7,ED,42,C2,4C,A0,37,C9,2A,D2,A8,01")
  ManualsHelp_L("1430 DATA D5,AC,B7,E5,ED,42,E1,DA,5D,A0,21,D4,A8,56,23,5E")
  ManualsHelp_L("1440 DATA 23,22,D2,A8,B7,EB,C9,CD,B8,A0,BA,C8,CD,16,A0,ED")
  ManualsHelp_L("1450 DATA 53,CE,A8,CD,22,A0,3A,CE,A8,5F,AF,CD,F4,A0,CD,3D")
  ManualsHelp_L("1460 DATA A0,D8,24,C4,A1,A0,25,CA,8F,A0,25,CD,A1,A0,24,2D")
  ManualsHelp_L("1470 DATA 3E,FF,BD,C4,A1,A0,2C,2C,3E,D3,BD,D4,A1,A0,C3,7E")
  ManualsHelp_L("1480 DATA A0,CD,B8,A0,57,3A,CF,A8,BA,C8,3A,CE,A8,BA,C8,5F")
  ManualsHelp_L("1490 DATA AF,CD,F4,A0,CD,22,A0,C9,F3,CD,3A,A1,ED,4B,06,00")
  ManualsHelp_L("1500 DATA 0C,3E,20,ED,79,3E,91,ED,79,0C,0C,AF,ED,61,ED,79")
  ManualsHelp_L("1510 DATA ED,69,ED,79,0D,0D,ED,79,3E,AD,ED,79,3E,40,ED,79")
  ManualsHelp_L("1520 DATA 3E,AE,ED,79,CD,3A,A1,3E,07,CD,2A,A1,F5,AF,CD,2A")
  ManualsHelp_L("1530 DATA A1,F1,FB,C9,F3,F5,CD,3A,A1,ED,4B,06,00,0C,3E,24")
  ManualsHelp_L("1540 DATA ED,79,3E,91,ED,79,C5,0C,0C,AF,ED,61,ED,79,ED,69")
  ManualsHelp_L("1550 DATA ED,79,C1,3E,2C,ED,79,3E,91,ED,79,0C,0C,ED,59,AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("1560 DATA ED,79,1E,50,F1,B3,ED,79,FB,C9,C5,ED,4B,06,00,0C")
  ManualsHelp_L("1570 DATA ED,79,3E,8F,ED,79,ED,78,C1,C9,3E,02,CD,2A,A1,E6")
  ManualsHelp_L("1580 DATA 01,C2,3A,A1,AF,CD,2A,A1,C9")
  ManualsHelp_L("1590 DATA END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.6 Speeding Up Commands")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX-VIDEO performs various screen management duties in addition to executing ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the specified commands. Sometimes the command execution speed seems to be a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bit slow because of this. Thus, by discarding these operations, the speed of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the command executions can be made faster. This can be done using the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("following method.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1. Sprite display inhibition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This method is useful since speedup can be realised while the screen remains ")
  ManualsHelp_L("displayed. Set " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " to bit 1 of R#8.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2. Screen display inhibition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This method cannot be used frequently except in the case of initialising the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("screen, since the screen fades out in this mode. Set " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " to bit 6 of R#1.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.7 Register Status at Command Termination")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Table 4.7 shows the register status at the command termination for each ")
  ManualsHelp_L("command.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the number of dots to be executed in Y direction assumes N, the values ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of SY*, DY*, and NYB can be calculated as follows:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SY*=SY+N, DY*=DY+N .................... when DIY bit is 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SY*=SY-N, DY*=DY-N .................... when DIY bit is 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NYB=NY-N")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	Note: when MAJ bit is 0 in LINE, N = N - 1.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 4.7  Register status at command termination")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| command name | SX  | SY  | DX  | DY  | NX  | NY  | CLR |CMR H|CMR L| ARG |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     HMMC     | --- | --- | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     YMMM     | --- |	.  | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     HMMM     | --- |	.  | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     HMMV     | --- | --- | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     LMMC     | --- | --- | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     LMCM     | --- |	.  | --- | --- | --- |	#  |  .  |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     LMMM     | --- |	.  | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     LMMV     | --- | --- | --- |  .  | --- |	#  | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     LINE     | --- | --- | --- |  .  | --- | --- | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     SRCH     | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     PSET     | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     POINT    | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  .  |  0  | --- | --- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("--- :	no change")
  ManualsHelp_L(" .  :	coordinate (SY*, DY*) and the colour code at the command termination")
  ManualsHelp_L(" #  :	the number of counts (NYB), when the screen edge is fetched")
  ManualsHelp_Commit("4. VDP e Tela (parte 6)", "MSX2 Technical Handbook")

  ManualsHelp_Begin()
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX2 TECHNICAL HANDBOOK")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Edited by:		ASCII Systems Division")
  ManualsHelp_L("Published by:		ASCII Coprporation - JAPAN")
  ManualsHelp_L("First edition:		March 1987")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Text file typed by:	Nestor Soriano (Konami Man) - SPAIN")
  ManualsHelp_L("			October 1997")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.2, unused bits are marked as " + Chr(34) + "x" + Chr(34) + ", and inverted signals are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("marked with " + Chr(34) + "*" + Chr(34) + ", for easiest readability.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- Figure 5.17B was added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In List 5.4, the last line before the work area, " + Chr(34) + "JR START" + Chr(34) + ", has been ")
  ManualsHelp_L("corrected to " + Chr(34) + "JR SCAN" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.18, the addresses for GETPNT y PUTPNT were swapped. They have ")
  ManualsHelp_L("been corrected.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of BIOS routines PINLIN and INLIN, " + Chr(34) + "BUF" + Chr(34) + " address has been ")
  ManualsHelp_L("corrected from F55DH to F55EH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.22 (B), " + Chr(34) + "Arabaic mode display" + Chr(34) + " has been changed to " + Chr(34) + "Arabic or ")
  ManualsHelp_L("kana mode display" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of BIOS routine GTTRIG, the input needed for reading B ")
  ManualsHelp_L("buttons has been added in the " + Chr(34) + "Input" + Chr(34) + " field.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Table 5.5, in the Note 4, " + Chr(34) + "the trigger button of the mouse or the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("trigger button" + Chr(34) + " has been changed to " + Chr(34) + "the trigger button of the mouse or the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("trigger button of the track ball" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.29, " + Chr(34) + "1200 or 2400 hours" + Chr(34) + " indication has been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "12 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("or 24 hours" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.32, " + Chr(34) + "Register 3 #11" + Chr(34) + " indication has been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "Register ")
  ManualsHelp_L("#11" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.33, " + Chr(34) + "Adjust Y (8 to +7)" + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "Adjust Y (-8 to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("+7)" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of BIOS routine WRTCLK, the input needed in the A register ")
  ManualsHelp_L("has been added in the " + Chr(34) + "Input" + Chr(34) + " field.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHAPTER 5 - ACCESS TO PERIPHERALS THROUGH BIOS (Parts 1 to 6)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The basic philosophy of MSX is to have a standard interface, independent of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("machines or versions, to access peripherals through BIOS. Thus, the user ")
  ManualsHelp_L("should get to know about using BIOS first. In chapter 5, accessing ")
  ManualsHelp_L("peripherals using BIOS and the structure used for each peripheral are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("described.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1. PSG AND SOUND OUTPUT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX has the following three kinds of sound output functions, but function (3) ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is not installed in the standard MSX, so it is not described in this manual. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("This section describes functions (1) and (2).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1)  PSG sound output (3 channels, 8 octaves)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2)  Sound output by 1 bit I/O port")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(3)  Sound output by MSX-AUDIO (FM sound generator) ........ not described")
  ManualsHelp_L("							     in this manual")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.1. PSG functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("An AY-3-8910 compatible LSI is used for the MSX music play function and for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("BEEP tone generation. This LSI is referred to as the PSG (Programmable Sound ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Generator), and can generate complex music and varios tones. It has the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("following features:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* There are three tone generators, each of which can independently specify ")
  ManualsHelp_L("4096 scales (equivalent to 8 octaves) and 16 volume levels.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* It can generate piano and organ tones by using envelope patterns. Note ")
  ManualsHelp_L("that, since there is only one envelope generator, the tone of only one ")
  ManualsHelp_L("channel can be modified fundamentally.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* With the noise generator inside, tones such as the wind or waves can easily ")
  ManualsHelp_L("be generated. Note that since there is only one noise generator, only one ")
  ManualsHelp_L("channel can generate the noise.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Any necessary frequency, such as the tone or the envelope, is obtained by ")
  ManualsHelp_L("dividing the input clock (in MSX, it is defined that fc = 1.7897725 MHz). So ")
  ManualsHelp_L("there is no unsteady pitch or rythm.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.1  PSG block diagram")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(" R0, R1 		    R7			R8")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------	 -------------	       ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Tone generator A | --> |	     | ------> | Volume control amplifier A |")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------	 |	     |	  +--> ---------------------------+--")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 |	     |	  |	      Channel A output <--+")
  ManualsHelp_L(" R2, R3 		 |  Three    |	  |	R9")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------	 |	     |	  |    ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Tone generator B | --> |  Channel  | ---:--> | Volume control amplifier B |")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------	 |	     |	  +--> ---------------------------+--")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 |  Mixer    |	  |	      Channel B output <--+")
  ManualsHelp_L(" R4, R5 		 |	     |	  |	R9")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------	 |	     |	  |    ------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Tone generator C | --> |	     | ---:--> | Volume control amplifier C |")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------	 -------------	  +--> ---------------------------+--")
  ManualsHelp_L("				 ^	  |	      Channel C output <--+")
  ManualsHelp_L("				 |	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    R6		 |	  |  R11, R12, R13")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 ---------------------	 ------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 |  Noise generator  |	 |  Envelope generator	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 ---------------------	 ------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The PSG has two additional I/O (input/output) ports used for other than tone ")
  ManualsHelp_L("generating functions, which are omitted in the block diagram above. MSX uses ")
  ManualsHelp_L("them as general-purpose I/O ports to connect to I/O devices such as joystick, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("a touch pad, a paddle, or a mouse. These general-purpose I/O ports are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("described in section 5.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* PSG registers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since the PSG generates tones, the CPU simply notifies PSG when the tone is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to be changed. This is done by writing values in 16 8-bit registers inside ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the PSG as shown in Figure 5.2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Roles and uses of these registers are described below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting the tone frequency (R0 to R5)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Each tone frequency of channel A, B, and C is set by R0 to R5. The input ")
  ManualsHelp_L("clock frequency (fc = 1.7897725 MHz) is divided by 16 and the result is the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("standard frequency. Each channel divides the standard frequency by the 12-bit ")
  ManualsHelp_L("data assigned for each, and the objective pitch is obtained. The following ")
  ManualsHelp_L("relation exists between 12-bit data (TP) and the tone frequency to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("generated (ft).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ft = fc/(16 * TP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   = 0.11186078125/TP [MHz]")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   = 111860.78125/TP [Hz]")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("A 12-bit data TP is specified for each channel by 4 high order bit coarse ")
  ManualsHelp_L("tune CT and 8 low order bit fine tune value FT, as shown in Figure 5.3. Table ")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.1 shows the register settings to make the scales.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.2  PSG register structure")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			Bit |	  |	|     |     |	  |	|     |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			    | B7  | B6	| B5  | B4  | B3  | B2	| B1  | B0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Register		    |	  |	|     |     |	  |	|     |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R0    | Channel A note |		     8 low order bits		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------|		    |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R1    | Dividing rate  |  x     x	   x	 x  |	4 high order bits   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R2    | Channel B note |		     8 low order bits		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------|		    |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R3    | Dividing rate  |  x     x	   x	 x  |	4 high order bits   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R4    | Channel C note |		     8 low order bits		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------|		    |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R5    | Dividing rate  |  x     x	   x	 x  |	4 high order bits   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R6    | Noise div. rate|  x     x	   x  | 			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	   |		    |  IN*/OUT	|      NOISE*	  |	 TONE*	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R7    | Enable*	    |-----------+-----------------+-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	   |		    | IOB | IOA |  C  |  B  |  A  |  C	|  B  |  A  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------+-----+-----------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R8    | Chan. A volume |  x     x	   x  |  M  |			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------+-----+-----------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R9    | Chan. B volume |  x     x	   x  |  M  |			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------+-----+-----------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R10   | Chan. C volume |  x     x	   x  |  M  |			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R11   |		    |		     8 low order bits		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------| Envelope Cycle |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R12   |		    |		     8 high order bits		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R13   | Env. wave shape|  x     x	   x	 x  |			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R14   | I/O port A     |						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R15   | I/O port B     |						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NOTE:	x = unused bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	* = inverted signal")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.3  Setting the pitch")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R0, R2, R4	|		     8	bits			| --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		-------------------------------------------------   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		-------------------------------------------------   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("R0, R2, R4	|  x	 x     x     x	|	 4 bits 	|   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		-------------------------------------------------   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("						    |		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    ----------------------------------------+		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    |							    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    V							    V")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Coarse Tune (CT)	|		 Fine Tune (FT) 	      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|								      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+-------------------------------- TP ---------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("						   [ Channel A - R0, R1 ]")
  ManualsHelp_L("						   [ Channel B - R2, R3 ]")
  ManualsHelp_L("						   [ Channel C - R4, R5 ]")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 5.1  Setting the tone frequency (scale data)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	Octave |     |	   |	 |     |     |	   |	 |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	       |  1  |	2  |  3  |  4  |  5  |	6  |  7  |  8  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Note	       |     |	   |	 |     |     |	   |	 |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      C       | D5D | 6AF | 357 | 1AC |  D6 |	6B |  35 |  1B |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      C#      | C9C | 64E | 327 | 194 |  CA |	65 |  32 |  19 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      D       | BE7 | 5F4 | 2FA | 17D |  BE |	5F |  30 |  18 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      D#      | B3C | 59E | 2CF | 168 |  84 |	5A |  2D |  16 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      E       | A9B | 54E | 2A7 | 153 |  AA |	55 |  2A |  15 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      F       | A02 | 501 | 281 | 140 |  A0 |	50 |  28 |  14 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      F#      | 973 | 4BA | 25D | 12E |  97 |	4C |  26 |  13 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      G       | 8EB | 476 | 23B | 11D |  8F |	47 |  24 |  12 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      G#      | 88B | 436 | 21B | 10D |  87 |	43 |  22 |  11 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      A       | 7F2 | 3F9 | 1FD |  FE |  7F |	40 |  20 |  10 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      A#      | 780 | 3C0 | 1E0 |  F0 |  78 |	3C |  1E |   F |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      B       | 714 | 38A | 1C5 |  E3 |  71 |	39 |  1C |   E |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting the noise frequency (R6)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The noise generator is used for synthesizing explosion sounds or wave sounds. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("The PSG can send the noise output by the noise generator to channels A to C. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since there is only one noise generator, the same noise is sent to all ")
  ManualsHelp_L("channels. By changing the average frequency, various noise effects can be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("obtained and this is done by R6 register settings. The 5 low order bit data ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(NP) of this register is divides into the standard frequency (fc/16) and this ")
  ManualsHelp_L("determines the average frequency of the noise (fn).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.4  Setting the noise frequency")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("      -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R6    |  x     x     x	|			      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("      -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|			      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			+------------- NP ------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The following relation exists between NP and fn.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	fn = fc/(16 * NP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   = 0.11186078125/NP [MHz]")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   = 111860.78125/NP [Hz]")
  ManualsHelp_L("	")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since the value of NP is from 1 to 31, the average frequency of the noise can ")
  ManualsHelp_L("be set from 3.6kHz to 111.9kHz.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Mixing the sound (R7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("R7 is used to select the output of the tone and noise generator, or a mixture ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of both. As shown in Figure 5.5, the 3 low order bits (B0 to B2) of R7 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("control the tone output and the next 3 bits (B3 to B5) control the noise ")
  ManualsHelp_L("output. In both cases, when the corresponding bit is 0, the output is ON and, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("when 1, it is OFF.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.5  Output selection for each channel")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("      -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R7    | B7  | B6  | B5	| B4  | B3  | B2  | B1	| B0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("      -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      V")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    B7	   B6		  B5	  B4	  B3		B2	B1	B0")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------     -------------------------     -------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Input enable* |     |     Noise enable*     |     |	  Tone enable*	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|---------------|     |-----------------------|     |-----------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   B	|   A	|     |   C   |   B   |   A   |     |	C   |	B   |	A   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------     -------------------------     -------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" I/O port	       Noise output		     Tone output")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Input - 0		 ON - 0 		       ON - 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Output - 1		 OFF - 1		       OFF - 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The 2 high order bits of R7 do not affect sound output. These are used to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("determine the direction of the data of two I/O ports which PSG has. When the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("corresponding bit is 0, the input mode is selected and, when 0, the output ")
  ManualsHelp_L("mode is selected. In MSX, port A is used for the input and port B for the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("output, so it should always be set so that bit 6 = " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " and bit 7 = " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting the volume (R8 to R10)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("R8 to R10 are used to specify the volume of each channel. Two ways can be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("selected by these registers: specifying the fixed volume by 4-bit data (0 to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("15) and generating sound effects such as vibrato or fade-out by using the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("envelope.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.6  Setting the volume")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R8, R9, R10    |  x	x     x  | B4  | B3  | B2  | B1  | B0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    |  |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    |  +---------- L ----------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    V")
  ManualsHelp_L("				  Use envelope:")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    No	- 0 (set volume by the value of L)")
  ManualsHelp_L("				    Yes - 1 (ignore the value of L)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When bit 4 of these registers is " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ", the envelope is not used and the 4 low ")
  ManualsHelp_L("order bit value L (0 to 15) of the registers specify the volume. When bit 4 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", the volume depends on the envelope signals and the value L is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("ignored.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting the envelope cycle (R11, R12)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("R11 and R12 specify the envelope cycle in 16-bit data. The 8 high order bits ")
  ManualsHelp_L("are set in R12 and the 8 low order bits are set in R11.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.7  Setting the envelope cycle")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R11	   |						   | --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -------------------------------------------------   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -------------------------------------------------   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("R12	   |						   |   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   -------------------------------------------------   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("					       |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      ---------------------------------+	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      | 					       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      V 					       V")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	   Coarse Tune (CT)	     |		  Fine Tune (FT)	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|									    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+----------------------------------- EP ------------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The following relation exists between the envelope cycle T and 16-bit data ")
  ManualsHelp_L("EP.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	T = (256 * EP) / fc")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  = (256 * EP) / 1.787725 [MHz]")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  = 143.03493  * EP [micro second]")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting the envelope pattern (R13)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("R13 sets the envelope pattern by the 4 low order bit data as shown in Figure ")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.8. The intervals of T specified in the figure correspond to the envelope ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cycle specified by R11 and R12.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.8  Setting the wave forms of the envelopes")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("R13	    |  x     x	   x	 x  | B3  | B2	| B1  | B0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    ------------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    V")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |    :\				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   0	 0    x    x   |  __:  \______________________	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |      /:			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   0	 1    x    x   |  __/  :______________________	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |    :\	:\  :\	:\  :\	:\  :\	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 0    0    0   |  __:  \:  \:  \:  \:  \:  \:_	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |    :\				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 0    0    1   |  __:  \______________________	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |    :\	   / \	   / \	   / \	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 0    1    0   |  __:  \ /     \ /     \ /	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |	 _____________________	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |    :\	:			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 0    1    1   |  __:  \:			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |      /:  /:  /:  /:  /:  /:	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 1    0    0   |  __/  :/  :/  :/  :/  :/  :/	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |	______________________	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |      / 			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 1    0    1   |  __/				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |      / \     / \     / \	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 1    1    0   |  __/	  \ /	  \ /	  \ /	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |      /:			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   1	 1    1    1   |  __/  :______________________	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			   |   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			   +---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("			     T")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* I/O port (R14, R15)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("R14 and R15 are the ports to send and receive 8-bit data in parallel. MSX ")
  ManualsHelp_L("uses these as the general-purpose I/O interface. For more information, see ")
  ManualsHelp_L("section 5.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.2 Access to the PSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("For access the PSG from assembly language programs, several BIOS routines ")
  ManualsHelp_L("described below are available.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* GICINI (0090H/MAIN) .................. PSG initialization")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	initializes PSG registers and does the initial settings of")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the work area in which PLAY statement of BASIC is executed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Each register of PSG is set to the value as shown in")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Figure 5.9.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.9  Initial values of PSG registers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			Bit |	  |	|     |     |	  |	|     |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			    |  7  |  6	|  5  |  4  |  3  |  2	|  1  |  0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Register		    |	  |	|     |     |	  |	|     |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R0    | Channel A	    |  0     1	   0	 1     0     1	   0	 1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------|		    |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R1    | frequency	    |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R2    | Channel B	    |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------|		    |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R3    | frequency	    |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R4    | Channel C	    |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------|		    |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R5    | frequency	    |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R6    | Noise frequency|  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R7    | Channel setting|  1     0	   1	 1     1     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R8    | Chan. A volume |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R9    | Chan. B volume |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R10   | Chan. C volume |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R11   |		    |  0     0	   0	 0     1     0	   1	 1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------| Envelope Cycle |-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R12   |		    |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R13   | Env. pattern   |  0     0	   0	 0     0     0	   0	 0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R14   | I/O port A     |						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|----------+----------------+-----------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    R15   | I/O port B     |						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* WRTPSG (0093H/MAIN) ................. writing data in PSG registers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- PSG register number")
  ManualsHelp_L("		E <-- data to be written")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	writes the contents of the E register in the PSG register")
  ManualsHelp_L("		whose number is specified by the A register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RDPSG (0096H/MAIN) .................. reading PSG register data")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- PSG register number")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- contents of the specified register")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	reads the contents of PSG register whose number is specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("		by the A register and stores the value in the A register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* STRTMS (0099H/MAIN) ................. starting the music")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		(QUEUE) <-- MML which is translated into the intermediate")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    language")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	examines whether the music is played as the background task,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		and plays the music which is set in the queue, if the music")
  ManualsHelp_L("		has not yet been played.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.1  Single tone generation")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";   List 5.1   440 Hz tone")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTPSG	EQU	0093H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0B000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,7		;Select Channel")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,00111110B	;Channel A Tone := On")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTPSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,8		;Set Volume")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,10")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTPSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,0		;Set Fine Tune Channel A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,0FEH		;Data 0FEH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTPSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,1		;Set Coarse Tune Channel A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,0		;Data 0H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTPSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.3 Tone Generation by 1-bit Sound Port")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX has another sound generator in addition to the PSG. This is a simple one ")
  ManualsHelp_L("that generates sound by turning ON/OFF the 1-bit I/O port output repeatedly ")
  ManualsHelp_L("using software.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.10	1-bit sound port")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		bit    7    6	 5    4    3	2    1	  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     | .  |    |    |	 |    |    |	|    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     --+--------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |    PPI port C (I/O address 0AAH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("::::::::::::	       V")
  ManualsHelp_L(":   PSG    :	   ---------")
  ManualsHelp_L(":  output  :::::::>|  MIX  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("::::::::::::	   ---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       V")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    /	  \   Speaker")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   ---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     / : \")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1.4 Access to 1-bit Sound Port")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To access to the 1-bit sound port, the following BIOS routine is offered.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CHGSND (0135H/MAIN)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- specification of ON/OFF (0 = OFF, others = ON)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output:")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	calling this routine with setting 0 in the A register turns")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the bit of the sound port OFF; calling it with another value")
  ManualsHelp_L("		turns it ON.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.2  Reading from cassette tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.2   Read from cassette tape")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	     Set music tape into tape-recorder")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	     and run this program.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	     Then your MSX will replay it.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGSNG	EQU	0135H")
  ManualsHelp_L("STMOTR	EQU	00F3H")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDPSG	EQU	0096H")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX	EQU	00B7H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0B000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----	Note:  Play tape using 1-bit sound port.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("START:	LD	A,1		;motor on")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	STMOTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LBL01:	LD	A,14		;register 14")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	RDPSG		;read PSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	80H		;check CSAR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHGSNG		;change SOUND PORT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	BREAKX		;check Ctrl-STOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,LBL01")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A		;stop cassette motor")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	STMOTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2. CASSETTE INTERFACE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Cassette tape recorders are the least expensive external storage devices ")
  ManualsHelp_L("available for the MSX. Knowledge of the cassette interface is required to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("treat information in cassette tapes within assembly language programs. This ")
  ManualsHelp_L("section offers the necessary information.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.1 Baud Rate")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The following two baud rates can be used by the MSX cassette interface (see ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Table 5.2). When BASIC is invoked, 1200bps is set by default.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 5.2  MSX baud rate")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  Baud rate  |        Characteristics	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  1200 bps   |  Low speed / high reliability  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  2400 bps   |  High speed / low reliability  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The baud rate is specified by the fourth parameter of the SCREEN instruction ")
  ManualsHelp_L("or the second parameter of the CSAVE instruction. Once the baud rate is set, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("it stays at that value.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SCREEN		,,,<baud rate>")
  ManualsHelp_L("CSAVE		" + Chr(34) + "filename" + Chr(34) + ",<baud rate>")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(<baud rate> is 1 for 1200bps, 2 for 2400 bps)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.2 One bit composition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("One bit data, the basis of I/O, is recorded as shown in Figure 5.11. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("pulse width is determined by counting the T-STATE of the CPU, so, while the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cassette interface is active, any interrupt is inhibited.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The bit data from the cassette can be read through the seventh bit of port B ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of the general-purpose I/O interface (register 15 of the PSG). This function ")
  ManualsHelp_L("was used in the program example of List 5.3, section 1 of chapter 5.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.11	One bit composition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| Baud rate |  Bit  |		     Wave form		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-------+----------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	    |  :	 -----------		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	0   |  :	 |	   |   (1200Hz x 1)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    1200   |	    |  :_________|	   |		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |-------+--:-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    baud   |	    |  :    ------    ------		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	1   |  :    |	 |    |    |   (2400Hz x 2)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	    |  :____|	 |____|    |		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-------+--:-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	    |  :    ------	   :		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	0   |  :    |	 |	   :   (2400Hz x 1)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    2400   |	    |  :____|	 |	   :		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |-------+--:-------------------:-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    baud   |	    |  :  ---  ---	   :		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	1   |  :  | |  | |	   :   (4800Hz x 2)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |	    |  :__| |__| |	   :		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------:--:-:----:---------:------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |  : :	 :	   |  2963 T-states (833 micro-sec)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       +--:-:----:---------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |  : :	 |  1491 T-states (417 micro-sec)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       +--:-:----+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |  : |  746 T-states (208 micro-sec)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       +--:-+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |  |  373 T-states (104 micro-sec)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       +--+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.3 One byte composition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("One byte data is recorded in the array of bits as shown in Figure 5.12. There ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is one " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " bit as the start bit, followed by the 8-bit data body from LSB to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX and by two " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " bit as the stop bits, so 11 bits are used.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.12	One byte composition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	     LSB				       MSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	0  |  X  |  X  |  X  |	X  |  X  |  X  |  X  |	X  |  1  :  1  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	   |						   |	       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +-----+-----------------------------------------------+-----------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("    Start bit			  Data			      Stop bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.4 Header Composition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The header is the portion where the signal of the specific frequency is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("recorded on the tape for a certain period. This allows the cassette tape ")
  ManualsHelp_L("speed to stabilize after it is started, or divides two files. There is a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("long header and a short header. The long header is used to wait until the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("motor is stabilized. The baud rate at reading the tape is determined by ")
  ManualsHelp_L("reading the long header. The short header is used to divide file bodies. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Table 5.3 shows the compositions of both.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 5.3  Header composition")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  Baud rate  |    Header    |	      Header composition	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------+-----------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | Long header  |	2400 Hz x 16000 (about 6.7 sec)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  1200 baud  |--------------+-----------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | Short header |	2400 Hz x  4000 (about 1.7 sec)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------+-----------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | Long header  |	4800 Hz x 32000 (about 6.7 sec)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  2400 baud  |--------------+-----------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | Short header |	4800 Hz x  8000 (about 1.7 sec)  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.5 File Formats")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX BASIC supports the following three kinds of cassette format files.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1) BASIC text file")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC programs saved with the CSAVE command are recorded in this format. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("file is divided into the preceding file header and the succeeding the body.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.13	Binary file format")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  6.7 sec		 10 bytes		  6 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		     |				    |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Long header  |		0D3H x 10	    |	 File name     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		     |				    |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |								       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +----------+		  +------------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		|   File header   |  |	      File body 	|	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("				     |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +-------------------------------+				+------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |								       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------\  \--------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Short	|		       /  /	 |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	header	|     BASIC program    \  \	 |	 00H x 7       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		|		       /  /	 |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------\  \--------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("       1.7 sec		   Any length			 7 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In the file header, ten bytes each of the value 0D3H follow after the long ")
  ManualsHelp_L("header and six bytes containing the file name are placed after them. In the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("file body, program body follows the short header and the end of the file is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("indicated by seven bytes of 00H.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2) ASCII text file")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC programs saved in ASCII format by the SAVE command and data files ")
  ManualsHelp_L("created by the OPEN command are recorded in this format.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.14	ASCII file format")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  6.7 sec		 10 bytes		  6 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		     |				    |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Long header  |		0EAH x 10	    |	 File name     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		     |				    |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |								       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +----------+		  +------------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		|   File header   |  |	      File body 	|	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("				     |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +-------------------------------+				+------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |								       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -----------------------------------------------\  \----------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		 |	     |		 |	 /  /	   |   Last    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Block 1  |  Block 2  |	Block 3  | ..... \  \ .... |   block   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		 |	     |		 |	 /  /	   |	 .     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -----------------------------------------------\  \------------+---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 |	     |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +-----------+	     +-----------+		    CTRL+Z (EOF)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |					 |		is included in data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  ------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Short	|			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	header	|	   Data 	 | .....")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		|			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  ------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	1.7 sec 	256 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(3) Machine code file")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Machine code files saved by the BSAVE command are recorded in the following ")
  ManualsHelp_L("format. In the file header, 10 bytes each of the value 0D0H follow after the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("long header and 6 bytes containing the file name are placed after them.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In the file body, the starting address, the end address, and the entry ")
  ManualsHelp_L("address are recorded in order after the short header, and the machine codes ")
  ManualsHelp_L("follow after them. Since the amount of data can be calculated from the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("starting and ending addresses, there is no special mark for the end of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("file. The entry address is the address where the program is executed when the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("R option of the BLOAD command is used.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.15	Machine code file format")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  6.7 sec		 10 bytes		  6 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		     |				    |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Long header  |		0D0H x 10	    |	 File name     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		     |				    |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |								       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +----------+		  +------------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		|   File header   |  |	      File body 	|	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("				     |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +-------------------------------+				+------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |								       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	Short	|   Top    |   End    | Starting |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	header	| address  | address  | address  |    Program body     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |		|	   |	      | 	 |		       |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  -------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("       1.7 sec	  2 bytes    2 bytes	2 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2.6 Access to cassette files")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The following BIOS routines are offered to access cassette files.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TAPION (00E1H/MAIN) ................. OPEN for read")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	CY flag = ON at abnormal terminations")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	starts the motor of the tape recorder and reads the long")
  ManualsHelp_L("		header or the short headet. At the same time, the baud rate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		in which the file is recorded is detected and the work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is set according to it. Interrupts are inhibited.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TAPIN (00E4H/MAIN) .................. read one byte")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- data which has been read")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CY flag = ON at abnormal terminations")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	reads one byte of data from the tape and stores it in the A")
  ManualsHelp_L("		register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TAPIOF (00E7H/MAIN) ................. CLOSE for read")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	ends reading from the tape. At this point, interrupts are")
  ManualsHelp_L("		allowed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TAPOON (00EAH/MAIN) ................. OPEN for write")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- type of header (0 = short header, others = long header)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	CY flag = ON at abnormal terminations")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	starts the motor of the tape recorder and writes the header")
  ManualsHelp_L("		of the type specified in the A register to the tape.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Interrupts are inhibited.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TAPOUT (00EDH/MAIN) ................. write one byte")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- data to be written")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	CY flag = ON at abnormal terminations")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	writes the contents of the A register to the tape.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TAPOOF (00F0H/MAIN) ................. CLOSE writing")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	ends writing the tape. At this point, interrupts are allowed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* STMOTR (00F3/MAIN) .................. specify the actions of the motor")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- action (0 = stop, 1 = start, 255 = reverse the current")
  ManualsHelp_L("							 status)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	sets the status of the motor according to the value specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("		in the A register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When READ/WRITE routines for the cassette files are created using these BIOS ")
  ManualsHelp_L("calls, only READ or WRITE, without any other action, should be done. For ")
  ManualsHelp_L("example, reading data from the tape and displaying it on the CRT might cause ")
  ManualsHelp_L("a READ error.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.3 is a sample program which uses BIOS routines.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.3  Listing names of files saved in the cassette")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.3	 Cassette files")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Set cassette tape into recorder and run this program.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Then all the names and attributes of the programs")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	in that tape will be listed.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHPUT	EQU	00A2H")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPION	EQU	00E1H")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPIN	EQU	00E4H")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPIOF	EQU	00E7H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0C000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----	Note:  View program names on cassette tape.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("START:	CALL	TAPION		;motor on and read header")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,16")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,WORK 	;work area address")
  ManualsHelp_L("LBL01:	PUSH	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	TAPIN		;read a byte of data from tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,ERROR 	;set carry flag if read error")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(HL),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DJNZ	LBL01")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,FILNAM	;write file name")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,WORK+10")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CRLF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WORK)	;check file attributes")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,BINFIL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	0D3H		;check binary file")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,LBL03")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,ASCFIL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	0EAH		;check ascii file")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,LBL03")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,MACFIL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	0D0H		;check machine code file")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,LBL03")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ERROR:	LD	HL,ERRSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LBL03:	CALL	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	TAPIOF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- put CRLF -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CRLF:	LD	HL,STCRLF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- put string -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUTSTR: LD	A,(HL)		;get a character from strings")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	'$'             ;check end of strings")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	Z")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHPUT		;write a character to CRT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- strings data -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FILNAM: DB	'FILE NAME :$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("ASCFIL: DB	'ASCII FILE',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("BINFIL: DB	'BINARY FILE',0DH,0Ah,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("MACFIL: DB	'BSAVE FILE',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("ERRSTR: DB	'TAPE READ ERROR',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("STCRLF: DB	0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- WORK AREA -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WORK:	DS	16,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'$'             ;end of strings")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=========================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3. KEYBOARD INTERFACE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Altough the MSX2 keyboard has the same design as that of the MSX1, it is more ")
  ManualsHelp_L("convenient to use because of the Romand-to-kana translation available for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("kana input. This chapter describes the keyboard interface of the MSX2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Descriptions of the key aarangement are based on the Japanese keyboard ")
  ManualsHelp_L("standard; note that data is slightly different for the international MSX ")
  ManualsHelp_L("versions.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3.1 Key Scanning")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX uses the key matrices as shown in Figure 5.16, Figure 5.17 and Figure ")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.17B. The key status can be obtained in real time by examining this key ")
  ManualsHelp_L("matrix and is available for reading input.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Scanning the key matrix is done by the following BIOS routine.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* SNSMAT (0141H/MAIN) ................. reads the specified line of the")
  ManualsHelp_L("					key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- key matrix line to be read (0 to 10)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- status of the specified line of the key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      (when pressed, the bit of the key is 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	specifies a line of the key matrix shown in Figure 5.16,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Figure 5.17 or Figure 5.17B and stores its status in the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A register. The bit corresponding with the key being pressed")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ", and " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " for the key not being pressed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.16	MSX USA version key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSB								       LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	7	6	5	4	3	2	1	0")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 0  |	B   |	L   |	    |	/   |	1   |	S   |	X   |	,   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 1  |	V   |	J   |	=   |	`   |	Q   |	A   |	C   |	N   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 2  |	G   |	8   |	0   |	]   |	W   |	F   |	Z   |	M   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 3  |	T   |	I   |	~   |	;   |	2   |	D   |	U   |	\   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 4  |	6   |	K   |	P   |	'   |   3   |   R   |   7   |   H   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 5  |	5   |	0   |	9   |	[   |	4   |	E   |	Y   |	.   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 6  |	F3  |	F2  |	F1  | CODE  | CAPS  | GRAPH | CTRL  | SHIFT |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 7  | RETURN| SELECT|	BS  | STOP  |  TAB  |  ESC  |	F5  |	F4  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 8  | RIGHT | DOWN  |	UP  | LEFT  |  DEL  |  INS  | HOME  | SPACE |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    [TEN KEY]")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 9  |	4   |	3   |	2   |	1   |	0   | option| option| option|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("10  |	.   |	,   |	-   |	9   |	8   |	7   |	6   |	5   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.17	MSX International version key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSB								       LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	7	6	5	4	3	2	1	0")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 0  |	B   |	L   |deadkey|	/   |	1   |	S   |	X   |	,   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 1  |	V   |	J   |	^   |	]   |	Q   |	A   |	C   |	N   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 2  |	G   |	8   |	0   |	[   |	W   |	F   |	Z   |	M   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 3  |	T   |	I   |	~   |	;   |	2   |	D   |	U   |	\   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 4  |	6   |	K   |	P   |	:   |	3   |	R   |	7   |	H   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 5  |	5   |	0   |	9   |	@   |	4   |	E   |	Y   |	.   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 6  |	F3  |	F2  |	F1  | CODE  | CAPS  | GRAPH | CTRL  | SHIFT |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 7  | RETURN| SELECT|	BS  | STOP  |  TAB  |  ESC  |	F5  |	F4  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 8  | RIGHT | DOWN  |	UP  | LEFT  |  DEL  |  INS  | HOME  | SPACE |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    [TEN KEY]")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 9  |	4   |	3   |	2   |	1   |	0   | option| option| option|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("10  |	.   |	,   |	-   |	9   |	8   |	7   |	6   |	5   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.17B  MSX European version key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSB								       LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	7	6	5	4	3	2	1	0")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 0  |	7   |	6   |	5   |	4   |	3   |	2   |	1   |	0   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 1  |	;   |	]   |	[   |	\   |	=   |	-   |	9   |	8   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 2  |	B   |	A   | accent|	/   |	.   |	,   |	`   |	'   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 3  |	J   |	I   |	H   |	G   |	F   |	E   |	D   |	C   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 4  |	R   |	Q   |	P   |	O   |	N   |	M   |	L   |	K   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 5  |	Z   |	Y   |	X   |	W   |	V   |	U   |	T   |	S   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 6  |	F3  |	F2  |	F1  | CODE  | CAPS  | GRAPH | CTRL  | SHIFT |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 7  | RETURN| SELECT|	BS  | STOP  |  TAB  |  ESC  |	F5  |	F4  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 8  | RIGHT | DOWN  |	UP  | LEFT  |  DEL  |  INS  | HOME  | SPACE |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    [TEN KEY]")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 9  |	4   |	3   |	2   |	1   |	0   | option| option| option|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("10  |	.   |	,   |	-   |	9   |	8   |	7   |	6   |	5   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.4  Use of the key scanning routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.4   scan key-matrix and display it")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHPUT	EQU	00A2H")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX	EQU	00B7H")
  ManualsHelp_L("POSIT	EQU	00C6H")
  ManualsHelp_L("SNSMAT	EQU	0141H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0B000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----	Note:  read key matrix and display key")
  ManualsHelp_L("				       pattern.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SCAN:	LD	C,0		;C := line of key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SC1:	LD	A,C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	SNSMAT		;Read key matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,8")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,BUF		;HL : = buffer address")
  ManualsHelp_L("SC2:	LD	D,'.'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLA			;Check bit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,SC3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,'#'")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SC3:	LD	(HL),D		;store '.' or '#' to buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DJNZ	SC2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,05H		;x := 5")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,C		;y := C+1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	POSIT		;set cursor position")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,8		;put out bit patterns to CRT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,BUF")
  ManualsHelp_L("SC4:	LD	A,(HL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHPUT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DJNZ	SC4")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	BREAKX		;check Ctrl-STOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C		;line No. increment")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	09")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,SC1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	SCAN")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- work area -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BUF:	DS	8")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3.2 Character Input")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX scans the key matrix every 1/60 second using the timer interrupt and, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("when a key is pressed, stores the character code in the keyboard buffer as ")
  ManualsHelp_L("shown in Figure 5.18. Key input to MSX is generally done by reading this ")
  ManualsHelp_L("keyboard buffer.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.18	Keyboard ring buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("+----------------------------------<----------------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      KEYBUF (FBF0H, 40)			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("| --------------------------------------/ /-------------------------------- |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+>|  D	|  E  |  F  |  G  |	|     | \ \ |	  |	|  A  |  B  |  C  |-+")
  ManualsHelp_L("  --------------------------------------/ /--------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			     ^				   ^")
  ManualsHelp_L("			     |				   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  [PUTPNT]			[GETPNT]")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GETPNT (F3FAH, 2) points to the next character to be obtained in CHGET ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routine.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUTPNT (F3F8H, 2) points to the next location for the character to be put ")
  ManualsHelp_L("when the keyboard is pressed next time.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BIOS routines having functions for key input using this keyboard buffer and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("functions related to it are described below. Inhibiting the timer interrupt ")
  ManualsHelp_L("renders them useless, of course.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CHSNS (009CH/MAIN) .................. checks the keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	Z flag = ON when the buffer is empty")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	examines whether any characters remain in the keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("		and sets the Z flag when the buffer is empty.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CHGET (009FH/MAIN) .................. one character input from the keyboard")
  ManualsHelp_L("					buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	reads one character from the keyboard buffer and stores it in")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the A register. When the buffer is empty, it displays the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		cursor and waits for a key input. While a key input is waited")
  ManualsHelp_L("		for, the CAP lock, KANA lock, and Roman-to-kana translation")
  ManualsHelp_L("		lock are valid. The related work area is listed below. In the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		list, since SCNCNT and REPCNT are initialised after the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		execution of CHGET routine, this area should be set at each")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CHGET call to change the interval of the auto-repeat.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CLIKSW (F3DBH, 1)	key click sound (0 = OFF, others = ON)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SCNCNT (F3F6H, 1)	key scanning interval (1, normally)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	REPCNT (F3F7H, 1)	delay until beginning auto-repeat")
  ManualsHelp_L("				(50, normally)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CSTYLE (FCAAH, 1)	figure of the cursor")
  ManualsHelp_L("				(0 = block, others = underline)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CAPST  (FCABH, 1)	CAPS lock (0 = OFF, others = ON)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DEADST (FCACH, 1)	dead key lock")
  ManualsHelp_L("					0 = on preceding dead key")
  ManualsHelp_L("					1 = dead key")
  ManualsHelp_L("					2 = shifted dead key")
  ManualsHelp_L("					3 = code dead key")
  ManualsHelp_L("					4 = code shift dead key")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* KILBUF (0156H/MAIN) ................. empty the keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	empties the keyboard buffer.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.5  Use of one character input routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";   List 5.5	get key code")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		this routine doesn't wait for key hit")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHSNS	EQU	009CH		;check keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGET	EQU	009FH		;get a character from buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHPUT	EQU	00A2H		;put a character to screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX	EQU	00B7H		;check Ctrl-STOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("KILBUF	EQU	0156H		;clear keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("REPCNT	EQU	0F3F7H		;time interval until key-repeat")
  ManualsHelp_L("KEYBUF	EQU	0FBF0H		;keyboard buffer address")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0B000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- prgram start -----	Note:  Real-time input using CHGET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KEY:	CALL	CHSNS		;check keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,KEY1")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(REPCNT),A	;not to wait until repeat")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHGET		;get a character (if exists)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	KEY2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KEY1:	LD	A,'-'           ;A := '-'")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KEY2:	CALL	CHPUT		;put the character")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	KILBUF		;clear keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	BREAKX		;check Ctrl-STOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,KEY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CNVRCHR (00AB/MAIN) ................. graphic character operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- translated graphic character")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      (normal characters are not translated)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CY flag = OFF (input was the graphic header byte 01H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CY flag = ON, Z flag = ON  (input was the graphic character")
  ManualsHelp_L("					    and was translated)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CY flag = ON, Z flag = OFF (input was the normal character")
  ManualsHelp_L("					    and was not translated)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	executing CNVCHR after CHGET causes the graphic character")
  ManualsHelp_L("		to be translated to one byte code as shown in Figure 5.19")
  ManualsHelp_L("		and causes other character not to be translated and to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("		returned. Since the graphic character is represented by")
  ManualsHelp_L("		irregular 2-byte code with the graphic header byte (01H),")
  ManualsHelp_L("		annoying procedures are required for the character")
  ManualsHelp_L("		operations; this routine makes it somewhat easy.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.19	Graphic character translation chart")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    Before    |    After     |    Before    |	  After     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  conversion  |  conversion  |  conversion  |	conversion  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------------------+-----------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			      |    0150H    -->     50H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0141H    -->     41H     |    0151H    -->     51H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0142H    -->     42H     |    0152H    -->     52H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0143H    -->     43H     |    0153H    -->     53H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0144H    -->     44H     |    0154H    -->     54H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0145H    -->     45H     |    0155H    -->     55H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0146H    -->     46H     |    0156H    -->     56H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0147H    -->     47H     |    0157H    -->     57H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0148H    -->     48H     |    0158H    -->     58H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    0149H    -->     49H     |    0159H    -->     59H     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    014AH    -->     4AH     |    015AH    -->     5AH     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    014BH    -->     4BH     |    015BH    -->     5BH     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    014CH    -->     4CH     |    015CH    -->     5CH     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    014DH    -->     4DH     |    015DH    -->     5DH     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    014EH    -->     4EH     |    015EH    -->     5EH     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    014FH    -->     4FH     |    015FH    -->     5FH     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* PINLIN (00AEH/MAIN) ................. one line input")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	HL <-- F55DH")
  ManualsHelp_L("		[F55EH] <-- input string (the end of te line is represented")
  ManualsHelp_L("					  by 00H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CY flag <-- terminated by STOP=ON, terminated by RETURN=OFF")
  ManualsHelp_L("function:	stores input string in the line buffer BUF (F55EH). All")
  ManualsHelp_L("		functions of the screen editing are available at the string")
  ManualsHelp_L("		input. Pressing RETURN or STOP causes the input to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("		finished. The work area is listed below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("	BUF    (F55EH, 258)	the line buffer where the string is stored")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LINTTB (FBB2H, 24)	00H when the one physiscal line is the")
  ManualsHelp_L("				succession of the line above")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* INLIN (00B1H/MAIN) .................. one line input (prompt available)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	same as PINLIN")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	stores input string in the line buffer BUF (F55EH), as")
  ManualsHelp_L("		PINLIN routine. Note that the portion before the cursor")
  ManualsHelp_L("		location at the time when the routine begins to execute is")
  ManualsHelp_L("		not received. List 5.6 shows the difference between PINLIN")
  ManualsHelp_L("		and INLIN.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.6  Difference between INLIN and PINLIN")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.6   INLIN and PINLIN")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHPUT	EQU	00A2H")
  ManualsHelp_L("INLIN	EQU	00B1H")
  ManualsHelp_L("PINLIN	EQU	00AEH")
  ManualsHelp_L("KILBUF	EQU	0156H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BUF	EQU	F55EH")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0B000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,PRMPT1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTMSG		;put prompt message")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	INLIN		;use INLIN routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,BUF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTMSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,PRMPT2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTMSG		;put prompt message")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PINLIN		;use PINLIN routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,BUF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTMSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- put a string -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUTMSG: LD	A,(HL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	Z")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHPUT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	PUTMSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- string data -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMPT1: DB	0DH,0AH,'INLIN:$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMPT2: DB	0DH,0AH,'PINLIN:$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3.3 Function Keys")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX has ten function keys, which can be defined by the user at will. A 16 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("byte work area is allocated for the definition of each key. The following ")
  ManualsHelp_L("list shows their addresses.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	FNKSTR (F87FH, 16) ............ F1 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 10H  (F88FH, 16) ............ F2 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 20H  (F89FH, 16) ............ F3 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 30H  (F8AFH, 16) ............ F4 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 40H  (F8BFH, 16) ............ F5 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 50H  (F8CFH, 16) ............ F6 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 60H  (F8DFH, 16) ............ F7 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 70H  (F8EFH, 16) ............ F8 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 80H  (F8FFH, 16) ............ F9 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	+ 90H  (F90FH, 16) ............ F10 key definition address")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Pressing a function key causes the string defined in that key to be stored in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("[KEYBUF]. The end of the string is indicated by 00H and a maximum of 15 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("keystrokes can be defined for one function key (definitions longer than 16 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("keystrokes are defined over more than one function key definition area). To ")
  ManualsHelp_L("restore the initial settings of the function keys, use the following BIOS ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routine.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* INIFNK (003EH/MAIN) ................. initialize function keys")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	restores the function key definition to the setting when")
  ManualsHelp_L("		BASIC starts.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3.4 STOP Key During Interrupts")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGET, the one-character input routine described in 3.3, determines the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("pressed key in the timer interrupt routine. Thus, when the timer interrupt is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("inhibited, such as during cassette data I/O, pressed keys cannot be detected. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("By using the BIOS routine described below, the CTRL key + STOP key ")
  ManualsHelp_L("combination can be detected even when interrupts are inhibited.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BREAKX (00B7H/MAIN) ................. CTRL + STOP detection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	CY flag = ON, when CTRL + STOP is pressed")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	scans keys and decides whether CTRL key and STOP key are")
  ManualsHelp_L("		pressed at the same time. When both are pressed, this routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("		sets " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " to the CY flag and returns. Otherwise, it resets " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("		to the CY flag and returns. This routine is available while")
  ManualsHelp_L("		interrupts are inhibited.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("4. PRINTER INTERFACE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This section describes how to access the MSX printer interface from assembly ")
  ManualsHelp_L("language. The information described here is helpful if the printer is going ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to be used to print bit image graphics.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("4.1 Print Interface Overview")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The printer interface is supported by BIOS and BASIC. MSX drives the printer ")
  ManualsHelp_L("through an 8-bit parallel output port and uses a handshaking method with BUSY ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and STROBE signals. The standard connector is also defined (Amphenol 14-pin, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("female side to the machine). Figure 5.20 shows the signal lines.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.20	Printer interface")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 Printer interface pin connections")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" \	    ------------------------------------------- 	 /")
  ManualsHelp_L("  \	    | (7) | (6) | (5) | (4) | (3) | (2) | (1) | 	/")
  ManualsHelp_L("   \	---------------------------------------------------    /")
  ManualsHelp_L("    \	|						  |   /")
  ManualsHelp_L("     \	---------------------------------------------------  /")
  ManualsHelp_L("      \     | (14)| (13)| (12)| (11)| (11)| (10)| (9) |     /")
  ManualsHelp_L("       \    -------------------------------------------    /")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1) ........... STROBE*")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2) to (9) .... Data (b0 to b7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("(11) .......... BUSY")
  ManualsHelp_L("(14) .......... BGND")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("I/O port (91H)		    |  X  |  X	|  X  |  X  |  X  |  X	|  X  |  X  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("						   Data")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("I/O port (90H; at WRITE)    |  .  |  .	|  .  |  .  |  .  |  .	|  .  |  X  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("									 ^")
  ManualsHelp_L("									 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("					STROBE* (send data when " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ") ----+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("I/O port (90H; at READ)     |  .  |  .	|  .  |  .  |  .  |  .	|  X  |  .  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("								   ^")
  ManualsHelp_L("					       0: Printer READY    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("								---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("					       1: Printer BUSY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("4.2 Output to the MSX Standard Printer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("If data is sent from MSX to the printer, the action depends on whether the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("printer receiving the data is of the MSX standard. The use of MSX standard ")
  ManualsHelp_L("printers is described in this section. Descriptions about other printers are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in the next section.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("An MSX standard printer can print any character that can be displayed on the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("screen. Special graphic characters corresponding to character codes n = 01H ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to 1FH can be also printed by sending the code 40H + n after the graphic ")
  ManualsHelp_L("character header (01H). In addition to these, the control codes shown in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Table 5.4 can be used with MSX standard printers (see the manual of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("printer for controlling a printer which has other functions such as printing ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Chinese characters).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To feed lines in MSX standard printers, send 0DH and 0AH successively. To ")
  ManualsHelp_L("print the bit image, send nnnn bytes data, where nnnn means four decimal ")
  ManualsHelp_L("figures, after the escape sequence ESC + " + Chr(34) + "Snnnn" + Chr(34) + ". Note that, MSX has a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("function to transform the tab code (09H) to the adequate number of space ")
  ManualsHelp_L("codes (20H) for printers not having a tab function. This transformation is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("normally done. To print a bit image which includes the value 09H correctly, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("change the following work area.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RAWPRT (F418H, 1) ................... replaces a tab by spaces when the")
  ManualsHelp_L("					contents are 00H, othereise not.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 5.4  Control codes of the printer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      code	  |			   function			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------+---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| 0AH		  |  line feed						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------+---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| 0CH		  |  form feed						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------+---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| 0DH		  |  carriage return					    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------+---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| ESC + " + Chr(34) + "A" + Chr(34) + "       |  normal line spacing                                    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		  |  (spaces between lines; characters are read easily)     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------+---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("| ESC + " + Chr(34) + "B" + Chr(34) + "       |  line spacing for graphics (no space between lines)     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------------+---------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  ESC + " + Chr(34) + "Snnnn" + Chr(34) + "  |  bit image printing                                     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("4.3 Access to the printer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To send output to the printer, the following BIOS routines are offered.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* LPTOUT (00A5H/MAIN)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A register <-- character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	CY flag = ON at abnormal termination")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	sends a character specified by the A register to the printer.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* LPTSTT (00A8/MAIN)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A register <-- printer status")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	examines the current printer status. After calling this")
  ManualsHelp_L("		routine, the printer can be used when the A register is 255")
  ManualsHelp_L("		and the Z flag is 0; when the A register is 0 and the Z flag")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is 1, the printer cannot be used.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* OUTDLP (014DH,MAIN)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A register <-- character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	CY flag = ON at abnormal termination")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	sends a character specified by the A register to the printer.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Differences between this routine and LPTOUT routine is as")
  ManualsHelp_L("		following:")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* prints corresponding number of spaces for TAB code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* transforms hiragana to katakana for printers other than")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  MSX standard")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* returns Device I/O error at abnormal termination")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("5. UNIVERSAL I/O INTERFACE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("As described in section 1, the PSG used by MSX has two 8-bit I/O ports, port ")
  ManualsHelp_L("A and port B, in addition to the sound output function. In MSX, these two ")
  ManualsHelp_L("ports are connected to the universal I/O interface (joystick port) and are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("used to exchange data with the joystick or the paddle (see Figure 5.21). ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Various devices to be connected to this universal I/O interface have the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("necessary BIOS routine in ROM, so they are easily accessbile.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In this section, the funtion of each I/O device and the method for accessing ")
  ManualsHelp_L("with BIOS routines are described.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.21	Universal I/O interface")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Universal input/output interface -1")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  (1)	   (2)	   (3)	   (4)	   (5) -+- +5V	       Switching signal <---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   |  (6)  |  (7)  |  (8)  |  (9) -----+- GND		(to port B:b6)	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   |	|   |	|   |	|   |		|				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----:---:---:---:---:---:---:------------				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	|   |	|   |	|   |						    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	|   |	|   |	+---:--> To port B:b4	 -------------------------  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	|   |	|   |	    |			 |			 |  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    +---+---+---+---+-------+--------------------|			 |  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("						 |	 Switcher	 |--+")
  ManualsHelp_L("    +---+---+---+---+-------+--------------------|			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	|   |	|   |	    |			 |			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	|   |	|   |	+---:--> To port B:b5	 -------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	|   |	|   |	|   |			   |   |   |   |   |   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----:---:---:---:---:---:---:------------	  (1) (2) (3) (4) (6) (7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   |	|   |	|   |	|   |		|	|  |   |   |   |   |   |  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  (1)	   (2)	   (3)	   (4)	   (5) -+- +5V	+-------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      (6)     (7)     (8)     (9) -----+- GND		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|					|		     V")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------	     To port A:b0 to b5")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Universal input/output interface -2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.1 Functions of the Ports")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Two I/O ports of PSG are used as shown in Figure 5.22.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.22 (A)  Functions of PSG port A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Port A (PSG#14)")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| b7  |  .  | b5  : b4	: b3  : b2  : b1  : b0	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       |     |	   |	 |     |     |		       --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       |     |	   |	 |     |     +--> 1st terminal	 | connected")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       |     |	   |	 |     +--------> 2nd terminal	 |    to")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       |     |	   |	 +--------------> 3rd terminal	 | universal")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       |     |	   +--------------------> 4th terminal	 |    I/O")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       |     +--------------------------> 6th terminal	 | interface")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       +--------------------------------> 7th terminal	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |							       --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("   +-----------------------------------> Data input from the cassette tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.22 (B)  Functions of PSG port B")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Port B (PSG#15)")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| b7  | b6  | b5  | b4	| b3  | b2  | b1  | b0	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |     |     |	   |	 |     |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |     |     |	   +-----+-----+-----+--> Unused")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |     |     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |     |     +---> Connected to 8th terminal of univ. I/O interface 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |     +---------> Connected to 8th terminal of univ. I/O interface 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 +---> 0: b0-b5 of port A to be connected to univ. I/O interface 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	       1: b0-b5 of port A to be connected to univ. I/O interface 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   +---------> 0: Arabic or kana mode display lamp on")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       1: Arabic or kana mode display lamp off")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.2 Joystick Use")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure 5.23 shows the joystick circuit. As the circuit shows, sending " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the 8th terminal and reading the 1st to 4th and 6th to 7th terminals enable ")
  ManualsHelp_L("information about the stick and the trigger buttons to be obtained. However, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("it is advisable to use BIOS for accessing the joystick, in order to give ")
  ManualsHelp_L("portability to the program.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   figure 5.23	Joystick circuit")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  \")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1)	O---------------o  o------------+ ............. Front")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  \		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2)	O---------------o  o------------+ ............. Back")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  \		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("(3)	O---------------o  o------------+ ............. Left")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  \		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("(4)	O---------------o  o------------+ ............. Right")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  \		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("(6)	O---------------o  o------------+ ............. Trigger A")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			  \		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("(7)	O---------------o  o------------+ ............. Trigger B")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("(8)	O-------------------------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The following BIOS routines are offered for accessing the joystick. These ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routines have similar functions to the STICK function and STRIG function of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC. The status of the cursor keys or the space bar, in addition to the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("joystick, can be read in real time.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* GTSTCK (00D5H/MAIN) ................. read joystick")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- joystick number (0 = cursor key, 1 and 2 = joystick)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- direction of joystick or cursor key")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	returns the current status of the joystick or the cursor keys")
  ManualsHelp_L("		in the A register. The value is the same as the STICK")
  ManualsHelp_L("		function in BASIC.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* GTTRIG (00D8H/MAIN) ................. read trigger button")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- trigger button number (0 = space bar,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      1 and 2 = trigger button A, 3 and 4 = trigger button B)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- status of trigger button or space bar")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      (0FFH = pressed, 00H = released)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	returns the current status of the trigger buttons or the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		space bar in the A register. The value is 0FFH when the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		trigger is pressed, otherwise it is 0.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.7  Joystick use")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("; List 5.7  Joystick and trigger access")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHPUT	EQU	00A2H")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX	EQU	00B7H")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTSTCK	EQU	00D5H")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTTRIG	EQU	00D8H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0D00H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----	Note: display joystick status")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STICK:	LD	A,1		;choose joystick 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTSTCK		;read joystick status")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(WK1),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,1		;choose joystick 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTTRIG		;read trigger status")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,STCK1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,WDON 	;trigger ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	STCK2")
  ManualsHelp_L("STCK1:	LD	HL,WDOFF	;trigger OFF")
  ManualsHelp_L("STCK2:	CALL	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WK1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,BRKCH0	;do not use joystick")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("STCK3:	DEC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,STCK4")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	STCK3")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STCK4:	SLA	C		;C := C*16")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SLA	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SLA	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SLA	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,0		;Accounting Strings data address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,WDSTK")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BRKCH0: LD	A,0DH		;put carriage return")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHPUT		;code := 0DH")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BRKCHK: CALL	BREAKX		;break check")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	STICK")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- put strings to screen -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUTSTR: LD	A,(HL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	Z")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CHPUT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	PUTSTR")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- string area -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WDON:	DB	'Trigger ON:  $'")
  ManualsHelp_L("WDOFF:	DB	'Trigger OFF: $'")
  ManualsHelp_L("WDSTK:	DB	'UP only      ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Up and Right ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Right only   ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Right & Down ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Down only    ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Down and Left',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Left only    ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DB	'Left and Up  ',0DH,0AH,'$'")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WK1:	DW	0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.3 Paddle Use")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure 5.24 shows the paddle circuit. Sending a pulse to the 8th terminal ")
  ManualsHelp_L("causes the single stable multi-vibrator to generate a pulse with a specified ")
  ManualsHelp_L("interval. This interval depends on the value of the variable register which ")
  ManualsHelp_L("can range from 10 to 3000 microseconds (0.01 to 3.00 ms). Measuring the pulse ")
  ManualsHelp_L("length enables the value in the variable register and the turning angle to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("obtained.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.24	Paddle circuit")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      --+--")
  ManualsHelp_L("				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("			       <_")
  ManualsHelp_L("				_>  150KOhm Variable Resistor")
  ManualsHelp_L("			       <")
  ManualsHelp_L("				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		      0.04 uF	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       +--| |---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       |	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    ---+--------+---")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |\	    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |  \	    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("(8) -----|   >O----O| A 	 Q |------------- (1)  (For 2, 3, 4, 6, or 7,")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |  /	    |		   |			a similar circuit")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |/	    |		   |			would apply)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 +----------| B 	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |	    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |	    |		   | (One-shot trigger IC, LS123 compatible)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |	    |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" +5V	 |	    ----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(" --+--	 |		   O")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	 |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   +-----+-----------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			____")
  ManualsHelp_L("			:  :")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input to 8	________:  :_____________________________________")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			_________________________________")
  ManualsHelp_L("			:				:")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output to 1	________:				:________")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|<------- 10 us to 3 ms ------->|")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BIOS routines for accessing the paddle are described below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* GTPDL (00DEH/MAIN) .................. read paddle information")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- paddle number (1 to 12)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- turning angle (0 to 255)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	examines the status of the paddle specified in the A register")
  ManualsHelp_L("		and returns the result in the A register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.4 Use of Touch Panel, Light Pen, Mouse, and Track Ball")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The touch panel, light pen, mouse, and track ball (cat) are accessible using ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the same BIOS routine. This routine is described below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* GTPAD (00DBH/MAIN) .................. access to various I/O devices")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A <-- device ID (0 to 19)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A <-- objective information")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	obtains various information as shown in Table 5.5 according")
  ManualsHelp_L("		to the value specified in the A register. This is the same")
  ManualsHelp_L("		as the PAD function of BASIC. " + Chr(34) + "XXX1" + Chr(34) + " in the table means the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		" + Chr(34) + "XXX" + Chr(34) + " device connected to the universal I/O interface 1;")
  ManualsHelp_L("		" + Chr(34) + "XXX2" + Chr(34) + " means the one connected to the universal I/O interface")
  ManualsHelp_L("		#2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 5.5  GTPAD BIOS Function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  Device ID  |  Device specified  |	     Information returned	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------+--------------------+-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      0      | 		   |  0FFH when touching panel surface,  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | 		   |  00H when not			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      1      | 		   |  X-coordinate (0 to 255)		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------|   Touch panel 1    |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      2      | 		   |  Y-coordinate (0 to 255)		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      3      | 		   |  0FFH when button is pressed,	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | 		   |  00H when not			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------------+-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      4      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      5      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------|   Touch panel 2    |  Same as above			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      6      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      7      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------------+-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      8      | 		   |  0FFH: valid data, 		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | 		   |  00H: invalid data 		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      9      | 		   |  X-coordinate (0 to 255)		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------|   Light pen	   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     10      | 		   |  Y-coordinate (0 to 255)		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     11      | 		   |  0FFH when switch is pressed,	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | 		   |  00H when not			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------------+-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     12      | 		   |  Always 0FFH			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | 		   |  (used to request for input)	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     13      |   Mouse 1 or	   |  X-coordinate (0 to 255)		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------|   track ball 1	   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     14      | 		   |  Y-coordinate (0 to 255)		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     15      | 		   |  Always 00H			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	      | 		   |  (no meaning)			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------+--------------------+-------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     16      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     17      |   Mouse 2 or	   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------|   track ball 2	   |  Same as above			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     18      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------| 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     19      | 		   |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note 1: Though information of the coordinate of the light pen (A = 9, 10) and")
  ManualsHelp_L("	the switch (A = 11) are read at the same time when BIOS is called")
  ManualsHelp_L("	with A = 8, other values are valid only when the result is 0FFH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	In the case that the result of BIOS which is called with A = 8 is")
  ManualsHelp_L("	00H, the coordinate values and the status of the switch contained")
  ManualsHelp_L("	after that are meaningless.")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note 2: Mouse and track ball are automatically distinguished.")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note 3: To obtain the coordinate value of the mouse or the track ball, do the")
  ManualsHelp_L("	input request call (A = 12 or A = 16), then execute the call to")
  ManualsHelp_L("	obtain the coordinate value actually. In this case, the interval of")
  ManualsHelp_L("	these two calls must be minimized as possible. Too much interval")
  ManualsHelp_L("	between the input request and the coordinate input causes the")
  ManualsHelp_L("	obtained data to be unreliable.")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note 4: To obtain the status of the trigger button of the mouse or the")
  ManualsHelp_L("	trigger button of the track ball, use GTTRIG (00D8H/MAIN), not GTPAD")
  ManualsHelp_L("	routine.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.8  Touch panel use")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.8   touch pad access")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX	EQU	00B7H")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTPAD	EQU	00D8H")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTVRM	EQU	004DH")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0B000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----	Note:  Displays " + Chr(34) + "*" + Chr(34) + " at position specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("				       by touch pad.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PAD:	XOR	A		;check sense")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,PAD1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD		;break check")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	NZ")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	PAD")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PAD1:	LD	A,1		;get X axis")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SRL	A		;A := A/8")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SRL	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SRL	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(WORK),A	;reserve X axis")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2		;get Y axis")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,A		;HL := Y data (0-255)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC		;HL := HL*3 (HL := 0-767)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	11100000B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WORK)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	A,L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,1800H	;VRAM start address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2AH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTVRM		;write VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD		;break check")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	NZ")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	PAD")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- work area -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WORK:	DW	0		;work")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.9  Mouse and track ball use")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.9   mouse and track ball access")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTPAD	EQU	00DBH")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTVRM	EQU	004DH")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVRM	EQU	004AH")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX	EQU	00B7H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ORG	0D000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----	Note:  Displays " + Chr(34) + "*" + Chr(34) + " at position specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("				       by mouse or track ball.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEST:	CALL	VADR		;Put old data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WKOLD)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTVRM")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,12")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD		;Request mouse/track ball data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,13")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD		;Read X val.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(WKXVAL),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,14")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTPAD		;Read Y val.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(WKYVAL),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WKX)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WKXVAL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	A,B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	245		;X<0?")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,TEST01")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A		;X=0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	TEST02")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEST01: CP	32		;X>31?")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,TEST02")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,31")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEST02: LD	(WKX),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WKY)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WKYVAL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	A,B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	245		;Y<0?")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,TEST03")
  ManualsHelp_L("	XOR	A		;Y=0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	TEST04")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEST03: CP	24		;Y>23?")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	C,TEST04")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,23")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEST04: LD	(WKY),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	VADR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	RDVRM		;Read old data")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(WKOLD),A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	VADR")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,2AH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WRTVRM		;Put cursor (" + Chr(34) + "*" + Chr(34) + ").")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	BREAKX		;Break check")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET	C")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WAIT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	TEST")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VADR:	LD	A,(WKY) 	;Make SCREEN Address:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,A		;  From X,Y axis on WORK AREA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,0		;  To Hl reg.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SRL	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RR	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SRL	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RR	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	SRL	H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RR	L")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(WKX)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	A,L		;  Y=32+X")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,1800H	;  VRAM start address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WAIT:	LD	A,0		;WAIT routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("WLP1:	INC	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,(IX+0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NZ,WLP1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- data -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WKX:	DB	10		;X axis")
  ManualsHelp_L("WKY:	DB	10		;Y axis")
  ManualsHelp_L("WKOLD:	DB	0		;Character code on (X,Y)")
  ManualsHelp_L("WKXVAL: DB	0		;X variable")
  ManualsHelp_L("WKYVAL: DB	0		;Y variable")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6. CLOCK AND BATTERY-POWERED MEMORY")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX2 uses a CLOCK-IC to for its timer function. Since this IC is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("battery-powered, it remains active even after MSX2 is turned off. MSX2 uses a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("small amount of RAM inside to set the PASSWORD or to set the screen mode at ")
  ManualsHelp_L("startup automatically, in addition to the CLOCK functions.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.1 CLOCK-IC Functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This IC has the following three functions:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CLOCK function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	- set/read the settings of " + Chr(34) + "year, month, day, day of week, hour,")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  minute, second" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("	- for the expression of time, 24-hour clock/12-hour clock available")
  ManualsHelp_L("	- for months, months of 31 days and of 30 days are distinguished")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  (leap years are also recognised)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Alarm function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	- when the time for alarm is set, CLOCK generates signals")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  at that time.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	- the time for alarm is set as " + Chr(34) + "XXday XXhour XXminute" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Battery-powered memory function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	- has 26 sets of 4-bit memory, and can be battery-powered.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	- MSX2 stores the following data in this memory:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		1. adjustment value of CRT display width and height")
  ManualsHelp_L("		2. initial values of SCREEN, WIDTH, colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("		3. BEEP tone and volume")
  ManualsHelp_L("		4. title screen colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("		5. country code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		6. password	      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("		7. BASIC prompt 	| (one of 6 to 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		8. title caption      --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.2 Structure of the CLOCK-IC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The CLOCK-IC has four blocks inside as shown in Figure 5.25. Each block ")
  ManualsHelp_L("consists of 13 sets of 4-bit registers, which are specified by addresses from ")
  ManualsHelp_L("0 to 12. In addition, it has three 4-bit registers for selecting the block or ")
  ManualsHelp_L("controlling functions; they are specified by the addresses from 13 to 15.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The registers inside the block (#0 to #12) and the MODE register (#13) can be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("read from and written to. The TEST register (#14) and RESET register (#15) ")
  ManualsHelp_L("can only be written to.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.25	Clock IC structure")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("       BLOCK 0		  BLOCK 1	     BLOCK 2		BLOCK 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("       (CLOCK)		  (ALARM)	     (RAM-1)		(RAM-2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("   ----------------   ----------------	 ----------------   ----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   | Seconds (the |   | 	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 0 | 1st decimal  |   |   ________   |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   | place)	  |   | 	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |--------------|   |--------------|	 |-	       -|   |-		  -|")
  ManualsHelp_L("   | Seconds (the |   | 	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 1 | 2nd decimal  |   |   ________   |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   | place)	  |   | 	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |--------------|   |--------------|	 |-	       -|   |-		  -|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" . |	  .	  |   |      .	     |	 |   Any data	|   |	Any data   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" . |	  .	  |   |      .	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" . |	  .	  |   |      .	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" . |	  .	  |   |      .	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" . |	  .	  |   |      .	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |--------------|   |--------------|	 |-	       -|   |-		  -|")
  ManualsHelp_L("   | Year (the	  |   | 	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 12| 2nd decimal  |   |   ________   |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   | place)	  |   | 	     |	 |		|   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   ----------------   ----------------	 ----------------   ----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   :<-- 4 bits -->:   :<-- 4 bits -->:	 :<-- 4 bits -->:   :<-- 4 bits -->:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   ----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("13 |	 MODE	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |--------------| --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("14 |	 TEST	  |   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |--------------|   |-- Write only")
  ManualsHelp_L("15 |	 RESET	  |   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   ---------------- --+")
  ManualsHelp_L("   :<-- 4 bits -->:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.3 MODE Register Functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The MODE register has the following 3 functions:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Selecting block")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To read from or write to registers from #0 to #12, select the block to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("used and then access the objective address. The 2 low order bits of the MODE ")
  ManualsHelp_L("register are used to select the block.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Registers from #13 to #15 are accessible whichever block is selected.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Alarm output ON/OFF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To switch the alarm input ON/OFF, use bit 2 of the MODE register. Since the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("standard MSX2 does not support the alarm, modifying this bit causes nothing ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to happen in general.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Terminating CLOCK count")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("By writing " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " in bit 3 of the MODE register, the count in seconds is stopped ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(the stages before the seconds are not stopped) and the clock function is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("terminated. By writing " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " in bit 3, the count is resumed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.26	MODE register functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  B3   B2   B1	 B0")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| TE | AE | M1 : M0 |  MODE register (#13)")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |       |       00: select block 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |       |       01: select block 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |       +---->  10: select block 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |	       11: select block 3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    +------------>  0:  alarm output OFF")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |		       1:  alarm output ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  +----------------->  0:  CLOCK count stop (in seconds)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       1:  CLOCK count start")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.4 TEST Register functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The TEST register (#14) is used to increment the upper counter quickly and to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("confirm that date and time carries are done correctly. Setting " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " in each ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bit of the register, the pulse of 2^14 (=16384)[Hz] is directly set in day, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("hour, minute, and second counters.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.27	TEST register functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  B3   B2   B1	 B0")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| T3 | T2 | T1 | T0 |  TEST register (#14)")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |    |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |  Hours  |  Seconds ........ the location for the pulse to be placed")
  ManualsHelp_L(" Day	  Minutes")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.5 RESET Register Functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The RESET register (#15) has the following functions:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Resetting the alarm")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Setting " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " in bit 0 causes all alarm registers to be reset to 0.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting the seconds")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Setting " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " in bit 1 causes the stage before the seconds to be reset. Use ")
  ManualsHelp_L("this function to set the seconds correctly.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Clock pulse ON/OFF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Setting " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " in bit 2 turns the 16Hz clock pulse output ON, and setting " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bit 3 turns the 1Hz clock pulse output ON. Note that both are not supported ")
  ManualsHelp_L("by the MSX2 standard.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.28	RESET register function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  B3   B2   B1	 B0")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("| C1 | C16| CR | AR |  RESET register (#15)")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |    |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |    |	 +-->  When " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", all alarm registers are reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    |    +------->  When " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ", fractions smaller than a second are reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |    +------------>  When " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ", 16[Hz] clock pulse is ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("  +----------------->  When " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + ", 1[Hz] clock pulse is ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("6.6 Setting the Clock and Alarm")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Setting date and time")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Block 0 is used to set the clock. Selecting block 0 in the MODE register ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and writing data in the objective register causes the date and the time to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("set. The current time is acquired by reading the contents of the register. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("See Figure 5.29 for the meaning of the register and its address.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Block 1 is used to set the alarm. Note that the time of the alarm can be set ")
  ManualsHelp_L("only in days, hours, and minutes. Nothing happens, in general, when the time ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of the clock meets the time of the alarm.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In the clock, the year is represented by 2 digits (registers #11 and #12). In ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX-BASIC, the 2 low order digits of the year is represented by adding the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("offset 80 to this value. For example, after setting register #11 to 0 and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("register #12 to 0, the year would be 80, as " + Chr(34) + "80/XX/XX" + Chr(34) + ", when the date is read ")
  ManualsHelp_L("by using the GET DATE instruction of BASIC.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The day of the week is represented by 0 to 6. This is only a mod 7 counter ")
  ManualsHelp_L("which is renewed alomg with the date, and the correspondence between the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("actual day of the week and the number value 0 to 6 is not defined.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.29	Setting the CLOCK and ALARM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       block 0 : CLOCK")
  ManualsHelp_L("   ---------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			       |  B3  |  B2  |	B1  |  B0  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |---------------------------+---------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L(" 0 |  Seconds		       |			   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |  (the 1st decimal place)  |  X	 X	X      X   |")
