  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of SUBROM routine, comment " + Chr(34) + "see page 352" + Chr(34) + " has been changed ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to " + Chr(34) + "see appendix 2..." + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of SLTATR and SLTWRK work areas, expressions for calculate ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the concrete work area for a given slot and page have been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In the first line after beginning of section 7.2.3, " + Chr(34) + "The following ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routines..." + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to " + Chr(34) + "The following addresses..." + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure 5.52, indication of F380H address was placed in the middle of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("user's area. It has been moved to the beginning of system work.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHAPTER 5 - ACCESS TO PERIPHERALS THROUGH BIOS (Part 7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7. SLOTS AND CARTRIDGES")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The CPU (Z80) used in the MSX can access an address space of only 64K bytes ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(0000H to FFFFH). MSX is set up to access an effective space of 1M bytes. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("This is accomplished by using " + Chr(34) + "slots" + Chr(34) + ", which allocate more than one memory ")
  ManualsHelp_L("byte or device to the same address.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This chapter introduces the use of the slot and information necessary to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("connect the cartridge software or the new device to MSX via the slot.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.1 Slots")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("A slot is an interface to effectively use a large address space, and to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("interface any memory or devices connected to the MSX address bus installed ")
  ManualsHelp_L("via the slot. The BASIC ROM inside the machine or RAM at MSX-DOS mode are not ")
  ManualsHelp_L("exceptions. The place at which the cartridge software is installed is also ")
  ManualsHelp_L("one of the slots. The following descriptions introduce how the software and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the devices are connected to the slot.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.1.1 Basic slot and expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The slot is either a basic slot or a expansion slot. A " + Chr(34) + "basic slot" + Chr(34) + " is a slot ")
  ManualsHelp_L("directly connected to the CPU address bus, as shown in Figure 5.36. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("standard MSX machine can have up to four basic slots. The basic slot can be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("expanded up to four slots by connecting a slot expansion box (in some cases, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the expansion is already done inside the machine), and is called " + Chr(34) + "expansion ")
  ManualsHelp_L("slots" + Chr(34) + ". When each of four basic slots is expanded to four expansion slots, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the maximum number of slots is 16. If you multiply 16 slots x 64K bytes you ")
  ManualsHelp_L("will get 1M bytes of accessible address space.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note that the system itself cannot be started when expansion slot boxes are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("connected to the expansion slot. So the user should only connect expansion ")
  ManualsHelp_L("slot boxes to the basic slots. (Though the slot for the standard MSX ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridge is always a basic slot, in some cases the connector for the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("optional hardware of each machine might be connected to the expansion slot).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.36	Basic slot and expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("					---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|  CPU	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("					    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("					    O")
  ManualsHelp_L("					     \")
  ManualsHelp_L("					       \")
  ManualsHelp_L("						 \")
  ManualsHelp_L("						   \")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    O		    O		    O		    O")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    |		    |		    |		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		---------	---------	---------	---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|	|	|	|	|	|	|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Basic slot	|	|	|	|	|	|	|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|	|	|	|	|	|	|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		|	|	|	|	|	|	|	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("		---------	---------	---------	---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 Slot #0	    O		 Slot #2	 Slot #3")
  ManualsHelp_L("				  /")
  ManualsHelp_L("				/")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      /")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       O	     O		   O		 O")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       |	     |		   |		 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   ---------	 ---------     ---------     ---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   |	   |	 |	 |     |       |     |	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("Expansion  |	   |	 |	 |     |       |     |	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("slot	   |	   |	 |	 |     |       |     |	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   |	   |	 |	 |     |       |     |	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   ---------	 ---------     ---------     ---------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   Slot #1-0	 Slot #1-1     Slot #1-2     Slot #1-3")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Each slot has 64K bytes from 0000H to FFFFH of address space and MSX manages ")
  ManualsHelp_L("it by dividing it into four " + Chr(34) + "pages" + Chr(34) + " of 16K bytes each. The CPU can select and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("access any slot for each page, and, as shown in Figure 5.37, it is possible ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to select and combine portions of several slots. Note that a pages with a ")
  ManualsHelp_L("given page number cannot be assigned to a page with a different page number ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(that is, page n of each slot is also page n to the CPU).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.37	Example of the page selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-------    -------    -------	 -------		-------")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 0	|  A  |    |  E  |    |  I  |	 |  M  |  <---------->	|  A  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----|    |-----|    |-----|	 |-----|		|-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 1	|  B  |    |  F  |    |  J  |	 |  N  |  <---------->	|  J  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----|    |-----|    |-----|	 |-----|		|-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 2	|  C  |    |  G  |    |  K  |	 |  O  |  <---------->	|  G  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----|    |-----|    |-----|	 |-----|		|-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 3	|  D  |    |  H  |    |  L  |	 |  P  |  <---------->	|  H  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-------    -------    -------	 -------		-------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 Slot 0     Slot 1     Slot 2	  Slot 3	      CPU address")
  ManualsHelp_L("								 space")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.1.2 Selecting slots")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Selecting slots is different for the basic slot than for the expansion slot. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("For basic slots, it is done through the I/O port at A8H (see Figure 5.38), ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and for expansion slots, it is done through the " + Chr(34) + "expansion slot selection ")
  ManualsHelp_L("register (FFFFH)" + Chr(34) + " of the installed expansion slot (see Figure 5.39). It is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("not recommended to change them directly, so the user should not switch the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("slots without careful planning. When the program switches the slot of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("page in which it resides, the action is not always predictable. To call the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("program in another slot, use the inter-slot call described in the next ")
  ManualsHelp_L("section.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.38	Selecting the basic slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	     I/O port (A8H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    :	  |    :    |	 :    |    :	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	  |	    |	      | 	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------+---------+---------+---------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       |	 |	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       |	 |	   +---> Basic slot number of page 0 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       |	 +-------------> Basic slot number of page 1 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       +-----------------------> Basic slot number of page 2 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +---------------------------------> Basic slot number of page 3 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.39	Selecting the expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Expansion slot selection (FFFFH in expansion slot)")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    :	  |    :    |	 :    |    :	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	  |	    |	      | 	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+---------+---------+---------+---------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       |	 |	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       |	 |	   +---> Expn. slot number of page 0 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       |	 +-------------> Expn. slot number of page 1 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     |	       +-----------------------> Expn. slot number of page 2 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("     +---------------------------------> Expn. slot number of page 3 (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: to identify the kind of slot, in the case of the expansion slot, the")
  ManualsHelp_L("      value written is read as the reversed value. The value of this register")
  ManualsHelp_L("      is the same inside the basic slot.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The slot where MAIN-ROM or RAM is installed and the slot number of the slot ")
  ManualsHelp_L("for the cartridge depend on the machine. Refer to the appropriate manual to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("see how slots are used on your MSX. But the MSX standard guarantees the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("normal operation no matter what is in the slots, so it is not necessary to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("worry about the slot use, as long as you are following the standard.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In some cases, however, it is required to know the slot number of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("specified software. For example, in the previous version, BASIC MAIN-ROM was ")
  ManualsHelp_L("placed in basic slot #0 or in expansion slot #0-0 when basic slot #0 was ")
  ManualsHelp_L("expanded. So when MSX1 is upgraded to have the MSX2 functions by installing ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX-VIDEO and BASIC ver 2.0 ROM, the MAIN ROM should be placed somewhere ")
  ManualsHelp_L("other than slot #0 or slot #0-0. The slot where MSX2 SUB-ROM resides depends ")
  ManualsHelp_L("on the machine, but the information about the slot where BASIC interpreter ")
  ManualsHelp_L("ROM resides can be obtained by referring to the work area described below ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(the slot information can be obtained in the format shown in Figure 5.40). ")
  ManualsHelp_L("When calling BIOS from DOS, examine the slot of MAIN-ROM in this way.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* EXPTBL (FCC1H, 1)	the slot of MAIN-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("* EXBRSA (FAF8H, 1)	the slot of SUB-ROM (0 for MSX1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.40	Format for the slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSB				      LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("   7	6    5	  4    3    2	 1    0")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    |	  :    :    |	 :    |    :	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    |		    |	      | 	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+----+--------------+---------+---------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |	  Unused	 |	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |			 |	   +---> Basic slot number (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |			 +-------------> Expansion slot number (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  +------------------------------------> " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " if expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When a given routine resides over page 1 and page 2 (4000H to BFFFH), the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("same slot for page 2 as the one for page 1 should be selected when the jump ")
  ManualsHelp_L("from page 1 to page 2 occurs within this routine. To do this, you need to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("examine the slot, in page 1, where the program resides and then to switch ")
  ManualsHelp_L("page 2 to that slot. To obtain information about the slot where the program ")
  ManualsHelp_L("currently is, execute the program shown in List 5.11.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.11  Program to know the current slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.11   to know where you are")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Suppose your program cartridge is 32K bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	long (4000h..0BFFFH). You set the ID at 4000H")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	and 4001H and the execution start address within")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	page 1 (4000h..7FFFH), MSX passes control")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	to this address so the part which resides in")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	page 2 is not yet enabled at this point. You")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	have to know where you are (in what primary")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	slot, in what secondary slot) and enable the")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	part at page 2. Below is the sample program")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	to do this.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENASLT	EQU	0024H		;enable slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("RSLREG	EQU	0138H		;read primary slot select register")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXPTBL	EQU	0FCC1H		;slot is expanded or not")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- program start -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENAP2:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	RSLREG		;read primary slot #")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA			;move it to bit 0,1 of [Acc]")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00000011B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,EXPTBL	;see if this slot is expanded or not")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A		;save primary slot #")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(HL)		;See if the slot is expanded or not")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	C		;set MSB if so")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A		;save it to [C]")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL		;Point to SLTTBL entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(HL)		;Get what is currently output")
  ManualsHelp_L("				;to expansion slot register")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00001100B")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	C		;Finally form slot address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	H,80H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	ENASLT		;enable page 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.2 Inter-slot Calls (calls between slots)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("As described above, programs reside in different slots, so a program not in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the current slot might be needed in some cases. The most common cases are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("listed below:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	(1) calling BIOS in MAIN-ROM from MSX-DOS level")
  ManualsHelp_L("	(2) calling BIOS in SUB-ROM from BASIC level (only the case of MSX2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	(3) calling BIOS in MAIN-ROM or SUB-ROM from cartridge software")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In doing such calls, to switch slots easily and safely, there is a group of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("BIOS routines called the inter-slot calls, which can be called from the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routine in any slot. This section describes the use of the inter-slot calls.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.2.1 Inter-slot call operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When calling BIOS in MAIN-ROM from MSX-DOS, the state of slots changes as ")
  ManualsHelp_L("described below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1) Since, in the initial MSX-DOS mode, RAM is selected all over 64K address")
  ManualsHelp_L("    space, BASIC-ROM cannot be accessible in this state (see Figure 5.41-a).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2) To call BIOS in ROM, switch page 0 to MAIN-ROM or BASIC to access. Then,")
  ManualsHelp_L("    call BIOS (see Figure 5.41-b).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(3) Restore the original status after BIOS operations and return to the")
  ManualsHelp_L("    initial address.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.41	Inter-slot call")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("a) When using MSX-DOS")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	MSX-DOS   BASIC-ROM			  MSX-DOS   BASIC-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-------    -------			  -------    -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 0	| RAM |    | ROM |		  Page 0  | RAM |    | ROM | BIOS is")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----|    |-----|			  |-----|    |-----| called")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 1	| RAM |    | ROM |		  Page 1  | RAM |    | ROM |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----|    |-----|  <---------->	  |-----|    |-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 2	| RAM |    | ___ |		  Page 2  | RAM |    | ___ |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----|    |-----|			  |-----|    |-----|")
  ManualsHelp_L("Page 3	| RAM |    | ___ |		  Page 3  | RAM |    | ___ |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-------    -------			  -------    -------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 Slot 3     Slot 0			   Slot 3     Slot 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    ")
  ManualsHelp_L("This is easily done when the program resides in other than page 0, but there ")
  ManualsHelp_L("can be some problem when the calling program resides in page 0 which is the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("same page as BIOS of the called program. Care is needed to prevent the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("program from disappearing itself and generating unpredictable results when it ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is switched to page 0. The inter-slot call settles this problem by jumping to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("page 3 temporarily and then switching slots.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.2.2 Inter-slot call use")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("There are several ways to execute inter-slot calls, as described below. They ")
  ManualsHelp_L("are included in MAIN-ROM as BIOS calls. Some of them are offered in MSX-DOS, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("so inter-slot calls can be executed under MSX-DOS.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1) Inter-slot call routines in BIOS")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RDSLT (000CH/MAIN) .................. read value at specified address of")
  ManualsHelp_L("					specified slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A register <-- slot specification")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HL register <-- address to be read at")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A register <-- value which has been read out")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		AF, BC, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	reads the value at the specified address of the specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("		slot and stores it in the A register. The slot specification")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is done using the A register in the form shown in Figure")
  ManualsHelp_L("		5.40. At this point, when the objective slot is the basic")
  ManualsHelp_L("		slot, set " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " to the 6 high order bits and define the slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("		#0 to #3 using the 2 low order bits. When specifying the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		expansion slot, specify the basic slot by bit 0 and bit 1 and")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the expansion slot by bit 2 and bit 3 and set bit 7 to " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* WRSLT (0014H/MAIN) .................. write value at specified address of")
  ManualsHelp_L("					specified slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A register <-- slot specification (same format as in")
  ManualsHelp_L("						   Figure 5.40)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HL register <-- address to be written in")
  ManualsHelp_L("		E register <-- data to be written")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		AF, BC, D")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	writes E register value in the address specified by HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("		register of the slot specified by the A register (the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		specification format is the same as in Figure 5.40).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CALSLT (001CH/MAIN) ................. call specified address of specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("					slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		8 high order bits of IY register <-- slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(same format as in Figure 5.40)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		IX register <-- address to be called")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	depends on the result of the called program")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		depends on the result of the called program")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	calls the routine at the address specified by IX register")
  ManualsHelp_L("		of the slot specified by the 8 high order bits of IY register")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(the specification format is the same as in Figure 5.40).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* ENASLT (0024H/MAIN) ................. swicth slots")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A register <-- slot (same format as in Figure 5.40)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HL register <-- specifies the page to switch the slot by")
  ManualsHelp_L("				2 high order bits")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		all")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	switches the page specified by the 2 high order bits of the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HL register to the slot specified by the A register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CALLF (0030H/MAIN) .................. call specified address of specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("					slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		specifies the slot and the address in the inline parameter")
  ManualsHelp_L("		format")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	depends on the result of the called program")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		depends on the result of the called program")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	calls the specified address of the specified slot, but,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		different from CALSLT described above, the slot and the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		address is specified in the inline parameter format, as")
  ManualsHelp_L("		described below. That is, parameters are passet by one byte")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(same format as RDSLT) to specify that the slot is placed")
  ManualsHelp_L("		just after the instruction which calls CALLF and the next")
  ManualsHelp_L("		two bytes to specify the address are placed. " + Chr(34) + "CALL 0030H" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("		may be replaced by the RST (restart) instruction, " + Chr(34) + "RST 30H" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("		In this case, the inter-slot call is done in 4 bytes.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.42	Example of the inter-slot call execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|								|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	RST	30H		;interslot call 		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	DB	00000000B	;select slot#0			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	DW	006CH		;call address = 006CH		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|								|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RSLREG (0138H/MAIN) ................. read the basic slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("					register")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	A register <-- value which has been read")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	reads the contents of the basic slot selection register and")
  ManualsHelp_L("		stores it in the A register.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* WSLREG (013BH/MAIN) ................. write in the basic slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("					register")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		A register <-- value to be written")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		---")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	writes the A register value in the basic slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("		register and selects the slot.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* SUBROM (015CH/MAIN) ................. call specified address in SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		IX register <-- address to be called, PUSH IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("				(see Appendix 2, SUB-ROM list)")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	depends on the result of the called program")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		background register and IX, IY registers are reserved")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	This is the routine to call BASIC SUB-ROM especially. The")
  ManualsHelp_L("		slot where SUB-ROM resides is automatically examined.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Normally, EXTROM, described below, is used.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* EXTROM (015FH/MAIN) ................. call specified address in SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Input:		IX register <-- address to be called")
  ManualsHelp_L("Output: 	depends on the result of the called program")
  ManualsHelp_L("Use:		background register and IY register are reserved")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function:	This is the routine to call BASIC SUB-ROM. The difference")
  ManualsHelp_L("		between this and SUB-ROM above is the point whether the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		IX register value is pushed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2) Inter-slot call in MSX-DOS")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In MSX-DOS, five kinds of inter-slot calls are offered and their entry ")
  ManualsHelp_L("addresses are defined at jump vectors of MSX-DOS. These are the same as ones ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in BIOS, so refer to BIOS above for their functions or use. Note that these ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routines should not be used when calling routines in SUB-ROM from MSX-DOS.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RDSLT (000CH) ....... read value at specified address of specified slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("* WRSLT (0014H) ....... write value at specified address of specified slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CALSLT (001CH) ...... call specified address of specified slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("* ENASLT (0024H) ...... make specified slot available")
  ManualsHelp_L("* CALLF (0030H) ....... call specified address of specified slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.12  Calling BIOS from MSX-DOS")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.12	How to use BIOS from MSX-DOS.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALSLT	EQU	001CH		;Inter slot call")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXBRSA	EQU	0FAF0H		;Slot address of BIOS (main) ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXPTBL	EQU	0FCC1H		;Slot address of extended ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	LD	IY,(EXPTBL-1)	;Load slot address of the BIOS ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L(";				;in high byte of IY")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	LD	IX,address of the BIOS jump table")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	CALL	CALSLT")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- Sample program to set text mode -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INITXT	EQU	006CH")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINL40	EQU	0F3AEH")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("TOTEXT: LD	B,40")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(EXBRSA)	;slot address of SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	A		;0 if MSX1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,TO40")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,80")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TO40:	LD	(LINL40),B	;set width into work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	IX,INITXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	IY,(EXPTBL-1)	;get expanded slot status to IYH")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	CALSLT		;perform an inter-slot call")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI			;because CALSLT do DI")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.2.3 Work area to obtain the slot status")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The following addresses involve the slot work area.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* EXBRSA (FAF8H, 1) ........... SUB-ROM slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("     Figure 5.43  SUB-ROM slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSB				      LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("   7	6    5	  4    3    2	 1    0")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    |	  :    :    |	 :    |    :	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|    |		    |	      | 	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+----+--------------+---------+---------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |	  Unused	 |	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |			 |	   +---> Basic slot number (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |			 +-------------> Expansion slot number (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("  +------------------------------------> " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " if expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* EXPTBL (FCC1H, 4) ........... whether the basic slot is expanded or not")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.44	Selecting the basic slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 MSB				       LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    7	 6    5    4	3    2	  1    0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC1H]  |    |    :	:    |	  :    |    :	 |  MAIN-ROM slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC2H]  |    | 	   Unused		 |  Slot #1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC3H]  |    | 	   Unused		 |  Slot #2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC4H]  |    | 	   Unused		 |  Slot #3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   +--> 0: slot is not expanded")
  ManualsHelp_L("		1: slot is expanded")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* SLTTBL (FCC5H, 4) ........... preservation area for the expansion")
  ManualsHelp_L("				slot selection register value")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.45	Selecting the expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 MSB				       LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    7	 6    5    4	3    2	  1    0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------  expansion slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC5H]  |    :    |	:    |	  :    |    :	 |  register value of slot #0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------  expansion slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC6H]  |    :    |	:    |	  :    |    :	 |  register value of slot #1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------  expansion slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC7H]  |    :    |	:    |	  :    |    :	 |  register value of slot #2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------  expansion slot selection")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC8H]  |    :    |	:    |	  :    |    :	 |  register value of slot #3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |	   |	     |	       |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 +---------+---------+---------+---------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      | 	|	  |	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      | 	|	  |	    +---->  exp. slot num. for page 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      | 	|	  +-------------->  exp. slot num. for page 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      | 	+------------------------>  exp. slot num. for page 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	      +---------------------------------->  exp. slot num. for page 3")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* SLTATR (FCC9H, 64) .......... test for existance of application in each")
  ManualsHelp_L("				slot/page")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.46	Test for existence of application")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCC9H]  |    |    |	|	  Unused	 |  Slot #0-0, page 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |----+----+----+------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FCCAH]  |    |    |	|	  Unused	 |  Slot #0-0, page 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |----+----+----+------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |    |    |	|			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   .	   .	.    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("   .	   .	.    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("   .	   .	.    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |    |    |	|			 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |----+----+----+------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FD08H]  |    |    |	|	  Unused	 |  Slot #3-3, page 3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   |	|    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   |	|    +-->  Routine to process expanded statements  1:yes 0:no")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   |	+------->  Routine to process expansion device	   1:yes 0:no")
  ManualsHelp_L("	   +------------>  BASIC text				   1:yes 0:no")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The concrete work area for a given slot and page can be obtained with the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("following expression:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    SLTATR address = FCC9H + 16*basic slot + 4*expansion slot + page")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* SLTWRK (FD09H, 128) ......... work area for application")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.47	Work area for application")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------  Work area for")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FD09H]  |  ...................................  |  slot 0-0 page 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |---------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FD0BH]  |  ...................................  |  Work area for")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |---------------------------------------|  slot 0-0 page 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("   .	 .					 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("   .	 .					 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("   .	 .					 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |					 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 |---------------------------------------|  Work area for")
  ManualsHelp_L("[FD87H]  |  ...................................  |  slot 3-3 page 3")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 -----------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The concrete work area for a given slot and page can be obtained with the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("following expression:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    SLTWRK address = FD09H + 32*basic slot + 8*expansion slot + 2*page")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.3 Developing Cartridge Software")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX machines usually have at least one external slot and the hardware to be ")
  ManualsHelp_L("put there is called a " + Chr(34) + "cartridge" + Chr(34) + ". There are cartridges such as the ROM ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridges for application programs or games, input-output device cartridges ")
  ManualsHelp_L("for a disk or RS-232 interface, RAM expansion cartridges for expanding RAM, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and slot expansion cartridges for expanding slots. These cartridges make the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX easy to upgrade. BASIC and assembly language programs can also be stored ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in ROM cartridge easily. This section describes how to develop cartridge ")
  ManualsHelp_L("software.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.3.1 Catridge header")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX cartridges have a 16-bye common header and, when the system is reset, the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridge is initialised by the information written in this header. For ROM ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridges of BASIC or assembly language programs, they can be automatically ")
  ManualsHelp_L("started by using the information written in the header. Figure 5.48 shows the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridge header configuration.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.48	Program cartridge header")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	-------------------   4000H or 8000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("+0000H	|	ID	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+0002H	|      INIT	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+0004H	|    STATEMENT	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+0006H	|     DEVICE	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+0008H	|      TEXT	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-----------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("+000AH	|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|    Reserved	  |   Note:  Reserved area should")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		  |	     be filled with 00H.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("+0010H	-------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* ID")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In the case of ROM cartridges, these two bytes have codes " + Chr(34) + "AB" + Chr(34) + " (41H, 42H). ")
  ManualsHelp_L("For SUB-ROM cartridges, the ID is " + Chr(34) + "CD" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* INIT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the cartridge is made to initialise the work area or I/O, these two ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bytes are the addresses for the initialization routine; otherwise 0000H is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("assumed. After instructions such as getting the work area in the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("initialization routine are placed, end with " + Chr(34) + "RET" + Chr(34) + ". All registers except the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("SP register may be destroyed. For assembly language programs, such as games, ")
  ManualsHelp_L("which loop within the cartridge, it is possible to execute the object program ")
  ManualsHelp_L("from here.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* STATEMENT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the cartridge is made to expand the CALL statement, these two bytes are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the address for the statement expansion routine; otherwise 0000H is assumed. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("If so, the statement expansion routine should reside at 4000H to 7FFFH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The CALL statement is described in the following format:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALL <expression statement name> [(<argument>[, <argument>...])]")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The expression statement name can have up to 15 characters. As an ")
  ManualsHelp_L("abbreviation for CALL, " + Chr(34) + "_" + Chr(34) + " (underscore) is available.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the BASIC interpreter finds a CALL statement, it puts the expansion ")
  ManualsHelp_L("statement name in PROCNM (FD89H, 16) in the work area and passes the control ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to cartridges, whose contents of STATEMENT of the header is other than 0, in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the order from the one with the smaller slot number. The HL register points ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to the text address next to the expansion statement name at this point (see ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure 5.49a).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.49	Input-output of the operation routine of the expansion")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    ---------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("a)  |  Input setup when the interpreter calls routines to process	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  expanded statements						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CALL ABCDE(0,0,0):A=0						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		 ^							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		 |							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		 HL							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CY flag = 1				 +---- End of the name	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |						 |     of the expanded	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		-------------------------------------  statement	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	PROCNM	|  A  |  B  |  C  |  D	|  E  | 00H |			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		-------------------------------------			|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("b)  |  Output setup when the expanded statement was not processed	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CALL ABCDE(0,0,0):A=0						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		 ^							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		 |							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		 HL							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CY flag = 1							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("c)  |  Output setup when the expanded statement was processed		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CALL ABCDE(0,0,0):A=0						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |			^						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |			|						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |			HL						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CY flag = 0							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    ---------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To develop the statement expansion routine, recognise the name of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("expansion statement written in PROCNM first, then return with setting " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the carry flag without modifying the HL register if the statement is not to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("be handled (see Figure 5.49b); otherwise, handle it properly and set the HL ")
  ManualsHelp_L("register (text pointer) to the next handled statement (where 00H or 3AH is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("placed usually), then return after setting " + Chr(34) + "0" + Chr(34) + " to the carry flag (see Figure ")
  ManualsHelp_L("5.49c).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The BASIC interpreter determines the status of the carry flag whether a CALL ")
  ManualsHelp_L("statement has been executed, and, if not, calls the next cartridge. When all ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridges have not executed the statement (when the carry flag has been " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " ")
  ManualsHelp_L("all the time), it displays " + Chr(34) + "SYNTAX ERROR" + Chr(34) + ". To test arguments of the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("statement, it is convenient to use " + Chr(34) + "internal routines for the statement ")
  ManualsHelp_L("expansion" + Chr(34) + " in section 4.4 of chapter 2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* DEVICE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("These two bytes are the addresses of the device expansion routine, when the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridge does the device expansion (the input-output device expansion); ")
  ManualsHelp_L("otherwise 0000H is used. When doing the device expansion, the device ")
  ManualsHelp_L("expansion routine should be in 4000H-7FFFH. One cartridge can have up to 4 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("devices. The name of the expansion device should be less than 16 characters.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the BASIC interpreter finds an undefined device, it stores that in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("PROCNM (FD89H, 16) and put FFH in the A register and passes control to the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridge whose contents is not 0 in the order from the one with the smaller ")
  ManualsHelp_L("slot number (see Figure 5.50a).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When creating device expansion routines, identify the file descriptor of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("PROCNM first, and, when it is not for the device to be processed, return with ")
  ManualsHelp_L("setting 1 to the carry flag (see Figure 5.50b). Otherwise, process it and set ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the device ID (0-3) in the A register, then return with setting 0 to the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("carry flag (see Figure 5.50c).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The BASIC interpreter determines by the status of the carry flag whether or ")
  ManualsHelp_L("not it is processed, and, if not, call the next cartridge. When all ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cartridges were not processed (that is, when the carry flag was " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " all the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("time), " + Chr(34) + "Bad file name ERROR" + Chr(34) + " is displayed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the actual input-output operations are done, the BASIC interpreter sets ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the device ID (0-3) in DEVICE (FD99H) and sets the request to the device in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the A register (see Table 5.6), then calls the device expansion routine. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("device expansion routine should refer to it to handle the request.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.50	Input-output to the device expansion routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    ---------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("a)  |  Input setup when the interpreter calls routines to process	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  the expanded device						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  OPEN " + Chr(34) + "ABC:" + Chr(34) + "...                                                   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  A register = FFH 						|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CY flag = 1		     +---- End of the file descriptor	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |				     |					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		-------------------------				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |	PROCNM	|  A  |  B  |  C  | 00H |				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |		-------------------------				|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("b)  |  Output setup when the expanded device was not processed		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CY flag = 1							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |-------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("c)  |  Output setup when the expanded device was processed		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  A register = device ID (0 to 3)					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  CY flag = 0							|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |									|")
  ManualsHelp_L("    ---------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Table 5.6  Requests to the device")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  Register A  |       Request	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	0      |  OPEN		     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	2      |  CLOSE 	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	4      |  Random access      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	6      |  Sequential output  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	8      |  Sequential input   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      10      |  LOC function	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      12      |  LOF function	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      14      |  EOF function	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      16      |  FPOS function      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|--------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|      18      |  Backup character   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("--------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* TEXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("These two bytes are text pointers of the BASIC program, when the BASIC ")
  ManualsHelp_L("program in the cartridge would be auto-started (executed at reset); otherwise ")
  ManualsHelp_L("they are 0000H. The size of the program must be under 16K bytes, 8000H to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("BFFFH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The BASIC interpreter examines the contents of TEXT of the header after the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("initialization (INIT) and after the system is started. When they are not ")
  ManualsHelp_L("0000H, it begins the execution from the address as BASIC text pointer (see ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure 5.51). BASIC programs should be stored in the form of the intermediate ")
  ManualsHelp_L("code and the beginning of it (the address pointed by TEXT) must be 00H, which ")
  ManualsHelp_L("indicates the beginning of the program.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The execution speed of the program will be improved when the objective line ")
  ManualsHelp_L("number of statements such as GOTO is the absolute address of the objective ")
  ManualsHelp_L("text pointer.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.51	Executing BASIC program cartridge")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |  8000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	TEXT	    |----+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------------|	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |	 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------------|<---+")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   BASIC program   |  The first byte must be 00H")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("---------------------  BFFFH")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* How to place BASIC programs in ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1. Change the starting address of BASIC text to 8021H.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POKE &HF676,&H21 : POKE &HF677,&H80 : POKE &H8020,0 : NEW")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	Note:  these statements must be in one line")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2. Load the objective BASIC program.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LOAD " + Chr(34) + "PROGRAM" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3. Create ID.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AD = &H8000")
  ManualsHelp_L("	FOR I = 0 TO 31    ----+")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 POKE AD + I, 0        |  clears ID area")
  ManualsHelp_L("	NEXT I		   ----+")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POKE &H8000,ASC(" + Chr(34) + "A" + Chr(34) + ")")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POKE &H8001,ASC(" + Chr(34) + "B" + Chr(34) + ")")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POKE &H8008,&H20")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POKE &H8009,&H80")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("4. Put 8000H to BFFFH in ROM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("7.3.2 notes on the creation of the cartridge software")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In programs not requiring software from other cartridges (stand-alone ")
  ManualsHelp_L("software such as games), the portion with the smaller address than the work ")
  ManualsHelp_L("area used by BIOS (F380H) can be used freely.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("But in programs which are executed by using BASIC interpreter functions, the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("same area cannot be shared as the work area. To do this, there are three ")
  ManualsHelp_L("methods:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(1) Place RAM on the cartridge itself (the safest and most reliable method).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(2) When one or two bytes are needed for the work area, use two bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("    corresponding to itself in SLTWRK (FD09H to ...) as the work area.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("(3) When more than three bytes are needed for the work area, allocates it")
  ManualsHelp_L("    from RAM used by BASIC. To do this, put the contents of BOTTOM (FC48H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("    to the area corresponding to SLTWRK (FD09H to ...), and increase the")
  ManualsHelp_L("    value of BOTTOM by the needed work area, then allocate it for the")
  ManualsHelp_L("    work area (see figure 5.52).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.52	Allocating the work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("8000H	----------------- <-- (BOTTOM)	   ----------------- <-- (SLTWRK)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		|		   |   Work area   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		|		   |---------------| <-- (BOTTOM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|  User's area  |                  |               |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		|	--->	   |  User's area  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|		|		   |		   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("F380H	|---------------|		   |---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|  System work	|		   |  System work  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFFFH	-----------------		   -----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("See the following list for the reference of (2) and (3).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.13  Example of allocating the work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.13  subroutines to support slot")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	       for ROM in 1 page")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RSLGREG EQU	0138H")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXPTBL	EQU	0FCC1H")
  ManualsHelp_L("BOTTOM	EQU	0FC48H")
  ManualsHelp_L("HIMEM	EQU	0FC4AH")
  ManualsHelp_L("SLTWRK	EQU	0FD09H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";--------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	GTSL1	Get slot number of designated page")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Entry	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Return	A	Slot address as follows")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Modify	Flags")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	    FxxxSSPP")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	    |	||||")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	    |	||++-- primary slot # (0-3)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	    |	++---- secondary slot # (0-3)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	    |	       00 if not expanded")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	    +--------- 1 if secondary slot # specified")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	This value can later be used as an input parameter")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	for the RDSLT, WRSLT, CALSLT, ENASLT and 'RST 10H'")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	GTSL10")
  ManualsHelp_L("GETSL10:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL		;Save registers")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	RSLREG		;read primary slot #")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	11B		;[A]=000000PP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,0		;[DE]=000000PP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,EXPTBL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,DE		:[HL]=EXPTBL+000000PP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A		;[E]=000000PP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(HL)		;A=(EXPTBL+000000PP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	80H		;Use only MSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	Z,GTSL1NOEXP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E		;[A]=F00000PP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A		;save primary slot number")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL		;point to SLTTBL entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(HL)		;get current expansion slot register")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	11B		;[A] = 000000SS")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA			;[A] = 0000SS00")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	E		;[A] = F000SSPP")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTSL1END:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTSL1NOEXP:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,E		;[A] = 000000PP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	GTSL1END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";--------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	ASLW1	Get address of slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Entry	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Return	HL	address of slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Modify	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	ASLW10")
  ManualsHelp_L("ASLW10:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GTSL10		;[A] = F000SSPP, SS = 00 if not expanded")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00001111B	;[A] = 0000SSPP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	L,A		:[A] = 0000SSPP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA			;[A] = SSPP0000")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00110000B	;[A] = 00PP0000")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	L		;[A] = 00PPSSPP")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00111100B	;[A] = 00PPSS00")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	01B		;[A] = 00PPSSBB")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Now, we have the sequence number for this cartridge")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	as follows.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	00PPSSBB")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	  ||||||")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	  ||||++-- higher 2 bits of memory address (1)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	  ||++---- seconday slot # (0..3)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	  ++------ primary slot # (0..3)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RLCA			;*=2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,0		;[DE] = 0PPSSBB0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,SLTWRK")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";--------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	RSLW1	Read slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Entry	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Return	HL	Content of slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Modify	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	RSLW10")
  ManualsHelp_L("RSLW10:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	ASLW10		;[HL] = address of slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	E,(HL)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	D,(HL)		;[DE] = (slot work)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL		;[HL] = (slot work)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";--------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	WSLW1	Write slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Entry	HL	Data to write")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Return	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Modify	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	WSLW10")
  ManualsHelp_L("WSLW10:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL		;[DE] = data to write")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	ASLW10		;[HL] = address of slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(HL),E")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(HL),D")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL		;[HL] = data tow write")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";--------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("; How to allocate work area for cartridges")
  ManualsHelp_L("; If the work area is greater than 2 bytes, make the SLTWRK point")
  ManualsHelp_L("; to the system variable BOTTOM (0FC48H), then update it by the")
  ManualsHelp_L("; amount of memory required. BOTTOM is set up by the initizalization")
  ManualsHelp_L("; code to point to the bottom of equipped RAM.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	   Ex, if the program is at 4000H..7FFFH.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	WORKB	allocate work area from BOTTOM")
  ManualsHelp_L(";		(my slot work) <- (old BOTTOM)")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Entry	HL	required memory size")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Return	HL	start address of my work area = old BOTTOM")
  ManualsHelp_L(";			0 if cannot allocate")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	Modify	None")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUBLIC	WORKB0")
  ManualsHelp_L("WORKB0:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EX	DE,HL		;[DE] = Size")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,(BOTTOM)	;Get current RAM bottom")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WSLW10		;Save BOTTOM to slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL		;Save old BOTTOM")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,DE		;[HL] = (BOTTOM) + SIZE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,H		;Beyond 0DFFFH?")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CP	0E0H")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	NC,NOROOM	;Yes, cannot allocate this much")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(BOTTOM),HL	;Updtae (BOTTOM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL		;[HL] = old BOTTOM")
  ManualsHelp_L("WORKBEND:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	BOTTOM became greater than 0DFFFH, there is")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	no RAM to be allocated.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("NOROOM:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	WSLW10		;Clear slot work")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JR	WORKBEND	;Return 0 in [HL]")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Hook")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The area called " + Chr(34) + "hook" + Chr(34) + " is used for expanding BASIC functions in FD9AH to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFC9H of the work area used by MSX-BASIC. One hook has five bytes, which are ")
  ManualsHelp_L("normally " + Chr(34) + "RET" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When MSX-BASIC does a certain operation (such as the one in the description ")
  ManualsHelp_L("about the hook of the work area), it calls this hook from there once. When ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the hook is " + Chr(34) + "RET" + Chr(34) + ", the control returns immediately; but the function of BASIC ")
  ManualsHelp_L("can be expanded, when these five bytes were re-written to do the inter-slot ")
  ManualsHelp_L("call to the program inside the cartridge by the initialization routine (INIT) ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(see Figure 5.53).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.14 shows an example of the program that the cartridge uses to hook ")
  ManualsHelp_L("H.KEYI for the timer interrupt ptocess.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure 5.53	Setting the hook")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC internal routine	   HOOK -----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		+-----> |      RET	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		|  +--- |---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		|  |	|      RET	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("      CALL HOOK   ------+  |	|---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .	  <--------+	|      RET	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .			|---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .			|      RET	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("				|---------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("				|      RET	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("				-----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("					|")
  ManualsHelp_L("					V")
  ManualsHelp_L("						  Interslot call")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC internal routine	   HOOK ----------------- -----> .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		+-----> |    RST 30H	|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		|	|---------------|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		|	|  Slot number	|  Expanded process")
  ManualsHelp_L("      CALL HOOK   ------+	|---------------|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .	  <-----+	|    Branch	|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		|	|-   address   -|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("	  .		|	|		|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			|	|---------------|	 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			+------ |      RET	| <---- RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("				-----------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("List 5.14  Using the hook")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  List 5.14  Sample program to use HOOK")
  ManualsHelp_L(";********************************************************")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("; Start-up initialize entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("; This program will be called when system initializing.")
  ManualsHelp_L(";")
  ManualsHelp_L("H.KEYI	EQU	0FD9AH		; interrupt hook")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXPTBL	EQU	0FCC1H		; slots expanded or not")
  ManualsHelp_L("PSLTRG	EQU	0A8H		; I/O port address of primary slot register")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXT	MYINT")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIT:")
  ManualsHelp_L(";	<<< Please insert other initialization routine here, if you need. >>>")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("; Set interrupt entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	DI			; start of critical region")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("; Get old interrupt entry inter-slot call hook")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	DE,OLDINT	; get address of old int. hook saved area")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,H.KEYI	; get address of interrupt entry hook")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	BC,5		; lenght of hook is 5 bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LDIR			; transfer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("; Which slot address is this cartridge placed?")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	GETMSLT 	; get my slot address")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("; Set new inter-slot call of interrupt entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(H.KEYI+1),A	; set slot address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,0F7H		; 'RST 30H' inter-slot call operation code")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(H.KEYI),A	; set new hook op-code")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,INTENT	; get our interrupt entry point")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(H.KEYI+2),HL	; set new interrupt entry point")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,0C9H		; 'RET' operation code")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(H.KEYI+4),A	; set operation code of 'RET'")
  ManualsHelp_L("	EI			; end of critical region")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";--------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("; Which slot address is the cartridge placed?")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  Entry: No")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  Action: Compute my slot address")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  Return: A = slot address")
  ManualsHelp_L(";  Modify: Flag")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTMSLT:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	BC		; save environment")
  ManualsHelp_L("	PUSH	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	IN	A,(PSLTRG)	; read primary slot register")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA			; move it to bit 0,1 of A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RRCA")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00000011B	; get bit 1,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A		; set primary slot No.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	B,0")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,EXPTBL	; see if the slot is expanded or not")
  ManualsHelp_L("	ADD	HL,BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	(HL)		; set MSB if so")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	C,A")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL		; point to SLTTBL entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	INC	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	A,(HL)		; get what is currently output to")
  ManualsHelp_L("				; expansion slot register")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	AND	00001100B	; get bits 3,2")
  ManualsHelp_L("	OR	C		; finally form slot address")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	HL		; restore environment")
  ManualsHelp_L("	POP	BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("	RET			; return to main")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- Interrupt entry -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INTENT:")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	MYINT		; call interrupt handler")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	OLDINT		; go to old interrupt handler")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(";----- HOOK save area -----")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("OLDINT: DS	5")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	END")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Stack pointer initialisation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When MSX has an internal disk, sometimes the disk interface ROM does the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("initialisation before the cartridge does, depending on the slot location, and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("pushes down the stack pointer in the direction of the low order address to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("allocate the work area. In this case, software not using the disk should set ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the stack pointer again after the cartridge received control; otherwise, the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("stack area might be exhausted and a system crash might occur. Remember to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("initialise the stack pointer at the beginning of the program.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Testing the preformance of the expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When general software in the market is put in the expansion slot or when RAM ")
  ManualsHelp_L("resides in the expansion slot, sometimes the application program do not work. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since most MSX2 machines use the expansion slot inside, problems may sometime ")
  ManualsHelp_L("result. Software to be sold in the market should be thoroughly tested in both ")
  ManualsHelp_L("cases that it is put in the expansion slot and that RAM resides in expansion ")
  ManualsHelp_L("slot.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since the expansion slot register is placed in FFFFH, do not use it as if it ")
  ManualsHelp_L("were RAM. For example, setting the stack in FFFFH using " + Chr(34) + "LD SP, 0" + Chr(34) + " in the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("program causes machines using the expansion slot to go out of control.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Notes on CALSLT use")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Executing the inter-slot call in CALSLT and CALLF destroys the contents of ")
  ManualsHelp_L("IX, IY, and the background processing register. When returning from this ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routine, in MSX1 the interrupt is inhibited, but in MSX2 the state before the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("call is restored.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When using CALSLT or CALLF to execute the inter-slot call, the interrupt is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("always inhibited when calling the object program (see 2 in the figure below) ")
  ManualsHelp_L("and when returning to the calling program (see 6 below).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Caller		Interslot call		  Called")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LD IY,SLOT			      (3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      +-----------------> CALLME:")
  ManualsHelp_L("LD IX,CALLME		      | 		   .")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   (1)	      |(2)		   .")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALL CALSLT ------------------+ 		   .")
  ManualsHelp_L("				      (4)	   .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			      +------------------ RET")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   (6)	      |(5)")
  ManualsHelp_L("	    <-----------------+")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In MSX2, the state of the interrupt is reserved before and after the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("inter-slot call. That is, 3 in the figure is in the same state as 1, and 6 is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("in the same state as 4. Note when the called program executes " + Chr(34) + "EI" + Chr(34) + " or " + Chr(34) + "DI" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_Commit("5. Acesso a Perifericos via BIOS (parte 7)", "MSX2 Technical Handbook")

  ManualsHelp_Begin()
  ManualsHelp_L("MSX2 TECHNICAL HANDBOOK")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Edited by:		ASCII Systems Division")
  ManualsHelp_L("Published by:		ASCII Coprporation - JAPAN")
  ManualsHelp_L("First edition:		March 1987")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Text file typed by:	Nestor Soriano (Konami Man) - SPAIN")
  ManualsHelp_L("			October 1997")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original in APPENDIX 1:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of ENASLT, the needed input in HL has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of GETYPR, the Input field has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of INITXT (MAIN), the reference to " + Chr(34) + "INIPLOT" + Chr(34) + " has been ")
  ManualsHelp_L("corrected to " + Chr(34) + "INIPLT" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of SUBROM routine, the mark " + Chr(34) + "*1" + Chr(34) + " has been erased.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In description of INITXT (SUB), the needed input in LINL40 has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- Description of PHYDIO routine has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original in APPENDIX 2:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In the explanation before Figure A.3, the indication about the excess 64 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("method has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure A.3, in the third byte, " + Chr(34) + "63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to ")
  ManualsHelp_L(Chr(34) + "-63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In the explanation before Figure A.3, the indication about the excess 64 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("method has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure A.3, in the third byte, " + Chr(34) + "63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to ")
  ManualsHelp_L(Chr(34) + "-63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("APPENDIX 1 - BIOS LISTING")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("This section lists the 126 BIOS entries available to the user.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("There are two kinds of BIOS routines, the ones in MAIN-ROM and the ones in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("SUB-ROM. They each have different calling sequences which will be described ")
  ManualsHelp_L("later. The following is the entry notation.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Label name (address)	*n")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:   descriptions and notes about the function")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:      parameters used by call")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:     parameters returned by call")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:  registers which will be used (original contentes are lost)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The value of *n has the following meanings.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("    *1 ... same as MSX1")
  ManualsHelp_L("    *2 ... call SUB-ROM internally in screen modes 5 to 8")
  ManualsHelp_L("    *3 ... always call SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("    *4 ... do not call SUB-ROM while screen modes 4 to 8 are changed")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Routines without " + Chr(34) + "*n" + Chr(34) + " are appended for MSX2.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAIN-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To call routines in MAIN-ROM, the CALL or RTS instruction is used as an ")
  ManualsHelp_L("ordinary subroutine call.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* RSTs")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Among the following RSTs, RST 00H to RST 28H are used by the BASIC ")
  ManualsHelp_L("interpreter. RST 30H is used for inter-slot calls and RST 38H is used for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("hardware interrupts.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHKRAM (0000H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests RAM and sets RAM slot for the system")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SYNCHR (0008H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Funtcion:	tests whether the character of [HL] is the specified")
  ManualsHelp_L("		character. If not, it generates SYNTAX ERROR, otherwise it")
  ManualsHelp_L("		goes to CHRGTR (0010H).")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	set the character to be tested in [HL] and the character to")
  ManualsHelp_L("		be compared next to RST instruction which calls this routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(inline parameter).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Example:	LD	HL,LETTER")
  ManualsHelp_L("				RST	08H")
  ManualsHelp_L("				DB	" + Chr(34) + "A" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("					 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("					 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("					 .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			LETTER: DB	" + Chr(34) + "B" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL is increased by one and A receives [HL]. When the tested")
  ManualsHelp_L("		character is numerical, the CY flag is set; the end of the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement (00H or 3AH) causes the Z flag to be set.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDSLT (000CH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	selects the slot corresponding to the value of A and reads")
  ManualsHelp_L("		one byte from the memory of the slot. When this routine is")
  ManualsHelp_L("		called, the interrupt is inhibited and remains inhibited")
  ManualsHelp_L("		even after execution ends.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the slot number.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 F000EEPP")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 -   ----")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 |   ||++-------------- Basic slot number (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 |   ++---------------- Expansion slot number (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		 +--------------------- " + Chr(34) + "1" + Chr(34) + " when using expansion slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HL for the address of memory to be read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the value of memory which has been read in A")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHRGTR (0010H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	gets a character (or a token) from BASIC text")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	[HL] for the character to be read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL is incremented by one and A receives [HL]. When the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		character is numerical, the CY flag is set; the end of the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement causes the Z flag to be set.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRSLT (0014H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	selects the slot corresponding to the value of A and writes")
  ManualsHelp_L("		one byte to the memory of the slot. When this routine is")
  ManualsHelp_L("		called, interrupts are inhibited and remain so even after")
  ManualsHelp_L("		execution ends.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	specifies a slot with A (same as RDSLT)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC, D")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("OUTDO (0018H)		*2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Funtion:	sends the value to current device")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the value to be sent")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   sends output to the printer when PTRFLG (F416H) is other")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    than 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   sends output to the file specified by PTRFIL (F864H) when")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    PTRFIL is other than 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALSLT (001CH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	calls the routine in another slot (inter-slot call)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	specify the slot in the 8 high order buts of the IY register")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(same as RDSLT). IX is for the address to be called.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	depends on the calling routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	depends on the calling routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DCOMPR (0020H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	compares the contents of HL and DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	sets the Z flag for HL = DE, CY flag for HL < DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENASLT (0024H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	selects the slot corresponding to the value of A and enables")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the slot to be used. When this routine is called, interrupts")
  ManualsHelp_L("		are inhibited and remain so even after execution ends.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	specify the slot by A (same as RDSLT)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		specify the page to switch the slot by 2 high order bits")
  ManualsHelp_L("		of HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GETYPR (0028H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the type of DAC (decimal accumulator)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	S, Z, P/V flags are changed depending on the type of DAC:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		integer type			single precision real type")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   C = 1				C = 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   S = 1 *				S = 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   Z = 0				Z = 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   P/V = 1				P/V = 0 *")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		string type			double precision real type")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   C = 1				C = 0 *")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   S = 0				S = 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   Z = 1 *				Z = 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   P/V = 1				P/V = 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Types can be recognised by the flag marked by " + Chr(34) + "*" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALLF (0030H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	calls the routine in another slot. The following is the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		calling sequence:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("			RST	30H")
  ManualsHelp_L("			DB	n	;n is the slot number (same as RDSLT)")
  ManualsHelp_L("			DW	nn	;nn is the called address")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	In the method described above")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	depends on the calling routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, and other registers depending on the calling routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KEYINT (0038H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	executes the timer interrupt process routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Register:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* I/O initialisation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INITIO (003BH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the device")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIFNK (003EH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the contents of function keys")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* VDP access")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DISSCR (0041H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	inhibits the screen display")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENASCR (0044H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	displays the screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTVDP (0047H)		*2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data in the VDP register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	C for the register number, B for data; the register number")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is 0 to 23 and 32 to 46")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVRM (004AH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the contents of VRAM. This is for TMS9918, so only the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		14 low order bits of the VRAM address are valid. To use all")
  ManualsHelp_L("		bits, call NRDVRM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address to be read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value which was read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTVRM (004DH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data in VRAM. This is for TMS9918, so only the 14 low")
  ManualsHelp_L("		order bits of the VRAM address are valid. To use all bits,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		call NWRVRM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address, A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETRD (0050H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets VRAM address to VDP and enables it to be read. This is")
  ManualsHelp_L("		used to read data from the sequential VRAM area by using the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		address auto-increment function of VDP. This enables faster")
  ManualsHelp_L("		readout than using RDVRM in a loop. This is for TMS9918, so")
  ManualsHelp_L("		only the 14 low order bits of VRAM address are valid. To use")
  ManualsHelp_L("		all bits, call NSETRD.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETWRT (0053H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets VRAM address to VDP and enables it to be written. The")
  ManualsHelp_L("		purpose is the same as SETRD. This is for TMS9918, so only")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the 14 low order bits of VRAM address are valid. To use all")
  ManualsHelp_L("		bits, call NSETRD.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FILVRM (0056H)		*4")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	fills the specified VRAM area with the same data. This is for")
  ManualsHelp_L("		TMS9918, so only the 14 low order bits of the VRAM address")
  ManualsHelp_L("		are valid. To use all bits, see BIGFIL.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address to begin writing, BC for the length of")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the area to be written, A for data.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LDIRMV (0059H)		*4")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	block transfer from VRAM to memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for source address (VRAM), DE for destination address")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(memory), BC for the length. All bits of the VRAM address")
  ManualsHelp_L("		are valid.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LDIRVM (005CH)		*4")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	block transfer from memory to VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for source address (memory), DE for destination address")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(VRAM), BC for the length. All bits of the VRAM address are")
  ManualsHelp_L("		valid.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGMOD (005FH)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	changes the screen mode. The palette is not initialised. To")
  ManualsHelp_L("		initialise it, see CHGMDP in SUB-ROM.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the screen mode (0 to 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGCLR (0062H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	changes the screen colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   FORCLR (F3E9H) for foreground color")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   BAKCLR (F3EAH) for background color")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   BDRCLR (F3EBH) for border colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NMI (0066H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	executes NMI (Non-Maskable Interrupt) handling routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLRSPR (0069H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises all sprites. The sprite pattern is cleared to")
  ManualsHelp_L("		null, the sprite number to the sprite plane number, the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		sprite colour to the foregtound colour. The vertical location")
  ManualsHelp_L("		of the sprite is set to 209 (mode 0 to 3) or 217")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(mode 4 to 8).")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	SCRMOD (FCAFH) for the screen mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INITXT (006CH)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to TEXT1 mode (40 x 24). In this")
  ManualsHelp_L("		routine, the palette is not initialised. To initialise the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		palette, call INIPLT in SUB-ROM after this call.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	TXTNAM (F3B3H) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		TXTCGP (F3B7H) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		LINL40 (F3AEH) for the length of one line")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIT32 (006FH)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to GRAPHIC1 mode (32x24). In this")
  ManualsHelp_L("		routine, the palette is not initialised.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	T32NAM (F3BDH) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32COL (F3BFH) for the colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32CGP (F3C1H) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32ATR (F3C3H) for the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32PAT (F3C5H) for the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIGRP (0072H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to the high-resolution graphics mode.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		In this routine, the palette is not initialised.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	GRPNAM (F3C7H) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPCOL (F3C9H) for the colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPCGP (F3CBH) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPATR (F3CDH) for the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPPAT (F3CFH) for the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIMLT (0075H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to MULTI colour mode. In this routine,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the palette is not initialised.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	MLTNAM (F3D1H) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTCOL (F3D3H) for the colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTCGP (F3D5H) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTATR (F3D7H) for the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTPAT (F3D9H) for the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETTXT (0078H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	set only VDP in TEXT1 mode (40x24)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INITXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETT32 (007BH)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	set only VDP in GRAPHIC1 mode (32x24)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INIT32")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETGRP (007EH)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	set only VDP in GRAPHIC2 mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INIGRP")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETMLT (0081H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	set only VDP in MULTI colour mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INIMLT")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALPAT (0084H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Funtion:	returns the address of the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the sprite number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, DE, HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALATR (0087H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the address of the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the sprite number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, DE, HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GSPSIZ (008AH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the current sprite size")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the sprite size (in bytes). Only when the size is")
  ManualsHelp_L("		16 x 16, the CY flag is set; otherwise the CY flag is reset.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPPRT (008DH)		*2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	displays a character on the graphic screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the character code. When the screen mode is 0 to 8,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		set the logical operation code in LOGOPR (FB02H).")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* PSG")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GICINI (0090H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises PSG and sets the initial value for the PLAY")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTPSG (0093H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data in the PSG register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for PSG register number, E for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDPSG (0096H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the PSG register value")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for PSG register number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value which was read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STRTMS (0099H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests whether the PLAY statement is being executed as a")
  ManualsHelp_L("		background task. If not, begins to execute the PLAY statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Keyboard, CRT, printer input-output")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHSNS (009CH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests the status of the keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the Z flag is set when the buffer is empty, otherwise the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Z flag is reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGET (009FH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	one character input (waiting)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the code of the input character")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHPUT (00A2H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	displays the character")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the character code to be displayed")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LPTOUT (00A5H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sends one character to the printer")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the character code to be sent")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	if failed, the CY flag is set")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	F")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LPTSTT (00A8H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests the printer status")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	when A is 255 and the Z flag is reset, the printer is READY.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		when A is 0 and the Z flag is set, the printer is NOT READY.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CNVCHR (00ABH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	test for the graphic header and transforms the code")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is reset to not the graphic header")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the CY flag and the Z flag are set to the transformed code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is set in A")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the CY flag is set and the CY flag is reset to the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		untransformed code is set in A")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PINLIN (00AEH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	stores in the specified buffer the character codes input")
  ManualsHelp_L("		until the return key or STOP key is pressed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the starting address of the buffer minus 1, the CY")
  ManualsHelp_L("		flag is set only when it ends with the STOP key.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INLIN (00B1H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	same as PINLIN except that AUTFLG (F6AAH) is set")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the starting address of the buffer minus 1, the CY")
  ManualsHelp_L("		flag is set only when it ends with the STOP key.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("QINLIN (00B4H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	executes INLIN with displaying " + Chr(34) + "?" + Chr(34) + " and one space")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the starting address of the buffer minus 1, the CY")
  ManualsHelp_L("		flag is set only when it ends with the STOP key.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BREAKX (00B7H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests Ctrl-STOP key. In this routine, interrupts are")
  ManualsHelp_L("		inhibited.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is set when pressed")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BEEP (00C0H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	generates BEEP")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLS (00C3H)		*3")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	clears the screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	set zero flag")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("POSIT (00C6H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	moves the cursor")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	H for the X-coordinate of the cursor, L for the Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FNKSB (00C9H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests whether the function key display is active (FNKFLG).")
  ManualsHelp_L("		If so, displays them, otherwise erases them.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	FNKFLG (FBCEH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ERAFNK (00CCH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	erases the function key display")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DSPFNK (00CFH)		*2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	displays the function keys")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TOTEXT (00D2H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	forces the screen to be in the text mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Game I/O access")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTSTCK (00D5H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the joystick status")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the joystick number to be tested")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the joystick direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTTRIG (00D8H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the trigger button status")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the trigger button number to be tested")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	When A is 0, the trigger button is not being pressed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		When A is FFH, the trigger button is being pressed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTPAD (00DBH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the touch pad status")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the touch pad number to be tested")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GTPDL (00DEH)		*2")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the paddle value")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the paddle number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Cassette input-output routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPION (00E1H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the header block after turning the cassette motor ON.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	if failed, the CY flag is set")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPIN (00E4H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads data from the tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for data. If failed, the CY flag is set.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPIOF (00E7H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	stops reading the tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPOON (00EAH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes the header block after turning the cassette motor ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A = 0, short header; A <> 0, long header")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	if failed, the CY flag is set")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPOUT (00EDH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data on the tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	if failed, the CY flag is set")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TAPOOF (00F0H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	stops writing to the tape")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	if failed, the CY flag is set")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STMOTR (00F3H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets the cassette motor action")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A = 0		->	stop")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A = 1		->	start")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A = 0FFH	->	reverse the current action")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Miscellaneous")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGCAP (0132H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	alternates the CAP lamp status")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A = 0		->	lamp off")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A <>0		->	lamp on")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGSND (0135H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	alternates the 1-bit sound port status")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A = 0		->	OFF")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A <>0		->	ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RSLREG (0138H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the contents of current output to the basic slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("		register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value which was read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WSLREG (013BH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes to the primary slot register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the value to be written")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVDP (013EH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads VDP status register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value which was read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SNSMAT (0141H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the value of the specified line from the keyboard")
  ManualsHelp_L("		matrix")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the specified line")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for data (the bit corresponding to the pressed key will")
  ManualsHelp_L("		be 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, C")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PHYDIO (0144H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	Physical input/output for disk devices")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the drive number (0 = A:, 1 = B:,...)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		B for the number of sector to be read from or written to")
  ManualsHelp_L("		C for the media ID")
  ManualsHelp_L("		DE for the first sector number to be read rom or written to")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HL for the startinga address of the RAM buffer to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   read from or written to specified sectors")
  ManualsHelp_L("		CY set for sector writing; reset for sector reading")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	CY set if failed")
  ManualsHelp_L("		B for the number of sectors actually read or written")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A for the error code (only if CY set):")
  ManualsHelp_L("			0 = Write protected")
  ManualsHelp_L("			2 = Not ready")
  ManualsHelp_L("			4 = Data error")
  ManualsHelp_L("			6 = Seek error")
  ManualsHelp_L("			8 = Record not found")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       10 = Write error")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       12 = Bad parameter")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       14 = Out of memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       16 = Other error")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ISFLIO (014AH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	tests whether the device is active")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A = 0		->	active")
  ManualsHelp_L("		A <>0		->	inactive")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("OUTDLP (014DH)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	printer output.Different from LPTOUT in the following points:")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     1. TAB is expanded to spaces")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     2. For non-MSX printers, hiragana is transformed to")
  ManualsHelp_L("			katakana and graphic characters are transformed to")
  ManualsHelp_L("			1-byte characters.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     3. If failed, device I/O error occurs.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	F")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KILBUF (0156H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	clears the keyboard buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALBAS (0159H)		*1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	executes inter-slot call to the routine in BASIC interpreter")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	IX for the calling address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	depends on the called routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	depends on the called routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Entries appended for MSX2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SUBROM (015CH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	executes inter-slot call to SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	IX for the calling address and, at the same time, pushes IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("		on the stack")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	depends on the called routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	background registers and IY are reserved")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("EXTROM (015FH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	executes inter-slot call to SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	IX for the calling address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	depends on the called routine")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	background registers and IY are reserved")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("EOL (0168H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	deletes to the end of the line")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	H for X-coordinate of the cursor, L for Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BIGFIL (016BH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	same function as FILVRM. Differences are as follows:")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   In FILVRM, it is tested whether the screen mode is 0 to 3.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   If so, it treats VDP as the one which has only 16K bytes")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   VRAM (for the compatibility with MSX1). In BIGFIL, the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   mode is not tested and actions are carried out by the")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   given parameters.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as FILVRM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	same as FILVRM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	same as FILVRM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NSETRD (016EH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	enables VRAM to be read by setting the address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NSTWRT (0171H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	enables VRAM to be written by setting the address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NRDVRM (0174H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the contents of VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address to be read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value which was read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	F")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NWRVRM (0177H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data in VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address, A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SUB-ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The calling sequence of SUB-ROM is as follows:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	IX, INIPLT")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 ; Set BIOS entry address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	CALL	EXTROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 ; Returns here")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When the contents of IX should not be destroyed, use the call as shown below.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIPAL: PUSH	IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 ; Save IX")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	IX, INIPLT")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 ; Set BIOS entry address")
  ManualsHelp_L("	JP	SUBROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("			 ;Returns caller of INIPAL")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPRT (0089H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	one character output to the graphic screen (active only in")
  ManualsHelp_L("		screen modes 5 to 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NVBXLN (00C9H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	draws a box")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	start point: BC for X-coordinate, DE for Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		end point:   GXPOS (FCB3H) for X-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("			     GYPOS (FCB5H) for Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		colour:      ATRBYT (F3F3H) for the attribute")
  ManualsHelp_L("		logical operation code: LOGOPR (FB02H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NVBXFL (00CDH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	draws a painted box")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	start point: BC for X-coordinate, DE for Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		end point:   GXPOS (FCB3H) for X-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("			     GYPOS (FCB5H) for Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		colour:      ATRBYT (F3F3H) for the attribute")
  ManualsHelp_L("		logical operation code: LOGOPR (FB02H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGMOD (00D1H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	changes the screen mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the screen mode (0 to 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INITXT (00D5H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to TEXT1 mode (40 x 24)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	TXTNAM (F3B3H) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		TXTCGP (F3B7H) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		LINL40 (F3AEH) for the length of one line")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIT32 (00D9H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to GRAPHIC1 mode (32x24)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	T32NAM (F3BDH) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32COL (F3BFH) for the colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32CGP (F3C1H) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32ATR (F3C3H) for the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		T32PAT (F3C5H) for the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIGRP (00DDH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to the high-resolution graphics mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	GRPNAM (F3C7H) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPCOL (F3C9H) for the colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPCGP (F3CBH) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPATR (F3CDH) for the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		GRPPAT (F3CFH) for the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIMLT (00E1H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the screen to MULTI colour mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	MLTNAM (F3D1H) for the pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTCOL (F3D3H) for the colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTCGP (F3D5H) for the pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTATR (F3D7H) for the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		MLTPAT (F3D9H) for the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETTXT (00E5H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets VDP in the text mode (40x24)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INITXT")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETT32 (00E9H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	ses VDP in the text mode (32x24)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INIT32")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETGRP (00EDH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets VDP in the high-resolution mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INIGRP")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETMLT (00F1H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets VDP in MULTI COLOUR mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	same as INIMLT")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLRSPR (00F5H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises all sprites. The sprite pattern is set to null,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		sprite number to sprite plane number, and sprite colour to")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the foregtound colour. The vertical location of the sprite")
  ManualsHelp_L("		is set to 217.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	SCRMOD (FCAFH) for the screen mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALPAT (00F9H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Funtion:	returns the address of the sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(this routine is the same as CALPAT in MAIN-ROM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the sprite number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, DE, HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CALATR (00FDH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the address of the sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(this routine is the same as CALATR in MAIN-ROM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the sprite number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	HL for the address")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, DE, HL")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GSPSIZ (0101H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the current sprite size")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(this routine is the same as GSPSIZ in MAIN-ROM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the sprite size. The CY flag is set only for the size")
  ManualsHelp_L("		16 x 16.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GETPAT (0105H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	returns the character pattern")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the character code")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	PATWRK (FC40H) for the character pattern")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTVRM (0109H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data in VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address (0 TO FFFFH), A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDVRM (010DH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the contents of VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL for VRAM address (0 TO FFFFH) to be read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the value which was read")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGCLR (0111H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	changes the screen colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("		FORCLR (F3E9H) for the foreground color")
  ManualsHelp_L("		BAKCLR (F3EAH) for the background color")
  ManualsHelp_L("		BDRCLR (F3EBH) for the border colour")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLSSUB (0115H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	clears the screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DSPFNK (011DH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	displays the function keys")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTVDP (012DH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes data in the VDP register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	C for the register number, B for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VDPSTA (0131H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the VDP register")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the register number (0 to 9)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	F")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETPAG (013DH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	switches the page")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	DPPAGE (FAF5H) for the display page number")
  ManualsHelp_L("		ACPAGE (FAF6H) for the active page number")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("INIPLT (0141H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	initialises the palette(the current palette is saved in VRAM)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RSTPLT (0145H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	restores the palette from VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, BC, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GETPLT (0149H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	obtains the colour code from the palette")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	D for the palette number (0 to 15)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	4 high order bits of B for red code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		4 low order bits of B for blue code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		4 low order bits of C for green code")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF, DE")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SETPLT (014DH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sets the colour code to the palette")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	D for the palette number (0 to 15)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		4 high order bits of A for red code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		4 low order bits of A for blue code")
  ManualsHelp_L("		4 low order bits of E for green code")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	AF")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BEEP (017DH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	generates BEEP")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PROMPT (0181H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	displays the prompt")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NEWPAD (01ADH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the status of mouse or light pen")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	call with setting the following data in A;")
  ManualsHelp_L("		descriptions in parenthesis are return values.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   8 .......... light pen check (valid at 0FFH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   9 .......... returns X-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  10 .......... returns Y-coordinate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  11 .......... returns the light pen switch status")
  ManualsHelp_L("				(0FFH, when pressed)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  12 .......... whether the mouse is connected to the")
  ManualsHelp_L("				port 1 (valid at 0FFH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  13 .......... returns the offset in X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  14 .......... returns the offset in Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  15 .......... (always 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  16 .......... whether the mouse is connected to the")
  ManualsHelp_L("				port 2 (valid at 0FFH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  17 .......... returns the offset in X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  18 .......... returns the offset in Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  19 .......... (always 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CHGMDP (01B5H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	changes VDP mode. The palette is initialised.")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the screen mode (0 to 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KNJPRT (01BDH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	sends a kanki to the graphic screen (modes 5 to 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	BC for JIS kanji code, A for the display mode. The display")
  ManualsHelp_L("		mode has the following meaning, similar to the PUT KANJI")
  ManualsHelp_L("		command of BASIC.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   0 .......... display in 16 x 16 dot")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   1 .......... display even dots")
  ManualsHelp_L("		   2 .......... display odd dots")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("REDCLK (01F5H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	reads the clock data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	C for RAM address of the clock")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		  00MMAAAA")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    ------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    ||++++--- Address (0 to 15)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    ++------- Mode (0 to 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	A for the data which were read (only 4 low order bits are")
  ManualsHelp_L("		valid)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	F")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRTCLK (01F9H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	writes the clock data")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	A for the data to be written, C for RAM address of the clock")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	none")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	F")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=============================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original in APPENDIX 2:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In the explanation before Figure A.3, the indication about the excess 64 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("method has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure A.3, in the third byte, " + Chr(34) + "63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to ")
  ManualsHelp_L(Chr(34) + "-63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In the explanation before Figure A.3, the indication about the excess 64 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("method has been added.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- In Figure A.3, in the third byte, " + Chr(34) + "63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + " has been corrected to ")
  ManualsHelp_L(Chr(34) + "-63rd power of 10" + Chr(34) + ".")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("APPENDIX 2 - MATH-PACK")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The Math-Pack is the core for the mathematical routines of MSX-BASIC and, by ")
  ManualsHelp_L("calling these routines from an assembly language program, floating-point ")
  ManualsHelp_L("operations and trigonometrical functions are available.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Any operations involving real numbers in Math-Pack are done in BCD (Binary ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Coded Decimal). There are two ways of expressing a real number, " + Chr(34) + "single ")
  ManualsHelp_L("precision" + Chr(34) + " and " + Chr(34) + "double precision" + Chr(34) + "; a single precision real number (6 digits) ")
  ManualsHelp_L("is expressed by 4 bytes and a double precision real number (14 digits) by 8 ")
  ManualsHelp_L("bytes (see Figure A.1 and Figure A.2).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure A.1  BCD format for expressing real numbers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		     MSB   7	 6     5     4	   3	 2     1     0	 LSB")
  ManualsHelp_L("  ---	       ---	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   ^		^	|sign | 	       exponent 		|  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		|	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		|	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		|	|  mantissa 1st place	|  mantissa 2nd place	|  1")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	      single	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |	     precision	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		|	|  mantissa 3rd place	|  mantissa 4th place	|  2")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		|	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		|	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |		V	|  mantissa 5th place	|  mantissa 6th place	|  3")
  ManualsHelp_L(" double        ---	-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("precision		-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			|  mantissa 7th place	|  mantissa 8th place	|  4")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			|  mantissa 9th place	|  mantissa 10th place	|  5")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			|  mantissa 11th place	|  mantissa 12th place	|  6")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   |			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("   V			|  mantissa 13th place	|  mantissa 14th place	|  7")
  ManualsHelp_L("  ---			-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure A.2  Examples of expressions for real numbers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	Example of the single precision expression")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 123456 --> 0.123456 E+6")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       1     2	   3	 4")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    -------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		DAC |  46 |  12 |  34 |  56 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    -------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	Example of the double precision expression")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	 123456.78901234 --> 0.12345678901234 E+6")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		       1     2	   3	 4     5     6	   7	 8")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("		DAC |  46 |  12 |  34 |  56 |  78 |  90 |  12 |  34 |")
  ManualsHelp_L("		    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("A real number consists of a sign, an exponent, and a mantissa. The sign ")
  ManualsHelp_L("represents the sign of the mantissa; 0 for positive, 1 for negative. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("exponent is a binary expression and can be expressed as a power from +63 to ")
  ManualsHelp_L("-63, with an excess of 64 (see Figure A.3). Figure A.4 shows the valid range ")
  ManualsHelp_L("of double precision real numbers.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure A.3  Exponent format")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("|sign |<--------------- exponent -------------->|	meaning")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  0  |  0     0     0	   0	 0     0     0	| ..... 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  1  |  0     0     0	   0	 0     0     0	| ..... undefined (-0?)")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  x  |  0     0     0	   0	 0     0     1	| ..... -63rd power of 10")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  x  |  1     0     0	   0	 0     0     0	| ..... 0th power of 10")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  x  |  1     1     1	   1	 1     1     1	| ..... +63rd power of 10")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L(" Note: " + Chr(34) + "x" + Chr(34) + " is 1 or 0, both of which are allowed.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure A.4  Valid range for double precision real numbers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("       7     6	   5	 4     3     2	   1	 0     (byte)")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("DAC |  FF |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  -0.99999999999999 E+63")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  81 |  10 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  -0.10000000000000 E-63")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  00 |  x	|  x  |  x  |  x  |  x	|  x  |  x  |	0")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  01 |  10 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  00 |  +0.10000000000000 E-63")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("			    .")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("    |  7F |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  99 |  +0.99999999999999 E+63")
  ManualsHelp_L("    -------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In Math-Pack, the memory is predefined for operation. This memory area is ")
  ManualsHelp_L("called " + Chr(34) + "DAC (Decimal ACumulator (F7F6H)" + Chr(34) + " and the area which reserves the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("numerical value to be operated is called " + Chr(34) + "ARG (F847H)" + Chr(34) + ". For example, in ")
  ManualsHelp_L("multiplication, the product of the numbers in DAC and ARG is calculated and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("the result is returned in the DAC.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("In the DAC, single precision real numbers, double precision real numbers, and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("two-byte integers can be stored. In order to distinguish them, " + Chr(34) + "VALTYP ")
  ManualsHelp_L("(F663H)" + Chr(34) + " is used and its value is 4 for single precision real numbers, 8 for ")
  ManualsHelp_L("double precision real numbers, and 2 for two-byte integers.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Single and double precision numbers must be stored from the top of the DAC. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("For two-byte integers, the low and high bytes should be stored in DAC + 2 and ")
  ManualsHelp_L("DAC + 3.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since Math-Pack is an internal routine of BASIC, when an error occurs (such ")
  ManualsHelp_L("as division by 0 or overflow), control automatically jumps to the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("corresponding error routine, then returns to BASIC command level. To prevent ")
  ManualsHelp_L("this, change H.ERRO (FFB1H).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Math-Pack work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|  Size  |		   Meaning		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+--------+------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  VALTYP   |	F663H	|    1	 | format of the number in DAC		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DAC	    |	F7F6H	|   16	 | floating point accumulator in BCD format |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  ARG	    |	F847H	|   16	 | argument of DAC			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Math-Pack entry")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Basic operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|	Function	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+-----------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DECSUB   |	268CH	|   DAC <-- DAC - ARG	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DECADD   |	269AH	|   DAC <-- DAC + ARG	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DECNRM   |	26FAH	|   normalises DAC (*1) |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DECROU   |	273CH	|   rounds DAC		|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DECMUL   |	27E6H	|   DAC <-- DAC * ARG	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  DECDIV   |	289FH	|   DAC <-- DAC / ARG	|")
  ManualsHelp_L("-------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: These operations treat numbers in DAC and ARG as the double precision")
  ManualsHelp_L("      number. Registers are not preserved.")
  ManualsHelp_L("*1    Excessive zeros in mantissa are removed. (0.00123 --> 0.123 E-2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|	Function       |  Register modified  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+----------------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   COS     |	2993H	|   DAC <-- COS(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   SIN     |	29ACH	|   DAC <-- SIN(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   TAN     |	29FBH	|   DAC <-- TAN(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   ATN     |	2A14H	|   DAC <-- ATN(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   LOG     |	2A72H	|   DAC <-- LOG(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   SQR     |	2AFFH	|   DAC <-- SQR(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   EXP     |	2B4AH	|   DAC <-- EXP(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   RND     |	2BDFH	|   DAC <-- RND(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: These processing routines all have the same function names as those in")
  ManualsHelp_L("      BASIC. " + Chr(34) + "All" + Chr(34) + " registers are A, B, C, D, E, H, and L.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Function 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|	Function       |  Register modified  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+----------------------+---------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   SIGN    |	2E71H	|   A <-- sign of DAC  |	  A	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   ABSFN   |	2E82H	|   DAC <-- ABS(DAC)   |	 all	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   NEG     |	2E8DH	|   DAC <-- NEG(DAC)   |	 A,HL	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   SGN     |	2E97H	|   DAC <-- SGN(DAC)   |	 A,HL	     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: Except for SIGN, these processing routines all have the same function")
  ManualsHelp_L("      names as those in BASIC. Registers are A, B, C, D, E, H, and L.")
  ManualsHelp_L("      Note that for SGN, the result is represented as a 2-byte integer.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Movement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|      Function       |    Object    |	Reg. mod.  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+---------------------+--------------+-------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MAF     |	2C4DH	|   ARG <-- DAC       | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MAM     |	2C50H	|   ARG <-- (HL)      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOV8DH  |	2C53H	|   (DE) <-- (HL)     | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MFA     |	2C59H	|   DAC <-- ARG       | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MFM     |	2C5CH	|   DAC <-- (HL)      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MMF     |	2C67H	|   (HL) <-- DAC      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOV8HD  |	2C6AH	|   (HL) <-- (DE)     | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   XTF     |	2C6FH	|   (SP) <--> DAC     | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   PHA     |	2CC7H	|   ARG <-- (SP)      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   PHF     |	2CCCH	|   DAC <-- (SP)      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   PPA     |	2CDCH	|   (SP) <-- ARG      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   PPF     |	2CE1H	|   (SP) <-- DAC      | double prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   PUSHF   |	2EB1H	|   DAC <-- (SP)      | single prec. | D,E	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVFM   |	2EBEH	|   DAC <-- (HL)      | single prec. | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVFR   |	2EC1H	|   DAC <-- (CBED)    | single prec. | D,E	   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVRF   |	2ECCH	|   (CBED) <-- DAC    | single prec. | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVRMI  |	2ED6H	|   (CBED) <-- (HL)   | single prec. | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVRM   |	2EDFH	|   (BCDE) <-- (HL)   | single prec. | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVMF   |	2EE8H	|   (HL) <-- DAC      | single prec. | A,B,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVE    |	2EEBH	|   (HL) <-- (DE)     | single prec. | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   VMOVAM  |	2EEFH	|   ARG <-- (HL)      | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   MOVVFM  |	2EF2H	|   (DE) <-- (HL)     | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   VMOVE   |	2EF3H	|   (HL) <-- (DE)     | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   VMOVFA  |	2F05H	|   DAC <-- ARG       | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   VMOVFM  |	2F08H	|   DAC <-- (HL)      | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   VMOVAF  |	2F0DH	|   ARG <-- DAC       | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   VMOVMF  |	2F10H	|   (HL) <-- DAC      | VALTYP	     | B,C,D,E,H,L |")
  ManualsHelp_L("----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: (HL), (DE) means the values in memory pointed to by HL or DE. Four")
  ManualsHelp_L("      register names in the parentheses are the single precision real numbers")
  ManualsHelp_L("      which indicate (sign + exponent), (mantissa 1st and 2nd places),")
  ManualsHelp_L("      (mantissa 3th and 4th places), (mantissa 5th and 6th places) from left")
  ManualsHelp_L("      to right. Where the object is VALTYP, the movement (2, 4, 8 bytes) is")
  ManualsHelp_L("      according to the type indicated in VALTYP (F663H).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Comparison")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|      Object		   | Left | Right |Reg. mod.|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+--------------------------+------+-------+---------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FCOMP   |	2F21H	| single prec. real number | CBED |  DAC  |    HL   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   ICOMP   |	2F4DH	| 2-byte integer	   | DE   |  HL   |    HL   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   XDCOMP  |	2F5CH	| double prec. real number | ARG  |  DAC  |    all  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: Results will be in A register. Meanings of A register are:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       A = 1	-->	left < right")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       A = 0	-->	left = right")
  ManualsHelp_L("	       A = -1	-->	left > right")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("      In the comparison of single precision real numbers, CBED means that")
  ManualsHelp_L("      each register has single precision (sign + exponent),")
  ManualsHelp_L("      (mantissa 1st and 2nd places), (mantissa 3th and 4th places), and")
  ManualsHelp_L("      (mantissa 5th and 6th places).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Floating-point input/output")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|		      Function			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FIN     |	3299H	|  Stores a string representing the floating-point  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|  number in DAC, converting it in real.	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  Entry condition    HL  <--  Starting address of the string		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		      A   <--  First character of the string		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|  Return condition   DAC <--  Real number				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		      C   <--  FFH: without a decimal point		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|			       0:   with a decimal point		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		      B   <--  Number of places after the decimal point     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		      D   <--  Number of digits 			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|		      Function			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FOUT    |	3425H	|  Converts the real number in DAC to the string    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|    (unformatted)				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   PUFOUT  |	3426H	|  Converts the real number in DAC to the string    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|    (formatted)				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Entry condition   A   <-- format					    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 7   0: unformatted	 1: formatted				    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 6   0: without commas  1: with commas every three digits	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 5   0: meaningless	 1: leading spaces are padded with " + Chr(34) + "." + Chr(34) + "      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 4   0: meaningless	 1: " + Chr(34) + "$" + Chr(34) + " is added before the numerical value |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 3   0: meaningless	 1: " + Chr(34) + "+" + Chr(34) + " is added even for positive values   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 2   0: meaningless	 1: the sign comes after the value	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 1   unused							    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|     bit 0:  0: fixed point	 1: floating-point			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	B <-- number of digits before and not including the decimal point   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	C <-- number of digits after and including the decimal point	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Return condition  HL <-- starting address of the string		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|		      Function			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FOUTB   |	371AH	| Converts 2-byte integer in DAC+2, 3 to a	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|   binary expression string.			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FOUTO   |	371EH	| Converts 2-byte integer in DAC+2, 3 to an	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|   octal expression string.			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FOUTH   |	3722H	| Converts 2-byte integer in DAC+2, 3 to a	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|   hexadecimal expression string.		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Entry condition    DAC + 2	<-- 2-byte integer			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|		       VALTYP	<-- 2					    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Return condition   HL	<-- starting address of the string	    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: no strings are reserved. The starting address of the string in the")
  ManualsHelp_L("      output routine is normally in FBUFFR (from F7C5H). In some cases it")
  ManualsHelp_L("      may differ slightly. For the integer in DAC + 2, VALTYP (F663H) must")
  ManualsHelp_L("      be 2, even in cases other than FOUTB, FOUTO and FOUTH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Type conversion")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|		      Function			    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FRCINT  |	2F8AH	| Converts DAC to a 2-byte integer (DAC + 2, 3)     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FRCSNG  |	2FB2H	| Converts DAC to a single precision real number    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FRCDBL  |	303AH	| Converts DAC to a double precision real number    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   FIXER   |	30BEH	| DAC <-- SGN(DAC) * INT(ABS(DAC))		    |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: after execution, VALTYP (F663H) will contain the number (2, 4 or 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("      representing DAC type. No registers are reserved.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Integer operation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|	Function       |  Registers modified  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+----------------------+----------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   UMULT   |	314AH	|    DE <-- BC * DE    |    A, B, C, D, E     |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   ISUB    |	3167H	|    HL <-- DE - HL    |	 all	      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   IADD    |	3172H	|    HL <-- DE + HL    |	 all	      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   IMULT   |	3193H	|    HL <-- DE * HL    |	 all	      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   IDIV    |	31E6H	|    HL <-- DE / HL    |	 all	      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   IMOD    |	323AH	|    HL <-- DE mod HL  |	 alle	      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|	    |		|    (DE <-- DE/HL)    |		      |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Power")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   Label   |  Address	|    Function		     | Base | Exp. | Result |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|-----------+-----------+----------------------------+------+------+--------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   SGNEXP  |	37C8H	| power of single-prec. real | DAC  | ARG  |  DAC   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   DBLEXP  |	37D7H	| power of double-prec. real | DAC  | ARG  |  DAC   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("|   INTEXP  |	383FH	| power of 2-byte integer    | DE   | HL   |  DAC   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("-----------------------------------------------------------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note: No registers are reserved.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=============================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original in APPENDIX 3:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("none")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("APPENDIX 3 - BIT BLOCK TRANSFER")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The bit block transfer corresponds to the COPY command in BASIC and is used ")
  ManualsHelp_L("to transfer data from RAM, VRAM, and the disk. It is easily executed by the ")
  ManualsHelp_L("routine in expansion ROM and available from the assembly language program. ")
  ManualsHelp_L("Since it is in expansion ROM, use SUBROM or EXTROM of BIOS for this routine.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("1. Transferring in VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTVV (0191H/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	transfers data in VRAM area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SX (F562H, 2) 	X-coordinate of the source")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SY (F564H, 2) 	Y-coordinate of the source")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DX (F566H, 2) 	X-coordinate of the destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DY (F568H, 2) 	Y-coordinate of the destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NX (F56AH, 2) 	number of dots in the X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NY (F56CH, 2) 	number of dots in the Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* CDUMMY (F56EH, 1)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* ARG (F56FH, 1)	selects the direction and expansion")
  ManualsHelp_L("					RAM (same as VDP R#45)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* LOGOP (F570H, 1)	logical operation code (same as the")
  ManualsHelp_L("					logical operation code of VDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("2. Transferring data between RAM and VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("To use the routines below, the following memory space should be allocated as ")
  ManualsHelp_L("graphic area for screen modes.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* screen mode 6")
  ManualsHelp_L("     number of dots in X direction times number of dots in Y direction/4 + 4")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* screen mode 5 or 7")
  ManualsHelp_L("     number of dots in X direction times number of dots in Y direction/2 + 4")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* screen mode 8")
  ManualsHelp_L("     number of dots in X direction times number of dots in Y direction/2 + 4")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Note to raise fractions.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("For disk or RAM, data to indicate the size is added as the array data. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("first two bytes of data indicate the number of dots in X direction; the next ")
  ManualsHelp_L("two bytes indicate the number of dots in the Y direction.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTVM (0195H/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	transfers the array to VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DPTR (F562H, 2)	source address of memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DUMMY (F564H, 2)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DX (F566H, 2) 	X-coordinate of the destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DY (F568H, 2) 	Y-coordinate of the destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NX (F56AH, 2) 	number of dots in the X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("					(not required to be set; this is")
  ManualsHelp_L("					already in the top of data to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("					transferred)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NY (F56CH, 2) 	number of dots in the Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("					(not required to be set; this is")
  ManualsHelp_L("					already in the top of data to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("					transferred)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* CDUMMY (F56EH, 1)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* ARG (F56FH, 1)	selects the direction and expansion")
  ManualsHelp_L("					RAM (same as VDP R#45)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* LOGOP (F570H, 1)	logical operation code (same as the")
  ManualsHelp_L("					logical operation code of VDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is set when the number of data bytes to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("		transferred is incorrect")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTMV (0199H/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	transfers to the array from VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SX (F562H, 2) 	X-coordinate of the source")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SY (F564H, 2) 	Y-coordinate of the source")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DPTR (F566H, 2)	destination address of memory")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DUMMY (F568H, 2)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NX (F56AH, 2) 	number of dots in the X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NY (F56CH, 2) 	number of dots in the Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* CDUMMY (F56EH, 1)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* ARG (F56FH, 1)	selects the direction and expansion")
  ManualsHelp_L("					RAM (same as VDP R#45)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("3. Transferring between the disk and RAM or VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("The filename should be set first to use the disk (specify the filename as ")
  ManualsHelp_L("BASIC). The following is an example:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	HL,FNAME		; Get pointer to file name")
  ManualsHelp_L("	LD	(FNPTR),HL		; Set it to parameter area")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("		.")
  ManualsHelp_L("FNAME:	DB 22H," + Chr(34) + "B:TEST.PIC" + Chr(34) + ",22H,0       ; " + Chr(34) + "TEST.PIC" + Chr(34) + ", end mark")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("When an error occurs, control jumps to the error handler of the BASIC ")
  ManualsHelp_L("interpreter. Set the hook to handle the error in the user program or to call ")
  ManualsHelp_L("this routine from MSX-DOS or a ROM cartridge. This hook is H.ERRO (FFB1H).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTVD (019DH/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	transfers from disk to VRAM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* FNPTR (F562H, 2)	address of the filename")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DUMMY (F564H, 2)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DX (F566H, 2) 	X-coordinate of the destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DY (F568H, 2) 	Y-coordinate of the destination")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NX (F56AH, 2) 	number of dots in the X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("					(not required to be set; this is")
  ManualsHelp_L("					already in the top of data to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("					transferred)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NY (F56CH, 2) 	number of dots in the Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("					(not required to be set; this is")
  ManualsHelp_L("					already in the top of data to be")
  ManualsHelp_L("					transferred)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* CDUMMY (F56EH, 1)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* ARG (F56FH, 1)	selects the direction and expansion")
  ManualsHelp_L("					RAM (same as VDP R#45)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* LOGOP (F570H, 1)	logical operation code (same as the")
  ManualsHelp_L("					logical operation code of VDP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is set when there is an error in the parameter")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTDV (01A1H/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	transfers from VRAM to disk")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SX (F562H, 2) 	X-coordinate of the source")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SY (F564H, 2) 	Y-coordinate of the source")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* FNPTR (F566H, 2)	address of the filename")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* DUMMY (F568H, 2)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NX (F56AH, 2) 	number of dots in the X direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* NY (F56CH, 2) 	number of dots in the Y direction")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* CDUMMY (F56EH, 1)	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTMD (01A5H/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	loads array data from disk")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* FNPTR (F562H, 2)	address of the filename")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SY (F564H, 2) 	dummy (not required to be set)")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SPTR (F566H, 2)	the starting address for loading")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* EPTR (F568H, 2)	the end address for loading")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* BLTDM (01A9H/SUB)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Function:	saves array data to disk")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Input:	HL register <-- F562H")
  ManualsHelp_L("		The following parameters should be set:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* SPTR (F562H, 2)	the starting address for saving")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* EPTR (F564H, 2)	the end address for saving")
  ManualsHelp_L("		* FNPTR (F566H, 2)	address of the filename")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Output:	the CY flag is reset")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  Registers:	all")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("=============================================================================")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Changes from the original in APPENDIX 4:")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- Address of FLAGS variable is corrected from FB1BH to FB1CH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- Address of MCLLEN variable is corrected from FB39H to FB3BH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- Address of H.FIEL hook is corrected from DE2BH to FE2BH.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("APPENDIX 4 - WORK AREA LISTING")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("Figure A.5 shows the map of the MSX2 work area. In this section, the system ")
  ManualsHelp_L("work area and hook from F380H to FFCAH in the figure are described. The ")
  ManualsHelp_L("following notation is used. Length is in bytes.")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("	Label name (address, length)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("		Initial value, contents, purpose")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("   Figure A.5  Work area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFFF	---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("	| slot selection register |")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFFC	|-------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|	  reserved	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFF8	|-------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFF7	|  MAIN-ROM slot address  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|  register reservation   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|      area for new	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFE7	|	VDP (9938)	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|	program for	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("FFCA	|  expansion BIOS calls   |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|	hook area	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("FD9A	|			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|-------------------------|")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	|    system work area	  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("F380	|			  |")
  ManualsHelp_L("	---------------------------")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Subroutines for read/write calls of the inter-slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RDPRIM (F380H, 5)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	read from basic slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("WRPRIM (F385H, 7)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	write to basic slot")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLPRIM (F38CH, 14)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	basic slot call")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Starting address of assembly language program of USR function, text screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("USRTAB (F39AH, 20)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  FCERR")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of assembly language program of USR function")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(0 to 9); the value before defining assembly language program")
  ManualsHelp_L("		points to FCERR (475AH).")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINL40 (F3AEH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  39")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	screen width per line at SCREEN 0 (set by WIDTH statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("		at SCREEN 0)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINL32 (F3AfH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  32")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	screen width per line at SCREEN 1 (set by WIDTH statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("		at SCREEN 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LINLEN (F3B0H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  29")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	current screen width per line")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CRTCNT (F3B1H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  24")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	number of lines of current screen")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLMLST (F3B2H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  14")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	horizontal location in the case that items are divided by")
  ManualsHelp_L("		commas in PRINT statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Work for initialisation")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- SCREEN 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TXTNAM (F3B3H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TXTCOL (F3B5H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	unused")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TXTCGP (F3B7H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TXTATR (F3B9H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	unused")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TXTPAT (F3BBH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	unused")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- SCREEN 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("T32NAM (F3BDH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("T32COL (F3BFH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  2000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("T32CGP (F3C1H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("T32ATR (F3C3H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1B00H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("T32PAT (F3C5H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  3800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- SCREEN 2")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPNAM (F3C7H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPCOL (F3C9H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  2000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	colour table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPCGP (F3CBH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPATR (F3CDH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1B00H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GRPPAT (F3CFH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  3800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- SCREEN 3")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MLTNAM (F3D1H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MLTCOL (F3D3H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	unused")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MLTCGP (F3D5H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0000H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MLTATR (F3D7H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1B00H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	sprite attribute table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MLTPAT (F3D9H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  3800H")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	sprite generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Other screen settings")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CLIKSW (F3DBH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	key click switch (0 = OFF, otherwise = ON), set by")
  ManualsHelp_L("		<key click switch> of SCREEN statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CSRY (F3DCH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	Y-coordinate of cursor")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CSRX (F3DDH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	X-coordinate of cursor")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CNSDFG (F3DEH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	function key display switch (0 = display, otherwise = no")
  ManualsHelp_L("		display), set by KEY ON/OFF statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Area to save VDP registers")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG0SAV (F3DFH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG1SAV (F3E0H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  E0H")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG2SAV (F3E1H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG3SAV (F3E2H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG4SAV (F3E3H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG5SAV (F3E4H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG6SAV (F3E5H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RG7SAV (F3E6H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STATFL (F3E7H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	stores VDP status (contents of status register 0, in MSX2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TRGFLG (F3E8H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  FFH")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	stores trigger button status of joystick")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FORCLR (F3E9H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  15")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	foreground colour; set by colour statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BAKCLR (F3EAH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  4")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	background colour; set by colour statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BDRCLR (F3EBH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  7")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	border colour; set by colour statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAXUPD (F3ECH, 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  JP 0000H (C3H, 00H, 00H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used by CIRCLE statement internally")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MINUPD (F3EFH, 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  JP 0000H (C3H, 00H, 00H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used by CIRCLE statement internally")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ATRBYT (F3F2H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  15")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	colour code in using graphics")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Work area for PLAY statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("QUEUES (F3F3H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  QUETAB (F959H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	points to queue table at the execution of PLAY statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FRCNEW (F3F5H), 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  255")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used by BASIC interpreter internally")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Work area for key input")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SCNCNT (F3F6H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  1")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	interval for the key scan")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("REPCNT (F3F7H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  50")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	delay until the auto-repeat of the key begins")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PUTPNT (F3F8H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  KEYBUF (FBF0H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	points to address to write in the key buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("GETPNT (F3FAH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  KEYBUF (FBF0H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	points to address to read from key buffer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Parameters for Cassette")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CS120 (F3FCH, 5*2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- 1200 baud")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	83 (LOW01) ............ Low width representing bit 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		92 (HIGH01) ........... High width representing bit 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		38 (LOW11) ............ Low width representing bit 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("		45 (HIGH11) ........... High width representing bit 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HEADLEN * 2/256 ....... High bytes (HEDLEN = 2000)")
  ManualsHelp_L("					  of header bits for short")
  ManualsHelp_L("					  header")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("- 2400 baud")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	37 (LOW02) ............ Low width representing bit 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		45 (HIGH02) ........... High width representing bit 0")
  ManualsHelp_L("		14 (LOW12) ............ Low width representing bit 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("		22 (HIGH12) ........... High width representing bit 1")
  ManualsHelp_L("		HEADLEN * 4/256 ....... High bytes (HEDLEN = 2000)")
  ManualsHelp_L("					  of header bits for short")
  ManualsHelp_L("					  header")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LOW (F406H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  LOW01, HIGH01 (by default, 1200 baud)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	width of LOW and HIGH which represents bit 0 of current baud")
  ManualsHelp_L("		rate; set by <cassette baud rate> of SCREEN statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HIGH (F408H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  LOW11, HIGH11 (by default, 1200 baud)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	width of LOW and HIGH which represents bit 1 of current baud")
  ManualsHelp_L("		rate; set by <cassette baud rate> of SCREEN statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HEADER (F40AH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  HEADLEN * 2/256 (by default, 1200 baud)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	header bit for the short header of current baud rate")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(HEADLEN = 2000); set by <cassette baud rate> of SCREEN")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ASPCT1 (F40BH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	256/aspect ratio; set by SCREEN statement to use in CIRCLE")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ASPCT2 (F40DH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	256 * aspect ratio; set by SCREEN statement to use in CIRCLE")
  ManualsHelp_L("		statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENDPRG (F40FH, 5)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  " + Chr(34) + ":" + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	false end of program for RESUME NEXT statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Work used by BASIC internally")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ERRFLG (F414H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to store the error number")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("LPTPOS (F415H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  0")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	printer head location")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRTFLG (F416H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag whether to send to printer")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NTMSXP (F417H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	printer (0 = printer for MSX, otherwise not)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RAWPRT (F418H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	non-zero when printing in raw-mode")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VLZADR (F419H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	address of character to be replaced by VAL function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VLZDAT (F41BH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	character to be replaced with 0 by VAL function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CURLIN (F41CH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	currently executing line number of BASIC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("KBUF (F41FH, 318)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	crunch buffer; translated into intermediate language from")
  ManualsHelp_L("		BUF (F55EH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BUFMIN (F55DH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  " + Chr(34) + "," + Chr(34))
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used in INPUT statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("BUF (F55EH, 258)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	buffer to store characters typed; where direct statements")
  ManualsHelp_L("		are stored in ASCII code")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENDBUF (F660H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	prevents overflow of BUF (F55EH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TTYPOS (F661H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	virtual cursor location internally retained by BASIC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DIMFLG (F662H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used by BASIC internally")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VALTYP (F663H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used to identify the type of variable")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DORES (F664H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	indicates whether stored word can be crunched")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DONUM (F665H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag for crunch")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CONTXT (F666H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	stores text address used by CHRGET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CONSAV (F668H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	stores token of constant after calling CHRGET")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CONTYP (F669H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	type of stored constant")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CONLO (F66AH, 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	value of stored constant")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MEMSIZ (F672H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	highest address of memory used by BASIC")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STKTOP (F674H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	address used as stack by BASIC; depending on CLEAR statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TXTTAB (F676H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of BASIC text area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMPPT (F768H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  TEMPST (F67AH)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of unused area of temporary descriptor")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMPST (F67AH, 3 * NUMTMP)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area for NUMTEMP")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DSCTMP (F698H, 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	string descriptor which is the result of string function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FRETOP (F69BH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of unused area of string area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMP3 (F69DH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used for garbage collection or by USR function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMP8 (F69FH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	for garbage collection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ENDFOR (F6A1H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	stores next address of FOR statement (to begin execution from")
  ManualsHelp_L("		the next of FOR statement at loops)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DATLIN (F6A3H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	line number of DATA statement read by READ statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SUBFLG (F6A5H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag for array for USR function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FLGINP (F6A6H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag used in INPUT or READ")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMP (F6A7H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	location for temporary reservation for statement code; used")
  ManualsHelp_L("		for variable pointer, text address, and others")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PTRFLG (F6A9H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	0 if there is not a line number to be converted,otherwise not")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("AUTFLG (F6AAH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag for AUTO command validity (non-zero = valid, otherwise")
  ManualsHelp_L("		invalid)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("AUTLIN (F6ABH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	last input line number")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("AUTINC (F6ADH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  10")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	increment value of line number of AUTO command")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SAVTXT (F6AFH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to store address of currently executing text; mainly")
  ManualsHelp_L("		used for error recovery by RESUME statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ERRLIN (F6B3H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	line number where an error occurred")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DOT (F6B5H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	last line number which was displayed in screen or entered")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ERRTXT (F6B7H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	text address which caused an error; mainly used for error")
  ManualsHelp_L("		recovery by RESUME statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ONELIN (F6B9H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	text address to which control jumps at error; set by ON")
  ManualsHelp_L("		ERROR GOTO statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ONEFLG (F6BBH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag which indicates error routine execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("		(non-zero = in execution, otherwise not)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMP2 (F6BCH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	for temporary storage")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("OLDLIN (F6BEH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	line number which was terminated by Ctrl+STOP, STOP")
  ManualsHelp_L("		instruction, END instruction, or was executed last")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("OLDTXT (F6C0H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	address to be executed next")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("VARTAB (F6C2H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of simple variable; executing NEW statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("		causes [contents of TXTTAB(F676H) + 2] to be set")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ARYTAB (F6C4H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of array table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("STREND (F6C6H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	last address of memory in use as text area or variable area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DATPTR (F6C8H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	text address of data read by executing READ statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DEFTBL (F6CAH, 26)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to store type of variable for one alphabetical")
  ManualsHelp_L("		character; depends on type declaration such as CLEAR, DEFSTR,")
  ManualsHelp_L("		!, or #")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Work for user function parameter")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMSTK (F6E4H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	previous definition block on stack (for garbage collection)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMLEN (F6E6H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	number of bytes of objective data")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PARM1 (F6E8H, PRMSIZ)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	objective parameter definition table; PRMSIZ is number of")
  ManualsHelp_L("		bytes of definition block, initial value is 100")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMPRV (F74CH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  initial value:  PRMSTK")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	pointer to previous parameter block (for garbage collection)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMLN2 (F74EH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	size of parameter block")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PARM2 (F750H, 100)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	for parameter storage")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PRMFLG (F7B4H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	flag to indicate whether PARM1 was searched")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ARYTA2 (F7B5H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	end point of search")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NOFUNS (F7B7H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	0 if there is not an objective function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TEMP9 (F7B8H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	location of temporary storage for garbage collection")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FUNACT (F7BAH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	number of objective functions")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SWPTMP (F7BCH, 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	location of temporary storage of the value of the first")
  ManualsHelp_L("		variable of SWAP statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("TRCFLG (F7C4H, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	trace flag (non-zero = TRACE ON, 0 = TRACE OFF)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Work for Math-Pack")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FBUFFR (F7C5H, 43)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used internally by Math-Pack")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DECTMP (F7F0H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used to transform decimal integer to floating-point number")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DECTM2 (F7F2H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used at division routine execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DECCNT (F7F4H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used at division routine execution")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("DAC (F7F6H, 16)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to set the value to be calculated")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HOLD8 (F806H, 48)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	register storage area for decimal multiplication")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HOLD2 (F836H, 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used internally by Math-Pack")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("HOLD (F83EH, 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	used internally by Math-Pack")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("ARG (F847H, 16)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to set the value to be calculated with DAC (F7F6H)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RNDX (F857H, 8)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	stores last random number in double precision real number;")
  ManualsHelp_L("		set by RND function")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("* Data area used by BASIC interpreter")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("MAXFIL (F85FH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	maximum file number; set by MAXFILES statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FILTAB (F860H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	starting address of file data area")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NULBUF (F862H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	points to buffer used in SAVE and LOAD by BASIC interpreter")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PTRFIL (F864H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	address of file data of currently accessing file")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("RUNFLG (F866H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	non-zero value if program was loaded and executed; used")
  ManualsHelp_L("		by R option of LOAD statement")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FILNAM (F866H, 11)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to store filename")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FILNM2 (F871H, 11)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to store filename")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NLONLY (F87CH, 1)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	non-zero value if program is being loaded")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("SAVEND (F87DH, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	end address of assembly language program to be saved")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("FNKSTR (F87FH, 160)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	area to store function key string (16 character x 10)")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CGPNT (F91FH, 3)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	address to store character font on ROM")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("NAMBAS (F922H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	base address of current pattern name table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("CGPBAS (F924H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	base address of current pattern generator table")
  ManualsHelp_L("")
  ManualsHelp_L("PATBAS (F926H, 2)")
  ManualsHelp_L("  contents:	base address of current sprite generator table")
